1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=66650706
2 CONT
2 CONT Company B, 14th Virginia Cavalry, McCausland's Brigade, Lomax's Division, Valley District, Dept. of Northern Virginia, C.S.A.
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence Charlotte County VA; a 15 year-old Student.
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlisted on 5/15/1861 at Ashland, VA. for 2 years' service, he was mustered into Captain E.E. Bouldin's Company "Charlotte Cavalry", 14th Virginia Cavalry as a Private. (This company subsequently became Company B, 14th Virginia Ca
2 CONC valry.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wounded in 1861 by bushwhackers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stationed 8/31/1861 Monterey, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wounded 2/18/1862 New Market, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Present, Sept & Oct 1862 Roll.
2 CONT
2 CONT Present, Jan & Feb and March & April Rolls.
2 CONT
2 CONT Present 7/3/1863 Gettysburg, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Absent, on leave 2/29 - 8/31/64, due to death of his father. Since the family property was a large estate, Samuel's initial furlough was extended by his Commanding Officer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Absent, detail for horse on Sept & Oct 1864 Roll.
2 CONT
2 CONT On all rolls through Nov & Dec 1864 final roll.
2 CONT
2 CONT Promoted to 2nd Lieutenant early 1865; commanding company through end of war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surrendered/paroled on 4/9/1865 at Appomattox Court House, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Postwar:
2 CONT
2 CONT Attended University of Virginia 1866-7. Lawyer and Newspaper Editor, Hopkinsville, KY. Treasury Dept., Washington DC 1870-1905.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 14th Cavalry Regiment was organized in September, 1862, with nine companies, some of which had previously served in Jackson's Squadron Virginia Cavalry.
