1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth:  Apr. 25, 1860 Virginia, USA  Death:  Apr. 16, 1942 Virginia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bessie made two startling decisions for a woman of her generation. First, never to marry and second, to further her education. "I'm tired of being just a young lady," she said. After attending Vassar, she went on to M.I.T. to stud
2 CONC y biology, and was probably the first woman to graduate from that still very masculine institution.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1896 Bessie was invited to head the Biology Department at the newly founded Adelphi College; she remained in that position until 1916. In that year her father died and his children were faced with the decision of who would cont
2 CONC inue to keep up the farm at "Do-Well." Clem, married for a second time, had a young family, while Dick had remained a bachelor, but both of whom were established in their chosen careers far from Charlotte County. The same was true
2 CONC  of Bessie, but she gave up her teaching and returned to the homestead, where, with her sister Mattie, they were the last of the descendants to live there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
