2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Venable "Slate Hill," was member of House of Burgesses
2 CONT
2 CONT and VA House of Delegates 1766-1769-1776 and State Senator 1780-1785, Pr. Edw. Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1783 Va tax list, 10 whites, 43 blacks, making Nathaniel the third largest slave owner in Pr. Edw. Co in 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later Nathaniel owned 20-30 thousand acres and 100 slaves
2 CONT
2 CONT Was vestryman of St. Patrick's Parish and organized the first Presbyterian Church in Pr. Edw. Co
2 CONT
2 CONT Was first Episcopalian (which was the state church of Va before Rev.War) and later Presbyterian. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Founder of Hamden-Sidney College.
2 CONT
