1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Agnes Pleasants (Woodson)'''
2 CONT She was a Patriot of the American Revolution for Virginia. DAR Ancestor #: A081658 
2 CONT http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A081658
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Generation No. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.Joseph3 MORTON (John2, John1) was born 27 Dec 1709, and died 28 Jun 1782 in Charlotte
2 CONT Co., VA.
2 CONT He married Agnes WOODSON 1736 in Lunenburg, VA, daughter of Richard WOODSON and Anne SMITH.
2 CONT She was born 27 Feb 1710/11.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph MORTON and Agnes WOODSON are:
2 CONT *        18       i.       Josiah4 MORTON, born 25 Mar 1738 in Louisa Co., VA.
2 CONT *        19       ii.       Judith MORTON, born 27 Dec 1739 in Charlotte Co., VA.
2 CONT *        20       iii.       William T. MORTON, born 27 Nov 1743 in Prince Edward Co., VA.
2 CONT *        21       iv.       Jane MORTON, born 14 Feb 1744/45 in Prince Edward Co., VA.
2 CONT *        22       v.       Agnes MORTON, born 26 Feb 1746/47 in Charlotte Co., VA.
2 CONT *        23       vi.       Joseph Jr. MORTON, born 15 Nov 1749.
2 CONT *        24       vii.       Jacob MORTON, born 29 Jan 1750/51 in Charlotte Co., VA.
2 CONT *        25       viii.       Elizabeth MORTON, born 14 May 1754 in Charlotte Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
