2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT • Captain of Charlotte County cavalry during War of 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT 38. GEORGE HANNAH (son of 19 Ann Cunningham) b. 18 June (prob. 1782)(1780 per cemetery transcription), d. 12 June 1870 (Most of the dates pertaining to the Hannahs were furnished by Dr. J. D. Eggleston, Hampden-Sydney, Va. Other s
2 CONC ubstantial contributors were Mrs. Anne Atkinson Chamberlayne, also of Hampden-Sydney, and Mrs. Emory Shaffer, Bryn Mawr. Pa.) Captain of Charlotte County cavalry during War of 1812; lived at â?Gravel Hillâ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Rootsweb.com cemetery transcription Cub Creek Church Cemetery, Charlotte County, Virginia 39. George Hannah June 18, 1780 June 12, 1870
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Married, first,===
2 CONT 5 November 1805 Martha Brent, daughter of James, son of John Brent, and had: <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===two children===
2 CONT
2 CONT (74) i. Joel Watkins Hannah <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Julia Ann Hannah, married Samuel Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===He married secondly,===
2 CONT either 5 August or 11 December 1816, Lucy Morton (daughter of Colonel William Morton and Susannah Watkins) born 10 July 1798, died 14 October 1872 and had: <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===3 more children===
2 CONT
2 CONT (75) iii. George Cunningham Hannah <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT (76) iv.''' William Morton Hannah''' <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT (77) v. Susan Watkins Hannah <br/>
