1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Abraham Venables II, '''only surviving son''' of Abraham Venables I of New Kent Co., Va., was born on March 22, 1700, O.S. baptized . . . April 27, 1701, in St. Peters Parrish, New Kent Co., Va. 'He lived first on
2 CONC  the Pamunky River in what was then New Kent Co., Va., afterwards King and Queen, which was cut off from New Kent in 1691, and later and at present, King William County, which was cut off from King and Queen County in 1701.  …” 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Office:  Justice of the Peace, Hanover Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Office:  Justice of the Peace and County Lieutenant, Louisa Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Office:  Vestryman, Fredericksville Parish, [Louisa Co.,] VA  
2 CONT
2 CONT Office:  1742-1756, Virginia House of Burgesses 
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical:  friend and associate of Patrick HENRY 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Note
2 CONT
2 CONT FAMILY HISTORY: HISTORICAL GENEALOGY OF THE WOODSONS AND THEIR CONNECTIONS: pg 25: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Venable, who was born March 22, 1700, and was married in 1723 to Martha Davis, daughter of Nathaniel Davis of Hanover county; she was born July, 1703, and died Feb. 13, 1765.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Venable...he died in Louisa county Dec 16, 1768.  
2 CONT
2 CONT His will is dated April 11, 1768, and was probated in Louisa county, Jan. 9, 1669.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Martha Davis, his wife were the parents of ten children to wit:
2 CONT * (1) Abraham Venable born 1725, died 1778; was married in 1751 to Elizabeth Michaux. 
2 CONT * (2) Hugh Lewis Venable, married Mary Martin, daughter of William Martin of Albemarle county.  
2 CONT * (3) Charles Venable, marrie Elizabeth Smith, daughter of Robert Smith of Port Royal.  
2 CONT * (4) Col. Nathaniel Venable, born 1733, died 1804, was married march 29, 1755 to Elizabeth Woodson, 
2 CONT * (5) James Venable born in Hanvover county, died June 1814, married Jdith Moraton, daughter of Joseph Morton and Agnes Woodson.  
2 CONT * (6) William Venable married Ann Clark, daughter of Isaac Clark of Louisa County.
2 CONT * (7) John Venable, married Agnes Moorman, duaghter of Charles Moorman of Lousa County 
2 CONT * (8) Ann Venable, married Philip King of Cumberland.  
2 CONT * (9) Elizabeth Venable, married Josep Morton, son of Joseph Morton and Agnes Woodson.  
2 CONT * (10) Mary Venable, marrie Charles Moorman, son of Charles Moorman of Louis county. VIRGINIA GENEALOGIES: FHL US/CAn 975.5 D2h2, 1973, pg 320: Daniels Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT and Note: Information from Am. Pub.  V  Vol 6.  B 13012  B 45g24 Information from Am. Pub.  V  Vol 6.  B 13012  B 45g24
2 CONT
