1 NOTE {geni:about_me} “ 5. WILLIAM DANIEL, (James'), b. 1710–14 (?); d—; m. 1740 (?), ELIZABETH (WATKINS) WOODSON, widow of Jacob [SIC: Benjamin] Woodson.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her first marriage Mrs. Daniel had Jacob, Joel and Susanna. Mr. D. was "tall, of fair skin, and blue eyes. His sons were all farmers and his daughters m. farmers. His wife was noted for industry and lived to be upwards of 90 ye
2 CONC ars old” (Mrs. Worthy Allen.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Watkins-985
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Watkins was born in 1712 in Henrico, Virginia to parents Thomas Watkins of Swift Creek and Elizabeth Pride. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Daniel in May 1734 in Goochland, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Woodson, William Pride, Judith Daniel, Benjamin, Hezekiah, William, Benjamin, Sarah (Sally), Mary, Elizabeth (Betty), Judith, John, Rhoda, Mary (Polly), Hezekiah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 22 Mar 1802 in Cumberland, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Ambiguity 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel family genealogies call him Jacob Woodson.  Woodson genealogies call him Benjamin Woodson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Woodson Married Elizabeth Watkins, daughter of Thomas Watkins of Swift Creek. Their children were Thomas, Jacob, and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT 'By her 1st m. Mrs. D. had Jacob, Joel and Susanna. Mr. D. was "tall, of fair skin, and blue eyes. His sons were all farmers and his daughters m. farmers. His wife was noted for industry and lived to be upwards of 90 years old" (M
2 CONC rs. Worthy Allen.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL OF ELIZABETH (WOODSON) DANIEL 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Names: Husband - William Daniel not mentioned and deceased. 
2 CONT *Children - William Daniel, W. P. (William Pride) Daniel, Hezekiah Daniel, William Pride Daniel, John Daniel, Judith Daniel, Sarah Daniel, Mary Daniel, Elizabeth Daniel, and Rhold Daniel. 
2 CONT *Benjamin Daniel died unmarried before Hezekiah, and the extate of Hezekiah Daniel was divided into eight parts and distributed to his brother and sisters or of your Blood Pressure. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Watkins of Swift Creek, who left a will dated March 1760, names his daughter as Elizabeth Daniel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Virginia Genealogies: A Genealogy of the Glassell Family of Scotland and ... By Horace Edwin Hayden.  Page 301.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=SJcsAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA301#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://lists.rootsweb.com/hyperkitty/list/hancock@rootsweb.com/thread/26190939/
2 CONT * Historical genealogy of the Woodsons and their connections By H.M. Woodson.  Page 64.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=jigTAwAAQBAJ&lpg=PA64&ots=U0IGisxJW-&dq=jacob%20woodson%20elizabeth%20(watkins)&pg=PA64#v=onepage&q&f=fals
2 CONC e GoogleBooks]
