2 CONT
2 CONT [Note: There is no description of the grave of George W. Summers Sr. and Mrs. Ann Ratcliffe Summers (possibly confused with Ann Lewis Summers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Scipio. His name was Scipio, and he was an African prince. 
2 CONT But there is no name or title on his gravestone in Spring Hill Cemetery. Information is fragmentary about Scipio. But it is known that he came to America as a slave and that Col. George Summers purchased him, probably soon after t
2 CONC he Revolutionary War.  There is no record of the age of Scipio or when he died.  But he was buried near one side of Col. George Summers, and Mrs. Summers was placed on the other side.  
2 CONT "Movers of the cemetery kept the graves in the same positions in the new location. Thus Scipio's place by the side of his master has been retained.  The nameless stone marker, actually a boulder about 9 inches in diameter, can be 
2 CONC identified by its  location and by a pattern of surface cuts and slashes with no known meaning."* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/178887435/george_william-summers Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/proj
2 CONC ects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 27 2026, 4:08:26 UTC''
