1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Nathaniel served as a Captain during the American Revolutionary War for Virginia -  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A075119 DAR Ancestor #: A075119] and [https://sarpatri
2 CONC ots.sar.org/patriot/display/242853 SAR Patriot #: P-242853]
2 CONT MASSEY, NATHANIEL SR
2 CONT Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): CAPTAIN
2 CONT Birth:  8-2-1727    ST PETERS PAR NEW KENT CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Death:  4-6-1802     GOOCHLAND CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Service Source:  MCALLISTER, VA MIL IN THE REV WAR, PP 205, 206
2 CONT Service Description:  1) GOOCHLAND CO MILITIA
2 CONT RESIDENCE 1) County: GOOCHLAND CO - State: VIRGINIA
2 CONT SPOUSE  1) ELIZABETH WATKINS   2) ANN CLARKE VENABLE 
2 CONT —-
2 CONT In early American history, the name Nathaniel Massie (or Massey) refers to two highly documented individuals in the same direct line: Captain Nathaniel Massie Sr. (the father of Elizabeth Mize) and Major General Nathaniel Massie J
2 CONC r. (her brother, the famous founder of Chillicothe, Ohio).
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Nathaniel Massie Sr. (1727–1802) – The Father
2 CONT Nathaniel Massie Sr. was a prominent Virginia colonial landowner, civic leader, and military officer.Biographical Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: August 2, 1727, in St. Peter's Parish, New Kent County, Virginia Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: August 16, 1802 (some records state April 6), in Goochland County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Son of Charles Massie and Ann Macon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages:
2 CONT 1. Elizabeth Watkins (married c. 1755), daughter of Thomas Watkins. She was the mother of Elizabeth Mize and Nathaniel Jr. She passed away prior to 1783.
2 CONT 2. Ann Clark (married August 24, 1776).
2 CONT
2 CONT Factual Documentation & Historical Records
2 CONT Revolutionary War Service: He is a recognized patriot by the Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR #A075119) and the Sons of the American Revolution (SAR #P-242853). He served as a Captain in the Goochland County Militia durin
2 CONC g the American Revolution.Primary Source Evidence: His military rank and assignments are recorded officially in J.T. McAllister’s Virginia Militia in the Revolutionary War (Pages 205, 206).
