2 CONT Indexed Information
2 CONT ----
2 CONT On 21 April 1727, Jacob & John Michaux of St. James Parish, Henrico County, Virginia sold to Daniel Croom, for 100 pounds, a tract on the south side of the James River, which was bequeathed to them by their father, Abraham Michaux
2 CONC , deceased (Goochland, Virginia deed book 1, page 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Named in his father's will:
2 CONT
2 CONT Item, I give unto my son Jacob Michaux two hundred Acres of the tract of land I now live on to be laid off at the upper end thereof to have and to hold to him and his heirs forever. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All the residue of my personall Estate Goods and Chattles whatsoever I do give and bequest to my loving Wife Susanna whom with '''my Son Jacob''' I appoint full and Sole Executors and Executor of this my last will and Testament an
2 CONC d I leave my Executors in full power to sell the abovesaid plantation at Manakin Town and make undoubted rits in fee as witness my hand and seal this 13th day of May 1717. 
2 CONT ----
