2 SURN Venable
2 _MARNM Venable
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Venable Family Cemetery, Jefferson, Jackson County, Georgia, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1781
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1832
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jefferson
3 STAE GA
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He came from Virginia to Jefferson, Jackson Co., GA in 1791, with parents and five brothers Land Lottery of GA 1827: Nathaniel Venable received LL83, Sec.B, Jackson Co. The 1832 Cherokee Land Lottery of Georgia, Sm
2 CONC ith, James F., NY 1838, 235, 231: 166 Nathaniel Venable's ors 245th Jackson page 231, Tenth District Third Section Cherokee. DAR #:67499; 126407; 67498; 95419; 98527 MILITARY: Priv.in Capt. Jos. Whorton's Co. Jan. 5 - March 5, 181
2 CONC 4 Fort Daniel BURIED: prob. in Jackson Co., GA REF: (M.R. 1779 - 1836 p. 54).
2 CONT The headstones over his and his father Capt. John's graves were placed by Mrs. Thomas Eldridge (Leila Venable Mason) from Atlanta, GA in Dec 1931, after years of searching by her mother Mrs. Frank Mason (Elizabeth Venable). The he
2 CONC adstones were made in the family quarries at Lithonia, and read: Nathaniel Venable/ 1781-1832/ son of Captain John Venable/ and Agnes Moorman
2 CONT Darrell L. McGraw traveled to Jefferson to locate the Venable graveyard in Oct 1993. The cemetery  is fenced, and approximately 50 feet by 25 feet, just off a road, about 2 miles south of Jefferson, Jackson Co., GA.  He obtained p
2 CONC ermission from the current owner of the land surrounding the cemetery, Ed Davis, before clearing the cemetery. He placed a sign on the gate marking it as the "Venable Family Cemetery." There is a map in The Venable Letter, Vol II,
2 CONC  Issue 2, Sep/Oct, p.2.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31448981/nathaniel-venable Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 4 2022, 16:34:43 UTC''
