1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born at "Slate Hill", she stood 5'5" with blue eyes, brown hair and a faultless clear complexion. She was educated by governesses and later went to Mr. Reid's boarding school in Lynchburg where she became proficien
2 CONC t in French, music and Latin. She was also proficient on the piano and developed a keen executive presence in the household. At "Longwood" she wed on 7/16/1834 Thomas Frederick Venable of "Haymarket", Prince Edward County, her cou
2 CONC sin. They lived at "Scott-Greene" in Prince Edward County, a plantation that was given to her by her father. Prior to the war between the states, it was reputed to be a beautiful home and estate. At some point her husband moved to
2 CONC  "Kinderton" in Florida where he passed away.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married her cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was proficient in French and Latin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skilled pianist.
