1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the James Thomas Brown 1880 Testament.. – ‘John George Brown and his wife Rebecca Monteith Garden or Brown, payable by the testator as heir and representative of his deceased father under the couple’s antenupt
2 CONC ial marriage contract of 24 July 1843. Substantial legacies go to his sisters Isabella Alston Brown or Venable (of North Carolina) and Elizabeth Morton Brown, and to three nephews — Alexander Garden Brown, John George Garden Brown
2 CONC  and James Robert Brown, sons of John George Brown. The 1879 codicil bequeaths the ancient family sword by Andrew Ferrara, “with which my Ancestor of Auchlochan fought … for the cause of the Scottish Covenanters”, and the old Auch
2 CONC lochan family papers to his nephew Thomas Brown Venable’
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription on her stone:
2 CONT Daughter of Thomas Brown
2 CONT of Auchlachan, Scotland
2 CONT and beloved wife of
2 CONT A.W. Venable.
2 CONT Born Oct 29, 1807
2 CONT died Apr 14, 1876
2 CONT Her children arise up and call her blessed; her husband also.
