2 SURN Hoge
2 _MARNM Hoge
1 NAME Rev. Moses Hoge, 6th President of Hampden-Sydney College
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 FEB 1752
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cedar Grove
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 BURI
2 DATE 1820
2 PLAC Old Pine Street Presbyterian Church Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Philadelphia
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 JUL 1820
2 ADDR
3 CITY Philadelphia
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Clergyman, Sixth President of Hampden–Sydney College
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alongside of the pulpit, a large slab is erected to his memory with this inscription: "Near this monument erected by filial affection, reposes all that was mortal of the Rev. Moses Hoge, D.D., president of Hampden-
2 CONC Sidney College, and professor of Divinity in the Union Theological Seminary of the Synod of Virginia. A man of genius, profound erudition, and ardent piety, he lived, loved, and died lamented, aged sixty-eight. From the general as
2 CONC sembly of the United States of America to the general assembly of the church in Heaven, his translation, afflictive to his friends, but joyous to himself, was accomplished July 5, 1820."
