1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louise Scott Nelson Tucker BIRTH	8 Oct 1851 DEATH	26 Oct 1915 (aged 64) Danville, Danville City, Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Green Hill Cemetery Danville, Danville City, Virginia, USA  PLOT	X,Y - 23,24 MEMORIAL ID	133103
2 CONC 768 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWERS 0 She died at her home, 886 Grove street, at 1 o'clock, after three months of illness, aged 64 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of the late Dr. Robert Carter Nelson, of Chase City, and the family of Thomas Nelson (First) of Yorktown and Yorkshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother was Mary Scott Watkins, of Petersburg. Her grandfather, Samuel Venable Watkins, lived in Petersburg, where she passed her early girlhood.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1873 and resided in Mecklenburg and Brunswick, and then moved with her husband to Danville, in 1892.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving at her death were: Robert H. Tucker, son, assistant professor of econimies, Washington and Lee University. John L. Tucker, son, tabacconist Frank B. McFall, son-in-law, druggist Tucker McFall, only grandson. of Danville 
2 CONC Miss Annie V. Tucker, of Danville
2 CONT
2 CONT Watkins Leigh Nelson, brother, of Albany, Texas (deceased) John C. Nelson, brother, of Norfolk Mrs. Belle Patillo, sister, of Chase City Mrs. J. W. Roberts, sister, of Chase City Mrs. Alice Hardy, sister, of Chase City Mrs. Frank 
2 CONC Roberts, sister, of Chase City
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral at Church of Epiphany and burial in Green Hill Cemetery. (see obituary)
2 CONT
