1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Martha A. Boyd was born on January 17, 1815 in Albemarle County, Virginia. She was born as the eldest child of James and Jane Boyd. Martha remained in the household of her parents until she married Samuel Austin Le
2 CONC ake.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1820, Martha was marked down as a female, up to age 10 on the census. She was still living with her parents at the age of 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830, Martha was marked down as a female, ages 15 to 20 on the census. She was still living with her parents at the age of 15.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married Samuel “Sam” Austin Leake on October 10, 1836 in Virginia for 150 dollars total. She remained with her husband all the way to his death. Sam died of bronchitis on February 1, 1877 in Hillsboro, Albemarle County, Vir
2 CONC ginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together, Martha and Sam had eleven known children:
2 CONT Adelia Frances Leake (1838-1838)
2 CONT Samuel James Leake (1839-1878)
2 CONT Sophia Shelton Leake (1841-1909)
2 CONT Emma Jane Leake (1842-1887)
2 CONT William Pinkerton Leake (1843-1923)
2 CONT Frances Leake (1844-1845)
2 CONT Sarah A. Leake (1847-1928)
2 CONT Lucy Austin Leake (1849-1886)
2 CONT Shelton Mask Leake (1851-1902)
2 CONT Frank Leake (C. 1855-1878)
2 CONT Mary Ida Leake (1857-1938)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1850, she and Samuel A. Leake lived in District 7 of Fayette County, Tennessee. Their real estate was valued at 500 and Sam worked as a teacher. The members of the household went as follows: Saml A. Leake (age 40), Martha A Lea
2 CONC ke (age 36), Saml J Leake (age 11), Sophie A Leake (age 9), Wm P Leake (age 7), Emma J Leake (age 5), Sally A Leake (age 3), and Lucy A Leake (age 1). A boarder, Sarah Ann Lovell (age 18) was also living there.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, she and Samuel A. Leake lived in the Samuel Miller district of Albemarle County, Virginia. Their real estate was valued at 400 and Sam continued to work as a school teacher. The members of the household went as follows: S
2 CONC aml A. Leak (age 60), Martha A Leak (age 54), Wm P Leak (age 24), Emma J Leak (age 22), Shelton M Leake (age 17), Frank Leak (age 13), and M J Leak (age 11).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1880, she lived as a widow on Lowes Street in Staunton, Virginia. Martha (listed mistakenly as “Martin”) worked as a housekeeper, as she had done prior. The members of the household went as follows, children: Martin A Leake (ag
2 CONC e 60), Emma Leake (age 26), S M Leake (age 25), and Ida Leake (age 23), grandchildren: May Leake (age 11), Lulu Leake (age 9), and Percy Leake (age 4), and nephew: Jas B. Heck (age 28).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1889, Martha was now living in Berkeley, Virginia (presumably with her daughter Mary “Ida”, and son-in-law, Charles E. Moose).
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha’s passing unfortunately occurred on November 14, 1890 at approximately 8 PM. The death occurred at the residence of her daughter, Mary Ida (Leake) Moose and Charles E. Moose’s house in Berkeley (very close to Charlottesvill
2 CONC e). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha had many children with Sam (Martha never remarried). In the will for Jane (her mother), it is stated that Martha (for her kindness) was given a total of 10 dollars. Martha and Samuel are both buried in Lebanon Cemetery in G
2 CONC reenwood, Albemarle County, Virginia.
