2 CONT Robert Woodson b. 1634 m. Elizabeth Ferris, d. ca. 1707. Last known to be living in 1707, Henrico County, VA. when he made a deed to his grandson, William and Joseph Lewis. He married Elizabeth Ferris, daughter of Richard Ferris, 
2 CONC of Henrico, with whom, among others, received a patent, 21, October 1687, for 1785 acres at White Oak Swamp in Varina Parish, in that county. This man was the direct ancestor of Jesse Woodson James, and his brother, Alexander Fran
2 CONC klin "Frank" James, the famous James Boys. Robert Woodson married Elizabeth Ferris: son Benjamin Woodson, married Sarah Porter; their son Robert Woodson (d. 1748/50) married Rebecca Pryor. Their daughter Elizabeth married Shadrach
2 CONC  Mims (1734-1777) and became the mother of Elizabeth Mims (b. 1769) who married Robert Poor (1763-1801), a cornet in the American Revolutionary War. Their daughter in turn, Mary Poor, (died 1825) married John James (1775-1827), so
2 CONC n of William and Mary (Hinds) James of Goochland County, Virginia. Their son Robert Sallee James, who died in the Gold Rush area of California, married Zerelda Cole and they had sons Frank James and Jesse James. (See: Background o
2 CONC f a Bandit, by Joan M. Beamis and William E. Pullen (1971). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jesse Woodson James, the bandit, married his cousin Zerelda "Zee" Amanda Mims.  She was also a descendant of Elizabeth Woodson Mims, who married Robert Poor.
2 CONT ----
