1 NOTE  On 21 Oct 1687, Robert Woodson, Richard Ferris and three other
2 CONT planters patented 1780 acres on White Oak Swamp in Varina Parish.  On
2 CONT the same day, he, his brother, John Woodson Sr, and two others
2 CONT patented 470 acres, also in Henrico Co, VA.  Robert Woodson held 1157
2 CONT acres in Henrico County in 1704 and died after 1 Oct 1707.
1 NOTE DATE 11 DEC 2001
1 NOTE Robert Woodson was known as Colonel Woodson. In "The Woodsons and Their Connections it is stated that if Robert Woodson was known as Colonel it was because he was given the title by the authority of the British Government. ]
2 CONT
