2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/G5CX-P1P
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/photo/jpg/Woodson-23
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Woodson was the daughter of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris. She was born about 1657 in Henrico County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married Wiliam Lewis, son of John Lewis and Sarah, about 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was from Goochland, Virginia, they made their home there and had 3 sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT William died 25 December 1706. Their third child, John, was born about 1706, so Elizabeth was left with three small children to care for.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the oral will of William Lewis 24 Dec 1706 (see document, attached):
2 CONT
2 CONT >Rest of the estate to wife, adding that the children being hers as well as his, he knew she would do as well for them as he would.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * http://genforum.genealogy.com/woodson/messages/1593.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT WM. ROBARDS, Sr., m. second wife, ELIZABETH LEWIS, on January 5, 1758; she was daughter of Joseph Lewis, Sr., testator, granddaughter of William Lewis, Sr., testator, 1708 (son of John Lewis, colonist from Wales, testator, 1687, o
2 CONC f Henrico county, Va.), who m. Elizabeth Woodson, daughter of Robert Woodson (son of Dr. John Woodson) and his wife Elizabeth, daughter of Richard Ferris, of "Curles," in Henrico County.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://dgmweb.net/Resources/GenLin/Robards-JohnLewisRobards1903.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Colonel Robert & Elizabeth (Ferris) Woodson of Henrico Co Virginia.
2 CONT Elizabeth Ferris Woodson was born Curles Plantation, Henrico County, Virginia Colony. Elizabeth married Major William Lewis.
2 CONT "Virginia - Book - Woodson Descendant"
