2 TITL LDS Church Index
1 NOTE John Woodson (son of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris) was the cousin or nephew that was named in the will of John Woodson. He was a merchant and married Judith, daughter of Stephen Tarleton of New Kent County (VA) per Genealog
2 CONC ies of Virginia Families 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Woodsons of western Pennsylvania are supposed to descendants of this John Woodson 
2 CONT From pamphlet "Descendants of John Woodson of Dorsetshire, England, who settled in Virginia in 1624 
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogies of Virginia Families from the William and Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine, Volume V, Thompson - Yates (and Appendix) Indexed by Robert and Catherine Barnes, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc. Baltimore, 1982:
2 CONC  also has John Woodson, Jr. and son of John Woodson, the patriarch of this family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's brother John Woodson names in his will of 1684, the four youngest sons of his brother Robert, viz., Robert, Richard, Joseph and Benjamin and also cousin John Woodson (Cousin meant "nephew" in the seventeenth century) per 
2 CONC Genealogies of Virginia Families. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Woodson (son of John Woodson and Judith Tarleton) (approved in Goochland 21 May 1754) mentions the land his father, John Woodson gave to his children, John, Robert, Josiah, Stephen, Judith and Elizabeth Woodson per Ge
2 CONC nealogies of Virginia Families 
2 CONT
2 CONT HENRICO CO., VA. LAND DEEDS FILM #1697555 ITEM #9 
2 CONT On File with the Family History Library, 85 West South Temple St., Salt Lake City, Utah 84105 
2 CONT Deed #31 pg. 51: 
2 CONT John WOODSON of Henrico Co., Merchant, for 2 dollars to Thomas TAPLIN , Of same, planter, 100 acres on south side of Chickhomlay Swamp, bounded by mouth of Stoney Run and said WOODSON, being part of a patent taken up by Henry TURN
2 CONC ER of New Kent County, and 
2 CONT purchased by Sith RENCH, and from him by said WOODSON, with houses, etc. 
2 CONT Dated 1 August 1707 
2 CONT Witnesses: Littlebury EPES, Joseph PLEASANTS, Thomas WATKINS 
2 CONT Signed: John WOODSON 
2 CONT Recorded 1 Aug 1707 
2 CONT Judith, wife of WOODSON, relinquishes her dower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Cotter   cotterkaren@yahoo.com   2002-04-22 12:16:05
1 NOTE  John Woodson, fourth with this name, married Judith Tarleton.
