1 NAME Robert /Woodson/ Jr.
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Woodson
2 NSFX Jr.
2 _MARNM Woodson
2 NICK Robert Ferris Woodson
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1662
2 ADDR
3 CITY Curles
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE FEB 1729
2 ADDR
3 CITY Curles
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE JUL 1729
2 PLAC Henrico, Virginia, British Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT Updated 28 January 2026
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Woodson, Jr. '''c.1662 Curles, Henrico, Virginia- February, 1729 Curles, Henrico, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents: '''Robert Woodson c.1634- October 1, 1707 and Elizabeth Sarah Ferris c. May 8, 1634-1689
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wives: '''
2 CONT # Elizabeth (disputed existence) 
2 CONT # Sarah Lewis
2 CONT # Rachel Watkins
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children with 1st / 2nd wife   (dates uncertain) 
2 CONT # Stephen c.1682- m. Mary Woodson, daughter of Joseph Richard and Mary Jane Woodson
2 CONT # Joseph c.1685- m. Elizabeth Mattox
2 CONT # Robert c.1687-
2 CONT #  Elizabeth c.1689- m. John Povall
2 CONT # Sarah c.1692-  m. Joseph Parsons
2 CONT # Mary c.1695- died unmarried 
2 CONT # Agnes c.1697- m. Richard Williamson
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children with Rachel:
2 CONT # Jonathan b. 1711
2 CONT # Elizabeth 1713-c.1734 m. John Knight
2 CONT # Judith b. 1715 m. John Cooke
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1662, Robert Woodson Jr. (1660-1729) was in Curles, Henrico County, Virginia, where he died in February 1729.  Robert signed a will on 7/6/1729 in Henrico Co., Virginia, and the will was probated in February of the same year in
2 CONC  Henrico Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, Sarah to Joseph Parsons, Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson. <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >By Rachael Watkins, his second wife, Jonathan, and daughters, Elizabeth and Judith. Elizabeth married John Knight, and Judith married John Cook, and she was mother to all the money-making Cooks.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will & Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Robert Woodson Senior[5]
2 CONT Henrico County, Virginia.
2 CONT 6 July 1729.
2 CONT February 1729/30 (proved).
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed: Robert Woodson.
2 CONT Witnesses: William Porter Jr., Jacob Bosby, Theodrick Carter, Giles Davis (his mark), Tarlton Woodson (his mark).
2 CONT Executors: my loving son Stephen Woodson.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his Will, Robert makes bequests as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT * son Stephen (land that came to my possession by marriage with his mother; 50 acres of land which did once belong to John Lewis)
2 CONT * son Joseph (parcel of land in Goochland County on beginning on the west side Jennytoe Creek at a corner poplar, up the Creek to Rorksy branch, up Rorksy branch to Joseph Parson’s line to the fork, up the main branch to a corner 
2 CONC double poplar, and so bounded by the westward lines of the patent; one negro man named Jack, one feather bed with bedstand, all furniture thereunto belonging, my own gun)
2 CONT * son Robert (residue of land in Goochland on Jennytoe Creek; one negro man named York, all my tradesman tools, one new feather bed and colster rugg, a pair of blankets)
2 CONT * son Jonathan (parcel of land near White Oak Swamp lying between the land of Richard Cocke, Edward Mosby & Harryson; one negro man named Pompey; both him and his estate to be under the guardianship of my son Stephen until he is 1
2 CONC 8)
2 CONT * daughter Elizabeth (one negro girl named Aggy, one feather bed with Virginia Tirk bedstead, furniture)
2 CONT * son Jonathan (one feather bed and furniture being a new bed)
2 CONT * daughter Judith (one negro girl named Nanney, one feather bed, spotted silk rug, and all thereunto belonging to her, one seal skin trunk)
2 CONT * daughter Agnes (one negro child named Sue)
2 CONT * daughter Sarah (one cow and calf)
2 CONT * son Stephen (one negro woman named Jeney in consideration of his care of my children that are in their minoraty and their estates, and also in consideration of the faithful performance of which he shall execute as my Executor bo
2 CONC th in the Learning good Councill and care of them and their estates and his trouble about exedcuting my will to him and his heirs forever).
2 CONT * the residue of my estate to be equally divided among my four children Joseph, Robert, Jonathan, and Judith, to be divided by son Stephen and Thomas Watkins
2 CONT * 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/knight/167/
2 CONT
2 CONT I also have another copy of a periodical entitled "Historical Genealogy of the Woodsons and Their Connections".
2 CONT
2 CONT >In this periodical there is an entry which reads:37 Elizabeth, 4 was  undoubtedly born in Henrico, as her father lived and died in that county.It appears that her father had two daughters named Elizabeth--one by each wife--the el
2 CONC der sister married John Povall and athis one married John Knight and settled in Lunenburg county he died and his will was proved March 12, 1772, and names wife Elizabeth and ten children.The will was witnessed by Miller Woodson an
2 CONC d Thomas Jeffres. (See Wm. and Mary Qtly., Volume X, p.46.). [not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Lewis-of-Henrico-County/6000000084058525845]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From: Patricia Smith (on web)
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was married three times. 1. Elizabeth Lewis 2. Sarah Lewis 3. Rachel Watkins. I can name 7 of his 10 children: 1. Stephen 2. Joseph 3. Robert 4. Jonathan 5. Elizabeth 6. Judith 7. Agnes. Stephan m/ his first cousin, Mary Woods
2 CONC on. Joseph m/ Elizabeth Mattox. Robert died without issue. Elizabeth m/ John Povall. Sarah m/ Joseph Parson. Mary died a maid. Agnes m/ Richard Williamson. Jonathan. no news. Elizabeth II m/ John Knight and Judith m/ John Cooke. R
2 CONC achel Watkins, believe to have been daughter of Henry Watkins of Malvern Hill. Her mother later married Robert's brother-in-law, Edward Mosby. Robert and Rachel proposed their intention of marriage before the Henrico Monthly Meeti
2 CONC ng on 12th day 10th month 1710. When Robert died, his son Stephan, the executor of his estate, placed his younger children under his care. His wife, Rachel, must have died earlier as he did not mention her in his will."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Woodson Jr., was first married to Sarah Lewis, who was [NOT] the daughter of John Lewis and his wife, Isobel Warner Sarah's paternal grandfather was Robert Lewis, an immigrant from Wales. Her maternal grandfather was August
2 CONC ine Warner, an immigrant from Norwich, England. Sarah died before 1710.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Lewis was probably [NOT] a sister of John Lewis of Warner Hall. John Lewis and Lydia, his wife, first settled on Poropotank Creek in 1653. To them were born, probably a number of children; one of whom was Major John Lewis, w
2 CONC ho married Isabella. To these last was born, November 30, 1669, John Lewis who married Elizabeth Warner, daughter of Col. Augustine Warner and wife, Mildred Read. It is probable that Sarah Lewis, wife of Robert Woodson, was a daug
2 CONC hter of Major John Lewis and Isabella. This family became very prominent in colonial affairs in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In that year Robert Woodson (Jr.) requested to be “liberated” from his Henrico County Quaker community in order to marry Rachel Watkins, who was not of that Quaker community. In 1723, perhaps after Rachel's death, he requested to 
2 CONC be received back into his earlier community of Friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's 1729 will named only eight of his ten children, so two may have died before him.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriages of three of his children are of special interest:
2 CONT
2 CONT *       His son Joseph Woodson married Elizabeth Mattox, the daughter of Quaker immigrant, John Mattox, and his wife Margaret Kent.
2 CONT *       His daughter Sarah Woodson married Joseph Parsons.
2 CONT *       Elizabeth Woodson married John Knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In the next generation, Joseph Woodson (son of Joseph Woodson and Elizabeth Mattox) married his cousin, Elizabeth Parsons (daughter of Sarah Woodson and Joseph Parsons): his aunt becoming his mother-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The daughter of this marriage, Judith Woodson, married Jonathan Knight, the grandson of Robert Woodson Jr.'s second marriage: Judith was his great-granddaughter, whereas her husband was his grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Their daughter was Judith Woodson Knight who married William Amis.
