1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Joseph Woodson''' was born circa 1664 in Curles, Henrico , Virginia, Colonial America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-49375970 Col. Robert Woodson] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-104385439 Sarah Elizabeth Woodson]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married [https://www.geni.com/profile-39068740 Jane Woodson] on January 27, 1701 in Henrico, Virginia, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on October 15, 1735 in Goochland , Virginia, Colonial America and was buried on October 27, 1735. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Joseph Woodson, of Henrico and Goochland Counties ; died 1735 . He married his cousin Jane Woodson (daughter of John Woodson, Junior , son of John Woodson, Senior ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT IV * 9 Joseph,3 born about 1664, at Curles in Henrico county, and died October, 1735. He married his second cousin 18 Mary Jane Woodson,4 daughter of 4 John Woodson,' and Mary Tucker, who was the orphan of Samuel Tucker, Captain o
2 CONC f the Ship Vine Tree. Samuel Tucker's widow Jane, was married before 1680 to John Pleasants1 of Curles, and died in 1709. Her will was proved in Henrico county in 1709, and names her grand daughter 18 Jane Woodson,4 and grandsons,
2 CONC  15 Joseph Woodson,4 17 Benjamin Woodson4 and 16 Samuel Tucker Woodson.4 Mary Tucker Woodson, mother of 18 Mary Jane Woodson, died in 1710. In her will, proved in Henrico, August 1, 1710, she names a daughter, Jane, and grandson, 
2 CONC 46 John Woodson,4 son of daughter Jane, granddaughter 47 Mary,4 daughter of daughter Jane, and grandson 48 Joseph,4 son of daughter Jane. This seems to establish the fact that the wife of 9 Joseph Woodson' was 18 Jane Woodson;4 th
2 CONC ough her full name may have been, and doubtless was, Mary Jane Woodson. Mary Tucker Woodson also mentions in her will, grandson, "Sanburne Woodson, child of my daughter Mary, wife of my son Joseph." These last names, no doubt, mea
2 CONC n Mary Sanburne, wife of 15 Joseph Woodson.4 And the child Sanburne was 66 Sanburne Woodson6 who married Elizabeth Hughes.' 9 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Woodson' died in Goochland county and his will was proved October 15, 1735. In it he names children; 47 Mary Woodson,4 who married 29 Stephen Woodson;4 49 Judith Woodson,4 who married Charles Christian; 50 Martha Woodson,4 
2 CONC who married 61 John Cannon;4 and 51 Tucker Woodson.4 (See Wm. and Mary Qtly.) It appears that the last three children were born in Goochland; so 9 Joseph Woodson' must have moved to that county shortly after the death of his mothe
2 CONC r-in-law, Mary (Tucker) Woodson who died in Henrico in 1710.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT IV * 9 Joseph,3 born about 1664, at Curles in Henrico county, and died October, 1735. He married his second cousin 18 Mary Jane Woodson,4 daughter of 4 John Woodson,' and Mary Tucker, who was the orphan of Samuel Tucker, Captain o
2 CONC f the Ship Vine Tree. Samuel Tucker's widow Jane, was married before 1680 to John Pleasants1 of Curles, and died in 1709. Her will was proved in Henrico county in 1709, and names her grand daughter 18 Jane Woodson,4 and grandsons,
2 CONC  15 Joseph Woodson,4 17 Benjamin Woodson4 and 16 Samuel Tucker Woodson.4 Mary Tucker Woodson, mother of 18 Mary Jane Woodson, died in 1710. In her will, proved in Henrico, August 1, 1710, she names a daughter, Jane, and grandson, 
2 CONC 46 John Woodson,4 son of daughter Jane, granddaughter 47 Mary,4 daughter of daughter Jane, and grandson 48 Joseph,4 son of daughter Jane. This seems to establish the fact that the wife of 9 Joseph Woodson' was 18 Jane Woodson;4 th
2 CONC ough her full name may have been, and doubtless was, Mary Jane Woodson. Mary Tucker Woodson also mentions in her will, grandson, "Sanburne Woodson, child of my daughter Mary, wife of my son Joseph." These last names, no doubt, mea
2 CONC n Mary Sanburne, wife of 15 Joseph Woodson.4 And the child Sanburne was 66 Sanburne Woodson6 who married Elizabeth Hughes.' 9 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Woodson' died in Goochland county and his will was proved October 15, 1735. In it he names children; 47 Mary Woodson,4 who married 29 Stephen Woodson;4 49 Judith Woodson,4 who married Charles Christian; 50 Martha Woodson,4 
2 CONC who married 61 John Cannon;4 and 51 Tucker Woodson.4 (See Wm. and Mary Qtly.) It appears that the last three children were born in Goochland; so 9 Joseph Woodson' must have moved to that county shortly after the death of his mothe
2 CONC r-in-law, Mary (Tucker) Woodson who died in Henrico in 1710.
