1 NAME Sarah /Woodson/
2 GIVN Sarah
2 SURN Woodson
2 _MARNM Mosby
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JUN 1665
2 PLAC Curles Plantation
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 AUG 1716
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * circa 1665 at Tuckahoe Creek, Henrico County, Virginia
2 CONT * 1665 at Curles Neck Plantation, Varina District, Henrico County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1694 at Henrico?, Henrico County, Virginia
2 CONT * August 12, 1716 at Henrico?, Henrico County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. SARAH3 WOODSON (ROBERT2, JOHN1) was born 1665. She married EDWARD MOSBY 1689 in Henrico County, VA. He was born Abt. 1655.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for SARAH WOODSON: Sarah Woodson, daughter of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris, married Edward Mosby, of Henrico Co. (See Mosby family, ante page 2275.) in Descendants of John Woodson pamphlet which shows: " VI. Sarah, ma
2 CONC rried Edward Mosby"
2 CONT
2 CONT Early entry in Genealogies of Virginia Families from William & Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine - Woodson Family shows Sarah Woodson married Edward Mosely but at the end of the same publication in Woodson Pedigree it sho
2 CONC ws:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah3 Woodson (Robert2, John1) was born 1665 in Curles, Henrico County, VA, and died 12 August 1716 in Henrico County, VA. She married Edward Mosby 1689, son of Richard Mosby and Judith Parsens. He was born 1660 in Henrico County
2 CONC , VA, and died 03 May 1742 in Henrico County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 1. Descendants of John Woodson of Dorsetshire, England, who settled in Virginia in 1624, copied from the Standard, published in Richmond, VA, 1888 2, Genealogies of Virginia Families from the William and Mary College Quar
2 CONC terly Historical Magazine, Volume V, Thompson - Yates (and Appendix) Indexed by Robert and Catherine Barnes, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc. Baltimore, 1982)
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Woodson, Sr. , of Henrico Co. , deed of gift to his daughter Sarah wife of Edward Moseby , of same place. 100 acres of land on S. side of White Oak Swamp , formerly purchased of Robert Clark & now in possession of sd. Edwar
2 CONC d Moseby , & adj. lands of Thos. East, Sr. & part of that Pattent: Unto the sd. Sarah Mosby during her life-time & to John Mosby son of Edward Mosby & Sarah his wife & ye heirs of his body if it please God he lives to attain the a
2 CONC ge of 21 yrs. but if not then to the next surviving heir of sd. Sarah Mosby : Moreover it shall be lawful for sd. John Mosby when he has attained the age of 21 yrs. to clear, build & seat upon any part of the sd. 100 acres of land
2 CONC , not molesting nor troubleing the sd. Sarah , his mother, during her lifetime. June 1, 1689 . Recd. June 1, 1689 . Ibid. p. 66.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Woodson, Sr. , in consideracon of 20 days Carpenter's work secured to be paid, conveys to Edwd. Moseby , 50 acres of land adj. on the West side of 100 acres given by deed bearing date wth these present unto Sarah , wife of 
2 CONC ye sd. Edward Moseby : June 1, 1689 . Recd. June 1, 1689 . Ibid. p. 67.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for EDWARD MOSBY: Edward Mosby is shown to be the spouse of Sarah Woodson, daughter of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris, in two Woodson publications, though in some places he is shown as Edward Moseley:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Robert WOODSON, Sr., brother to the Sarah Woodson shown to be married to Edward Mosby, mentions in his will an Edward Mosby as a neighbor to his land near White Oak Swamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Son Stephen, the land that came in my possession by marriage with his mother, also 50 acres that belonged to John Lewis. To son Joseph, a parcel in Goochland County on West side of Jennytoe Creek, up Rockey branch and next to J
2 CONC oseph PARSONS' line, also a negro and items. To son Robert, the residue of land in Goochland on Jennytoe Creek.. To Son Jonathan, land near White Oak Swamp, between Richard Cocke, EDWARD MOSBY, and Harrison, and his estate to be u
2 CONC nder the guardianship of my son Stephen until he is 18. To daughter Elizabeth, a negro and items. To daughter Judith; a negro and items. To daughter Agnes, a negro. The rest devided between children Joseph, Robert, Jonathan, and J
2 CONC udith; to be divided by son Stephen and Thomas Watkins...Son Stephen to be executor......Dated 6. Jul 1729. Witnesses: William Porter, Jr., Theodorick Carter, Giles Davis, Tarlton Woodson......Recorded Feb. 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of SARAH WOODSON and EDWARD MOSBY are: 2.       i.       ROBE RT4 MOSBY, b. 1685, Henrico County, Virginia. 3.       ii.        JOHN MOSBY, b. Henrico County, Virginia. 4.       iii.        BENJAMIN MOSBY, b. 1690; d. 177
2 CONC 4.
2 CONT        iv.       AGNE S MOSBY, b. 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for AGNES MOSBY: Agnes Mosby is shown to be the daughter of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        v.        JACOB MOSBY, b. Abt. 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JACOB MOSBY: Jacob Mosby is shown to be a son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        vi.        HEZEKIAH MOSBY, b. 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for HEZEKIAH MOSBY: Hezekiah Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        vii.        JOSEPH MOSBY, b. 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOSEPH MOSBY: Joseph Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        viii.        RICHARD MOSBY, b. 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for RICHARD MOSBY: Richard Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Descendants of Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. SARAH3 WOODSON (ROBERT2, JOHN1) was born 1665. She married EDWARD MOSBY 1689 in Henrico County, VA. He was born Abt. 1655.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for SARAH WOODSON: Sarah Woodson, daughter of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris, married Edward Mosby, of Henrico Co. (See Mosby family, ante page 2275.) in Descendants of John Woodson pamphlet which shows: " VI. Sarah, ma
2 CONC rried Edward Mosby"
2 CONT
2 CONT Early entry in Genealogies of Virginia Families from William & Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine - Woodson Family shows Sarah Woodson married Edward Mosely but at the end of the same publication in Woodson Pedigree it sho
2 CONC ws:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah3 Woodson (Robert2, John1) was born 1665 in Curles, Henrico County, VA, and died 12 August 1716 in Henrico County, VA. She married Edward Mosby 1689, son of Richard Mosby and Judith Parsens. He was born 1660 in Henrico County
2 CONC , VA, and died 03 May 1742 in Henrico County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 1. Descendants of John Woodson of Dorsetshire, England, who settled in Virginia in 1624, copied from the Standard, published in Richmond, VA, 1888 2, Genealogies of Virginia Families from the William and Mary College Quar
2 CONC terly Historical Magazine, Volume V, Thompson - Yates (and Appendix) Indexed by Robert and Catherine Barnes, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc. Baltimore, 1982)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for EDWARD MOSBY: Edward Mosby is shown to be the spouse of Sarah Woodson, daughter of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris, in two Woodson publications, though in some places he is shown as Edward Moseley:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Robert WOODSON, Sr., brother to the Sarah Woodson shown to be married to Edward Mosby, mentions in his will an Edward Mosby as a neighbor to his land near White Oak Swamp.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Son Stephen, the land that came in my possession by marriage with his mother, also 50 acres that belonged to John Lewis. To son Joseph, a parcel in Goochland County on West side of Jennytoe Creek, up Rockey branch and next to J
2 CONC oseph PARSONS' line, also a negro and items. To son Robert, the residue of land in Goochland on Jennytoe Creek.. To Son Jonathan, land near White Oak Swamp, between Richard Cocke, EDWARD MOSBY, and Harrison, and his estate to be u
2 CONC nder the guardianship of my son Stephen until he is 18. To daughter Elizabeth, a negro and items. To daughter Judith; a negro and items. To daughter Agnes, a negro. The rest devided between children Joseph, Robert, Jonathan, and J
2 CONC udith; to be divided by son Stephen and Thomas Watkins...Son Stephen to be executor......Dated 6. Jul 1729. Witnesses: William Porter, Jr., Theodorick Carter, Giles Davis, Tarlton Woodson......Recorded Feb. 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of SARAH WOODSON and EDWARD MOSBY are: 2.       i.       ROBE RT4 MOSBY, b. 1685, Henrico County, Virginia. 3.       ii.        JOHN MOSBY, b. Henrico County, Virginia. 4.       iii.        BENJAMIN MOSBY, b. 1690; d. 177
2 CONC 4.
2 CONT        iv.       AGNE S MOSBY, b. 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for AGNES MOSBY: Agnes Mosby is shown to be the daughter of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        v.        JACOB MOSBY, b. Abt. 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JACOB MOSBY: Jacob Mosby is shown to be a son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        vi.        HEZEKIAH MOSBY, b. 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for HEZEKIAH MOSBY: Hezekiah Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        vii.        JOSEPH MOSBY, b. 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOSEPH MOSBY: Joseph Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT        viii.        RICHARD MOSBY, b. 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for RICHARD MOSBY: Richard Mosby is shown to be the son of Edward Mosby and Sarah Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Edward Mosby on 6-1-1688 in Curles, Henryco County, Virginia, USA, the son of Richard James Mosby & Judith Parsons.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT VI 11 Sarah,3 born about 1668 at Curles in Henrico county, was married about 1688 or '89 to Edward Moseley. As stated in William and Mary Quarterly, her father, 3 Robert Woodson2 of Henrico, made a deed in 1689 to "daughter Sarah,
2 CONC  wife of Edward Moseley." This may have been a bridal present. The descendants of this couple have not been traced.
