2 CONT === !1666 BIRTH: IGI-VA:  Benjamin Woodson s ===
2 CONT !1666 BIRTH: IGI-VA:  Benjamin Woodson son of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris was b. 1666 at Curles Plantation, Henrico Co., VA. !HISTORICAL GENEALOGY OF THE WOODSONS AND THEIR CONNECTIONS, By Henry Morton Woodson, 1915, HHBL 
2 CONC CS 43.G46x  G #743.  pg 23: QUAKER RECORDS: VA: pg 218: 1700, 5, 25. Benjamin, son of Robert, Henrico co,; married at Frs MH Henrico co., Sarah Porter, dau. of William, Jr. Henrico Co. QUAKER RECORDS: VA: ADVENTURERS OF PURSE AND 
2 CONC PERSON, VIRGINIA 1607-1624/5, 1987: BYU F225.A7: pg 708-716: 3. ROBERT (2) WOODSON (John-1) deposed, June 1680, that he was "46 years of age or thereabouts," and, 1 June 1696, the he was aged about 61.  He married Elizabeth Ferris
2 CONC , daughter of Richard Ferris.  On 21 Oct 1687 Robert (2) Woodson, Richard Ferris and three others patented 1780 acres on White Oak Swamp in Varina Parish and the same day he, John Woodson, Sr. and two others patented 470 acres, al
2 CONC so in Henrico county.  
2 CONT He held 1157 acres in Henrico County, 1704, and died after 1 Oct 1707. 
2 CONT ISSUE: 
2 CONT 7. JOHN (3), 
2 CONT 8. SARAH (3); 
2 CONT 9. ELIZABETH (3); 
2 CONT 10. JUDITH (3); 
2 CONT 11. MARY (3); 
2 CONT 12. ROBERT (3); 
2 CONT 13. RICHARD (3); 
2 CONT 14. JOSEPH (3); 
2 CONT 15. BENJAMIN (3). pg 7
2 CONT 16: 15. BENJAMIN (3) WOODSON (Robert-2, John-1) married 12 July 1700, Sarah Porter, daughter of William Porter, Jr.  He lived at curles, Henrico county, and left will, now lost, 19 Nov 1722-Aug 1723.... COLONIAL GRANVILLE COUNTY A
2 CONC ND ITS PEOPLE, By Worth S. Ray, pg 246: (2) John Daniel, of Accomac and Northampton County, VA, married Elizabeth. He died in 1666, and after his death his widow married as his third wife Thomas Harmonson of an old Eastern Shore f
2 CONC amily.  Children: (10) William Daniel married Sarah Williams (11) John Daniel married Mary Williams (12) Elizabeth Daniel married John Bates (10) William Daniel died leaving a will in Accomac County, dated in 1688 in which he ment
2 CONC iones two sons and his wife Sarah; witnessed by John Williams, Sr. The two sons of (10) William Daniel (of Accomac County, VA) whose will was d ated in1688, but not probated until 1692, were: (20) Alexander Daniels md Jane Collins
2 CONC  (21) James Daniel, md Anne Parker. The (21) James Daniel, who married Anne Parker, died in Goochland Co., VA intestate in the year 1734.  He left no will but his wife Anne was made administratrix of his estate and Richard Parker 
2 CONC was one of the bondsmen. He had three sons, Richard, William and James Daniel,.  This last named son, James Daniel was the one who married Elizabeth Wooden, daughter of Benjamin Wooden, who is mentioned in this volume in the noes 
2 CONC on page 213 and 242:
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === On June 2 1722, he patented 178 acres in ===
2 CONT On June 2 1722, he patented 178 acres in Goochland on Rocky Run on the head line of John Woodson.
