1 NAME John /Smith/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Smith
2 _MARNM Smith
2 NICK (Smythe)
1 NAME Lt. Colonel John Smith, of Turkey Island
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1625
2 PLAC Kirkham, Lancashire, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 APR 1691
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 TITL Lt. Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Smith was born Abt 1630 in England, and died Bef 1692 in Charles City Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hannah Daft Abt 1670, daughter of William Daft and Joan Parker. She was born Abt 1640 in England, and died Aft 1680 in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Luke Smith Was born in 1710 and died before 1783. His father was Obadiah Smith, son of John Smith who wrote his will in 1689 in Charles City County Virginia. John Smith and Hannah Daft had two sons: Obadiah, and Luke who married A
2 CONC rabella GROMARRIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT ———
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.unc.edu/~rowlett/families/smith_charles_city.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >10 John Smith I, usually called "John of Turkey Island," inherited the 200 acre plantation on Turkey Island Creek. There are a few scattered records of him in Charles City. His wife was named Hannah, and there is one record in wh
2 CONC ich her last name seems to be Daft or Dast; no one has been able to identify her. They had at least two sons Obadiah and John and two daughters Mary and Ann. John died in 1692 and left a will, but it has not survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT * Name:	John Smith Death Date:	28 Apr 1691 County:	Charles City State:	VA Country:	USA Source Information Edmund West, comp.. Family Data Collection - Deaths [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2001.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Links 
