1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/221029358/edward-goode<br/> (memorial removed)
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth 	1695 Henrico County, Virginia<br/>
2 CONT Death 	1733 (aged 37–38) Henrico County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Goode/6000000002967170199?through=6000000002228252007 did not mention a son Edward in his Last Will & Testament written 10 Dec 1734. Although I have found no other evidence that such a son ever e
2 CONC xisted, it is possible he might have died sometime before his father.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Parents: Father: Samuel Goode b: ABT 1658 in Barbados  and Martha Jones
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward was born on the north side of the James River in the Four Mile Creek area and died there. He is buried in a family burial ground on plantation, no marker known.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1701 he and his mother, Margaret were listed as witnesses at the Joseph Woodson wedding.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that Edward was bound out as an apprentice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1712 to ( ) unknown but she died before 1740 mother of all Edwards children. Edward was a farmer all his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second marriage was to Elizabeth (Woodson) Morton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records of Henrico County show Edward accumulated 1,125 acres of land in the Four Mile Creek area. He bought land from others (150 acres from Joseph Pleasants in 1714, in 1716, 15 more acres from Benjamin Burton, Joseph and Thomas
2 CONC  Pleasants) and also received three Kings grants to the land each were for 400 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=johnrobison&id=I00760
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *http://www.ericjames.org/html2014/fam/fam50416.html
2 CONT * https://findingourrootssite.blog/2017/06/03/245/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT This line is from George Brown Goode, (Our Virginia Cousins) published 1886. He worked for the Smithonian Institute for a while, traveled abroad. Some people disagree with his work.  But what I have found makes it right in my mind
2 CONC .
