1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Capt. Jacob 'Jack' Woodson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/124099623/jacob-woodson Find A Grave Memorial ID # 124099623]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A129200 DAR Ancestor #: A129200]
2 CONT Service: VIRGINIA 
2 CONT Rank(s): CAPTAIN
2 CONT Birth: 5-11-1748, PRINCE EDWARD COUNTY, VIRGINIA ''(incorrect county in the DAR database)''
2 CONT Death: 12-5-1839, PRINCE EDWARD COUNTY, VIRGINIA
2 CONT Service Source: GWATHMEY, HIST REG OF VA IN THE REV, P 845
2 CONT Service Description: 1) PRINCE EDWARD COUNTY MILITIA
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was born on 11 May 1748 in Prince Edward County, Virginia, the seventh of eight children and the sixth of seven sons of Obadiah Woodson and Constance Watkins. On 1 November 1775, when he was twenty-seven, he married Elizabet
2 CONC h Morton in Prince Edward County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From this union they had 12 children, four (4) sons and eight (8) daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Facts and Notes''':
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: Captain1
2 CONT Birth: 11 May 1748; Prince Edward County, Virginia, 
2 CONT Marriage: 4 November 1773; Elizabeth Morton; Prince Edward County, Virginia; After their marriage, Elizabeth Morton and Jacob Woodson settled on their farm on the Appomattox River, where they built their picturesque home called "H
2 CONC appy Valley."
2 CONT Military: After 1775; US Revolutionary War; Served in the 4th Virginia Regiment; Commissioned as a captain on 19 Apr 1780
2 CONT Residence: 1779; Prince Edward County, Virginia; No Township Listed
2 CONT Residence: 1783; Prince Edward County, Virginia; No Township Listed
2 CONT Residence: 1810; Prince Edward County, Virginia, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anecdote: Before 1839; He was a man of vigoruous personality, active in colonial affairs and a soldier in the Revolution; held many important offices, and was highly esteemed for his great integrity. His old home "Happy Valley," o
2 CONC n the Appomatox, still stands.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 5 December 1839; Prince Edward County, Virginia
2 CONT Burial: After 5 December 1839; Woodson Cemetery at "Happy Valley", Pamplin, Prince Edward County, Virginia 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Inscription on his tombstone reads: Sacred To the memory of Jacob Woodson Born May 11, 1748 Died Dec 5, 1839 in the 91st year of his age. The heavy head is a crown of glory if it be found in the way of rightness.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1776 - Nov., Took the oath of office as Justice of Prince Edward County
2 CONT 1779 - Aug., Appointed as a Lieutenant in the Militia
2 CONT 1779 - Promoted to Captain in the Militia. Robert Goode and Jacob Woodson were authorized to furnish corn to the soldiers' families
2 CONT 1784 - Served as a Company Captain in the Revolutionary War
2 CONT 1785 - Elected Prince Edward County Magistrate. Signed the Statute for Religious Freedom written by Thomas Jefferson.
2 CONT 1818-19 - Served another term as sheriff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob died at Happy Valley Dec 5, 1839.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jacob Woodson and Elizabeth Morton Woodson:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Obadiah, b. April 6, 1775, d. Sept. 1864
2 CONT 2. Mary, b. April 6, 1775, drowned in the Appomattox River at age of two
2 CONT 3. John Morton Woodson, b. June 28, 1778, d. at Camp Carter in War of 1812
2 CONT 4. Nancy Hix, b. April 3, 1780, m. Dr. Archibald Hix of Hixburg, VA. They went to Missouri.
2 CONT 5. Jane Virginia 'Ginny' Andrews-Atkinson
2 CONT 6. Jacob, Jr., b. Aug. 14, 1783, d. March 8, 1823
2 CONT 7. Sally, b. Aug. 4, 1785, d. July 24, 1871. Lived at Happy Valley, never married.
2 CONT 8. Richard, b. Sept. 21, 1789, d. July 3, 1821, m. Miss Robertson and moved to Missouri.
2 CONT 9. Elizabeth Morton (Betsy) Lewis b. April 22, 1790, m. Judge Henry Lewis, they also moved to Missouri.
2 CONT 10. Patsy, b. Sept. 11, 1792, d. April 18, 1871
2 CONT 11. A son, "Some deformed', died at birth.
2 CONT 12. Judith Elizabeth, b. Nov. 30, 1796, m. Silas Biglow in 1871
2 CONT 13. Agnes Morton Woodson, b. June 22, 1799, d. Aug. 26, 1823, with a fever.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://genealogytrails.com/vir/princeedward/mil_rw_militia_1777.html Prince Edward County Militia]
2 CONT
