1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hughes-3566
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Sydenham "Joanne" Morton formerly Hughes
2 CONT * Born 1660 in Kent, Englandmap
2 CONT * Daughter of Robert Steven Hughes and Rachel (Wade) Hughes
2 CONT * Sister of Sarah Hughes	
2 CONT * Wife of John Morton Sr. — married 25 Jul 1682 in Henrico County, Virginiamap
2 CONT * Mother of Richard Morton, Winifred Morton, Josiah Morton, William John Morton, John Morton, Thomas Morton, Mary Morton, James Morton and Joseph Morton
2 CONT * Died 25 Jul 1760 in Henrico, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Biography'''
2 CONT ======
2 CONT Deborah was born in 1660 in Kent County, England. She died in 1760 in Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Robert Steven Hughes 1630 - 1690 & Rachel (Wade) Hughes 1631 - 1691. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: John Morton Sr. Born in 1655 in Kent County, England. Christened 2/18/1655. They were Married on 7/25/1682 in Henrico County, Virginia. He died in 1722. His will was probated 5/2/1722 in Richmond County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Morton Sr. and Deborah "Joanne" from Muhlenberg County, Kentucky. They are Descendants of Sir William Morton. Generation 2. (link is below kids): 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John Morton Jr. Born: 1689 in Virginia -    Married Mary Jordan (Mountjoy) Born: 1693 - (daughter of Alvin Mountjoy, Sr.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. James Morton. Born 1692 in Richmond County, Virginia. Died 1760 in Lunenburg Parish, Richmond County, Virginia.     Married Elizabeth (Snead) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. William Morton. Born 1694 in Richmond County, Virginia. Died 1740.     Married John Christopher (son of Nicholas & Ann C. (Hughes) Christopher) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Thomas Morton. Born about 1695 in Richmond County, Virginia. Died 2/1729 or 1730 in Henrico County, Virginia.    Married in 1718 to Elizabeth (Woodson) Born: 1999 Died: 99/20/1740. (daughter of Richard & Ann (Smith) Woodson) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Mary Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Richard Morton. Born ? in Richmond County, Virginia. Died in 1732 in Westmoreland County, Virginia.    Married Mercy (Sanford) (daugter of Robert &  ? Sanford Sr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children/Dates/Spouses above are from this source: Muhlenberg County, Kentucky. Descendants of Sir William Morton. Generation 2. http://www.kykinfolk.com/muhlenberg/fgs/familyM/morton-tree.htm It also lists the children's children
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancesty.com and findagrave (on John Morton's page) lists these children with John Morton (names from above are on this list but with different dates and this list has more children) https://www.ancestry.co.uk/genealogy/records/deb
2 CONC orah-joanne-sydenham-hughes-24-3745mp : 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Josiah Morton 1683 - 1753     Married Elizabeth (Davis) in 1704    Has a findagrave page. Linked from his Dad's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Thomas Morton 1690 - 1730
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Richard Morton 1680 - 1732
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William Morton 1676 - 1748
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. James Morton 1692 - 1760
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Capt. John Sydenham Morton 1684 - 1728
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Winfred Morton 1678 - 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Mary Morton 1689 - 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Mary Morton 1682 - 1685
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Jane Morton 1678 - 1683
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Thomas Morton 1690 - 1731    Married Elizabeth (Wooderson) 1699 - 1740. Married in 1718.     Has a findagrave page. Linked from his Dad's. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Need to determine through more research which kids/dates are correct. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Widow Joane Wade married John Morton in 1682.  John Morton’s widow in 1722 was DEBORAH.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [According to the article "Morton Family of Henrico, Prince Edward and New Brunswick" published in the Wm and Mary Quarterly in July 1931, Joseph, Thomas and John were all three sons of the John Morton, Sr. who married Joane Hughe
2 CONC s, a widow.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Name seen as Deborah Joan Sydenham or Hughes. Joanne was married to John Wade (Anes in another place) prior to her marriage to John Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond County, Virginia Wills p.209 
2 CONT *John MORTON, Sitt. Par., will; 27 Jul 1721, 2 May 1722
2 CONT *son Richard land which I bought of Lawrence BARKER;
2 CONT *sons James and Thomas lands and plant, where I now live after the decease of 
2 CONT *wife Deborah; 
2 CONT *if they have no  heirs, to Mary and Winifred MORTON;
2 CONT * sons William and John; 
2 CONT *no ex; 
2 CONT *wits: J. DAVIS, Math. DAVIS.
2 CONT *p.210 - MORTON'S inv. by Deborah MORTON; 6 Jun 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children seen of John Morton and 2nd wife (born after 1682):
2 CONT #JOSIAH MORTON, b. 1683, Henrico County, VA; m. ELIZABETH DAVIS, Abt. 1704; b. Abt. 1687, Virginia.
2 CONT #John Morton Jr., born 1689 Virginia; married Mary Jordon Mountjoy born 1693
2 CONT #Thomas Morton, born 1690/ 1695 Richmond Co., Virginia; died February 1729-30 Henrico Co., Virginia; married Elizabeth Woodson, daughter of Richard Woodson & Ann Smith, 1718 Virginia. Elizabeth was born 1699 & 20 September 1740.
2 CONT #James Morton, born 1692 / 1695 Richmond Co., Virginia; died 1760 Lunenburg Parish, Richmond Co., Virginia; married Elizabeth Snead. Children: Charles Morton, Snead Morton, Thomas Morton
2 CONT #MARY MORTON, b. 1691, King George County, VA.
2 CONT #RICHARD MORTON, b. Abt. 1692, St. Thomas Parish, Richmond County, VA.
2 CONT #William Morton, born 1694 Richmond Co., Virginia; will probated 28 July 1747 Orange Co., Virginia; married Ann Batchelder, daughter of Thomas Batchelder & Mary Quisenberry, about 1719 Virginia. She was born about 1698 Virginia & 
2 CONC died 1748 Orange Co., Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond County, VA: Will Book No. 3[2] Morton, John. 27 July, 1721 - 2 May, 1722. Sons Richard, James, Thomas; wife Deborah, to have plantation and after her death to Mary and Winifred Morton; son William, son John
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1691 there appeared a petition of Henry Randolph for 100 acres of land because he had imported Susannah Symonds and Ann Hughes.  [Was Ann any relation to Joan?]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT supposedly she was from Luisa County Va and arrived from Europe with the Randolphs.  
2 CONT
2 CONT John Morton transferred 200 acres to William Randolph in Chickahominy Swamp 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From RootsWeb: It is said John Morton and William Randolph came to Virginia about 1675 on the same ship and probably the about the same age, twenty-two. William Randolph lived in Moreton Morrell Warwickshire west midlands of Engla
2 CONC nd. Henrico County Records shows "that John Morton had imported himself and wife from England and was entitled to land grant." Based on this assumption, John was married twice(Deborah Sydenham for first wife is debated?) There is 
2 CONC five years difference between second son Winfred 1678 and third son Josiah Morton 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia records shows John Morton married a widow Joane Wade in 1682. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Morton married Deborah "Joanne" (Sydenham) Hughes (b 1655 co. Kent , England), widow of John Hughes.
2 CONT
