1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RICHARD MORTON, b. Abt. 1692, St. Thomas Parish, Richmond County, VA .  
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: John Morton born: bet. 1640 & 1660 in [Shropshire], England died: bef. 5/2/1722 in Sittlenbourne Parish, Richmond County, Virginia
2 CONT *Mother:  'Joanne' (Hughes) born: bet. 1652 & 1655 in Kent, England died: aft. 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Massey Sanford.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond County, Virginia Wills p.209 
2 CONT *John MORTON, Sitt. Par., will; 27 Jul 1721, 2 May 1722
2 CONT *son Richard land which I bought of Lawrence BARKER;
2 CONT *sons James and Thomas lands and plant, where I now live after the decease of 
2 CONT *wife Deborah; 
2 CONT *if they have no  heirs, to Mary and Winifred MORTON;
2 CONT * sons William and John; 
2 CONT *no ex; 
2 CONT *wits: J. DAVIS, Math. DAVIS.
2 CONT *p.210 - MORTON'S inv. by Deborah MORTON; 6 Jun 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT WESTMORELAND COUNTY WILLS
2 CONT *MORTON, RICHARD, 18 Nov. 1731; 27 Sept. 1732.
2 CONT *Wife Massey and my children to have all my estate;
2 CONT *father in law Robert Sanford Sr. exr.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT === Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT named as a child of John Morton d 1722: Abstracts from Records of Richmond County, VA: Will Book No. 3; Wm. and Mary Qrtly., Vol.17-3 Morton, John. 27 July, 1721 - 2 May, 1722. Sons Richard, James, Thomas; wife Deborah, to have pl
2 CONC antation and after her death to Mary and Winifred Morton; son William, son John.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Morton-504
2 CONT * https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/i/v/e/Patricia-G-Iverson/GENE6-0002.html#CHILD2
2 CONT * https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I114394&tree=Tree1
