0 @I6000000013824764920@ INDI
1 NAME Joseph /Morton/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 SURN Morton
2 _MARNM Morton
2 NICK Moreton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1693
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 MAR 1753
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [According to the article "Morton Family of Henrico, Prince Edward and New Brunswick" published in the Wm and Mary Quarterly in July 1931, Joseph, Thomas and John were all three sons of the John Morton, Sr. who mar
2 CONC ried Joane Hughes, a widow.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Morton 
2 CONT *By 1733 he had married “Jene” [Jane?] [Unknown] per his son John’s bible record.[1] So Jane and John were undoubtedly her children.
2 CONT *In 1738 he married Elizabeth [Unknown]. When he sold 400 acres of 1072 patent on Sandy Rv to Jacob McGehee in 1738, wife Elizabeth relinquished her dower.[2] She was not mentioned when he sold 600 acres earlier that year to Edwar
2 CONC d Osborne.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jane Morton m. <1749 Reuben Roy
2 CONT # John Morton b. November 20, 1733.
2 CONT # Joseph Morton. Moved to Georgia.
2 CONT # Jehu Morton. Moved to North Carolina.
2 CONT # Martha Morton
2 CONT # Ann Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was working as an overseer for Col. Richard Randolph in 1737, and continued to pay tax in Amelia County until 1753. He was elected a vestryman of Nottoway Parish in 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT As "Joseph Morton Sr. of Brunswick County", he sold 225 acres on Sandy River to his nephew Thomas Morton and 800 acres near the Sandy River to Joseph Ligon 15 February 1744/45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was a resident of Lunenburg County when he made his will but it was recorded in the newly-formed Halifax County. He divided 1,200 acres on the Sandy Creek among sons John, Joseph, and Jehu and identified three daughters. Hi
2 CONC s wife was then Elizabeth --- (will dated 7 December 1749, recorded March 20, 1753). (From "Virginians: The Family History of John W. Pritchett" website: www.virginians.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Morton Sr. of Lunenburg Co. wrote his will on Dec 7 1749:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Named wife Elizabeth. Children: John, Joseph, Jehu, Jane Roy, Martha, and Ann.
2 CONT * Exec: Capt Charles Anderson, Joseph Morton, Jr. [not listed as son], wife, and son John.
2 CONT * Witns: Thomas Morton, Sam’l[+] Morton, Joseph Morton Jr.
2 CONT * [Thomas Morton [son of Thomas], Sam’l Morton and Joseph Morton Jr. [sons of John]. That his nephew was referred to as Jr. implies his son Joseph was still quit young
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT Not named as a child of John Morton d 1722: Abstracts from Records of Richmond County, VA: Will Book No. 3; Wm. and Mary Qrtly., Vol.17-3 Morton, John. 27 July, 1721 - 2 May, 1722. Sons Richard, James, Thomas; wife Deborah, to hav
2 CONC e plantation and after her death to Mary and Winifred Morton; son William, son John.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/photo.php/b/ba/Morton-157.pdf
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Morton-491
2 CONT * https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/i/v/e/Patricia-G-Iverson/GENE6-0003.html#CHILD5
2 CONT *https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/902228:2204?indiv=1&tid=&pid=&queryId=061f9b91521dfe080b9b556fa249d7c0&usePUB=true&_phsrc=yzO281&_phstart=successSource
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [According to the article "Morton Family of Henrico, Prince Edward and New Brunswick" published in the Wm and Mary Quarterly in July 1931, Joseph, Thomas and John were all three sons of the John Morton, Sr. who married Joane Hughe
2 CONC s, a widow.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Joseph Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1733 he had married “Jene” [Jane?] [Unknown] per his son John’s bible record.[1] So Jane and John were undoubtedly her children.
2 CONT In 1738 he married Elizabeth [Unknown]. When he sold 400 acres of 1072 patent on Sandy River to Jacob McGehee in 1738, wife Elizabeth relinquished her dower.[2] She was not mentioned when he sold 600 acres earlier that year to Edw
2 CONC ard Osborne.[3]
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Morton m. <1749 Reuben Roy
2 CONT John Morton b. November 20, 1733.
2 CONT Joseph Morton. Moved to Georgia.
2 CONT Jehu Morton. Moved to North Carolina.
2 CONT Martha Morton
2 CONT Ann Morton
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Joseph was working as an overseer for Col. Richard Randolph in 1737, and continued to pay tax in Amelia County until 1753. He was elected a vestryman of Nottoway Parish in 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT As "Joseph Morton Sr. of Brunswick County", he sold 225 acres on Sandy River to his nephew Thomas Morton and 800 acres near the Sandy River to Joseph Ligon 15 February 1744/45.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was a resident of Lunenburg County when he made his will but it was recorded in the newly-formed Halifax County. He divided 1,200 acres on the Sandy Creek among sons John, Joseph, and Jehu and identified three daughters. Hi
2 CONC s wife was then Elizabeth --- (will dated 7 December 1749, recorded March 20, 1753). (From "Virginians: The Family History of John W. Pritchett" website: www.virginians.com).
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Morton Sr. of Lunenburg Co. wrote his will on Dec 7, 1749:
2 CONT
2 CONT Named wife Elizabeth. Children: John, Joseph, Jehu, Jane Roy, Martha, and Ann.
2 CONT Exec: Capt Charles Anderson, Joseph Morton, Jr. [not listed as son], wife, and son John.
2 CONT Witns: Thomas Morton, Sam’l[+] Morton, Joseph Morton Jr.
2 CONT [Thomas Morton [son of Thomas], Sam’l Morton and Joseph Morton Jr. [sons of John]. That his nephew was referred to as Jr. implies his son Joseph was still quit young
2 CONT Origins
2 CONT Not named as a child of John Morton d 1722: Abstracts from Records of Richmond County, VA: Will Book No. 3; Wm. and Mary Qrtly., Vol.17-3 Morton, John. 27 July, 1721 - 2 May, 1722. Sons Richard, James, Thomas; wife Deborah, to hav
2 CONC e plantation and after her death to Mary and Winifred Morton; son William, son John.
