3 CITY Malvern Hills
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1729
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Daughter of Henry Watkins and Katherine (Pride) Watkins
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Removed 1729 as date of death - unknown. She probably died before 1729 because she was not mentioned in Robert Woodson's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Removed Era, Cooke, Texas, United States as place of death -- there were only a handful of English explorers in Texas at that time and no settlements. Why would she leave her husband in Virginia?
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, Sarah to Joseph Parsons, Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT >By Rachael Watkins, his second wife, Jonathan, and daughters, Elizabeth and Judith. Elizabeth married John Knight, and Judith married John Cook, and she was mother to all the money-making Cooks.
