1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 5) Edward Watkins, born about 1676; died 1771 in Cumberland County, VA.    Edward Watkins was a brother of Thomas “of Swift Creek” Watkins, as written by Mr. Francis N. Watkins of Farmville in 1859.  He is also dis
2 CONC cussed in several other publications, best recollected as the great-grandfather of Henry Clay.    The best I have been able to determine, '''Edward had three wives, the name of only the second known.'''  He did not name a wife in 
2 CONC his will, and it is '''not believed he had any children by his third wife.    ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by his first wife:
2 CONT # A)  John W. (son of Edward) WATKINS of Cumberland County, VA (b.Abt 1710 d.Jan 1765-Cumberland County,VA) sp: Phoebe HANCOCK (b.10 May 1719 d.Abt 1777-Buckingham County,VA)
2 CONT # B)  Thomas (son of Edward) WATKINS of Henrico Co., VA (b.Abt 1720-Swift Creek,Henrico County,VA d.1780/1781-Henrico County,VA) sp: Mary CLAY
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward’s second wife was Mary Bishop TAYLOR PENDLETON (m.Abt 1723).   They had the following children:
2 CONT # C) . Mary WATKINS (b.22 Mar 1726 d.13 Nov 1805-Chesterfield County,VA) | sp: Jordan ANDERSON (b.1723 m.15 Sep 1748 d.1805)
2 CONT # D)   Sarah Elizabeth WATKINS (b.Abt 1726 d.Abt 1750-Chesterfield County,VA) | sp: "Sir" John CLAY (b.1721 m.Abt 1740 d.1762)
2 CONT # E)   Edward (Jr.) WATKINS of Cumberland County, VA (b.Circa 1726 d.1812/1813-Powhatan Co.,VA)   | sp: Rhoda THOMPSON (b.1732 m.17 Apr 1759 d.1827)
2 CONT # F)   Martha WATKINS (b.Henrico County,VA)  | sp: Francis MOSELEY (d.1782/1783)
2 CONT # G)   Judith WATKINS | sp: Thomas BASS (b.1725 d.1804)
2 CONT # H)  Frances WATKINS  | sp: Richard MOSELEY (m.1803)
2 CONT # I)  George (son of Edward) WATKINS  | sp: Rebecca THOMPSON
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.oursoutherncousins.com/watkins2.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Watkins, born about 1676; died 1771 in Cumberland County, VA.    Edward Watkins was a brother of Thomas “of Swift Creek” Watkins, as written by Mr. Francis N. Watkins of Farmville in 1859.  He is also discussed in several o
2 CONC ther publications, best recollected as the great-grandfather of Henry Clay.    The best I have been able to determine, Edward had three wives, the name of only the second known.  He did not name a wife in his will, and it is not b
2 CONC elieved he had any children by his third wife.     
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by his first wife: 
2 CONT
2 CONT A)  John W. (son of Edward) WATKINS of Cumberland County, VA (b.Abt 1710 d.Jan 1765-Cumberland County,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: Phoebe HANCOCK (b.10 May 1719 d.Abt 1777-Buckingham County,VA) B)  Thomas (son of Edward) WATKINS of Henrico Co., VA (b.Abt 1720-Swift Creek,Henrico County,VA d.1780/1781-Henrico County,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: Mary CLAY
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward’s second wife was Mary Bishop TAYLOR PENDLETON (m.Abt 1723).   They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT C) . Mary WATKINS (b.22 Mar 1726 d.13 Nov 1805-Chesterfield County,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: Jordan ANDERSON (b.1723 m.15 Sep 1748 d.1805) D)   Sarah Elizabeth WATKINS (b.Abt 1726 d.Abt 1750-Chesterfield County,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: "Sir" John CLAY (b.1721 m.Abt 1740 d.1762) E)   Edward (Jr.) WATKINS of Cumberland County, VA (b.Circa 1726 d.1812/1813-Powhatan Co.,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: Rhoda THOMPSON (b.1732 m.17 Apr 1759 d.1827) F)   Martha WATKINS (b.Henrico County,VA)
2 CONT  | sp: Francis MOSELEY (d.1782/1783) G)   Judith WATKINS
2 CONT  | sp: Thomas BASS (b.1725 d.1804) H)  Frances WATKINS
2 CONT  | sp: Richard MOSELEY (m.1803) I)  George (son of Edward) WATKINS
2 CONT  | sp: Rebecca THOMPSON
