1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pride, of Pemaquid, married Jane Lovering before 1675.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He followed his father's initial occupation as a fisherman where he is first mentioned as such at Cape Bonawagon in 1661. He took the Oath of Fidelity to Massachusetts in 1674. He then took the oath of fidelity in Beverly, Massach
2 CONC usetts in 1677, but returned to Cape Bonawagon for a few years before his family permanently settled in Beverly where his wife died in 1713 and he died about 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of John Pride and Jane Lovering's six children were baptized on Dec. 12, 1686 in Beverly, Massachusetts.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Pride-113
2 CONT
2 CONT John Pride (1637 - 1730)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John Pride===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1637 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Pride and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Elizabeth (Pride) Tapley
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Jane (Lovering) Pride — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Peter Pride, William Pride, Elizabeth (Pride) Conant and Joseph Pride
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1730 at about age 93 in Beverly, Essex, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 19 Oct 2017 | Created 23 Jan 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Clarence Almon Torrey, New England Marriages Prior To 1700 (Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1985); PRIDE, John & Jane [LOVERING]; by 1675, 6 ch bpt 1686; Pemaquid/Beverly {Conant 155; Reg. 62:95; GDMNH 445,
2 CONC  569}
2 CONT ↑ Town and City Clerks of Massachusetts. Massachusetts Vital and Town Records. Provo, UT: Holbrook Research Institute (Jay and Delene Holbrook). Pride Family Baptism Records
2 CONT ↑ Clarence Almon Torrey, New England Marriages Prior To 1700 (Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 1985); PRIDE, John & Jane [LOVERING]; by 1675, 6 ch bpt 1686; Pemaquid/Beverly {Conant 155; Reg. 62:95; GDMNH 445,
2 CONC  569}
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT New England Historical and Genealogical Register (Boston, MA: New England Historical and Genealogical Society); Vol. 62, pg. 95
2 CONT Sybil Noyes, Charles Thornton Libby and Walter Goodwin Davis, Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire; (Republished Baltimore, MD: Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1996); pgs. 445, 569
2 CONT Frederick Odell Conant, A History and Genealogy of the Conant Family in England and America, Thirteen Generations, 1520 to 1887 (1887); pg. 155
