1 NOTE {geni:about_me} {{https://media.geni.com/p14/fa/ff/8a/5b/53444868b1bcaf54/children_of_lydia_watkins_original.jpg?hash=05045a4f6ee632f5bfb6d33e52626f6ffed907346d0885a849c5de018454394f.1745823599}}
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/sharing/36582555?mark=7b22746f6b656e223a2246766b50713161714956336f61674475344779464c73655630614168502b46494e6e71374764456c4650593d222c22746f6b656e5f76657273696f6e223a225632227d 
2 CONT *[http://oursoutherncousins.com/watkins.html Our Southern Cousins] ''Contains: Deeds, Wills, Quaker Meeting Records.'' 
2 CONT *[http://oursoutherncousins.com/Descendants%20of%20HENRY%20WATKINS,%20JR..pdf Descendants of Henry Watkins Pdf]
2 CONT
2 CONT HENRY WATKINS, son of Henry… Henry Watkins who died in Henrico County in 1714 was the son of Henry born about 1638. His will named wife MARY, sons John, '''Benjamin''', Joseph, Henry and Stephen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Watkins, son of Henry who died in 1714, married his cousin JANE WATKINS, daughter of Thomas Watkins of Swift Creek. Benjamin's will was proved in Goochland County in 1753 and Jane's was proved in 1778. Other Watkins wills
2 CONC  recorded in Goochland County give information on the children and grandchildren of Benjamin and Jane Watkins.
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin married Jean/Jane WATKINS, daughter of THOMAS "of Swift Creek" WATKINS * and Elizabeth PRIDE *, on 1726 in Henrico County, VA. Jean/Jane was born 1708 in Henrico County, VA. She died 2 Dec 1777 in Goochland County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Jane Watkins ' Will. Goochland (31st October, 1777 , p. March 16, 1778 ), mentions: Sons: Joseph , Thomas and Benj. Daughters: Mary Johnson , Judith Johnson , '''Lydia Johnson''' , Edith Riddle , Jane Matthews and Susannah Gr
2 CONC ay. Jane (Jaen) Watkins was born in 1708 in Henrico, Virginia. She died on 2 Dec 1777 in Goochland, Virginia. She was sealed to her parents on 5 Dec 1979 in the Salt Lake temple. She was baptized on 17 Aug 1979 in the Salt Lake te
2 CONC mple. She was endowed on 20 Sep 1979 in the Salt Lake temple. She married Benjamin Watkins in 1726 in , Henrico, Virginia. They were sealed on 5 Oct 1948 in the Manti Utah temple. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://oursoutherncousins.com/Descendants%20of%20HENRY%20WATKINS,%20JR..pdf
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia was a daughter of Benjamin Watkins. She married John Johnson III on 13 Jul 1754, Hanover, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: James Clark Johnson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy Vol. VI
