1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Skiffen''' was born about 1642 in England, the daughter of William Skiffen.  She died after 1694 in  Charles City County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, William Skiffen, was born Abt. 1620.  William Skiffen who was imported prior 1650 by John Hallowes of Northumberland County, Colony of Virginia. [Cavaliers and Pioneers, Patent Book 2, p. 193
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Skiffen married (1) Reynard Anderson 1662 in Charles City County, Virginia; married (2) Edward Hughes Aft. 1690 in Charles City County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1662 Charles City County Court Orders 1661-1664, page 373. “Wm House is charged with marrying Reynard Anderson & Elizabeth Skiffen without a license.[2]]”
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Anderson-22645
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Reynard and Elizabeth (Skiffen) ANDERSON:[17]
2 CONT
2 CONT # i. MAYBE JAMES ANDERSON, b. between 1663 and 1667 in Charles City Co., and d. between 1694 and 1704 in Prince George Co., Virginia. He may have married ELIZABETH THWEATT, daughter of James Thweatt and Mary Lee. Elizabeth was b. 
2 CONC ca. 1670 in Charles City Co. and d. after 1712 in Prince George Co.
2 CONT # ii. FRANCES ANDERSON, born between 1663 and 1670 in Charles City Co.; died 1726 in Prince George Co.; m. (1) JOHN HERBERT; m. (2) THOMAS COCKE; m. (3) JOSHUA WYNNE.
2 CONT # iii. MATTHEW ANDERSON, SR., b. between 1668 and 1683 in Charles City Co. Matthew was b. near Bailey’s Creek (vicinity of Petersburg, Virginia) after 1668 to be under the age of 21 at the time of the 1689 record identifying him a
2 CONC s a son of Reynard Anderson.
2 CONT # iv. WILLIAM ANDERSON, b. between 1670 and 1675 in Charles City Co.; d. before 1716 in Prince George Co.; m. MARY LIGON.
2 CONT # v. JOHN ANDERSON, b. between 1672 and 1683 in Charles City Co.; d. unmarried and childless in 1725 in Prince George Co. John was b. near Bailey’s Creek (vicinity of Petersburg, Virginia) after 1668 (he was under 21 when he was i
2 CONC dentified as the son of Reynard Anderson).
2 CONT # vi. HENRY ANDERSON, b. between 1674 and 1683 in Charles City Co.; died 1734 in Henrico Co., Virginia; m. (1) PRUDENCE STRATTON; m. (2) ELIZABETH CLAIBORNE.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://homepages.rootsweb.com/~anderson/va/trees/reynard.html
2 CONT
