1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note: Frances (Anderson) Wynne is a different woman, born about 1685 and married to Peter Wynne
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Anderson-13405
2 CONT
2 CONT FRANCES ANDERSON, daughter of Reynard Anderson and Elizabeth Skiffen, was born between 1663 and 1670 in Charles City County, Virginia, just northeast of current Petersburg, and died 1726 in Prince George County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT *(1) JOHN HERBERT before 1687.[4] He was born 1659 in London, England, and died 16 March 1703/04 at “Puddledock,” Charles City County. 
2 CONT * (2) THOMAS COCKE ca. 1705 [or 1707?]. 
2 CONT * (3) JOSHUA WYNNE ca. 1711. He was born 1662 and died 1715 in Prince George County.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Herbert, a wealthy trader, lived on his estate “Puddlecock,” east of Petersburg; the widowed Mrs. Herbert was credited with 3925 acres of land in the 1704 rent roll of Prince George County and 1360 acres in Henrico County
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1716 (during her third marriage) Mrs. Frances Wynne was still executrix of (her first husband’s) Herbert’s estate. She made her own will on 16 October 1725, probated 4 March 1726/7.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances’s second husband, CAPT. THOMAS COCKE was born ca. 1662, son of Thomas Cocke and (possibly) Agnes Powell. His will, 16 January 1706/7, with a codicil 14 February 1706/7, was proven 15 October 1725. In his will he named his 
2 CONC issue: Thomas, James Powell, Brazure, Mary, and Elizabeth. These were all children by his first wife, Mary Brasseur of Nansemond, daughter of John Brasseur and Mary Pitt.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and Frances (Anderson) HERBERT:
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. MARTHA HERBERT, b. 1688 in Charles City Co., Virginia; m. JAMES POWELL COCKE. He was the son of Thomas Cocke and Thomas’s first wife, Mary Brasseur. Martha and James Powell were step siblings—with her mother married to his fa
2 CONC ther.
2 CONT * ii. ANN HERBERT, b. between 1690 and 1700; dead by 1725.
2 CONT * iii. BULLER HERBERT, b. between 1690 and 1700 in Charles City County; d. after Nov. 1730 in Prince George Co., Virginia; m. MARY STITH.
2 CONT * iv. RICHARD HERBERT, b. between 1690 and 1700 in Charles City Co.; d. 1731 in Henrico County, Virginia; m. PHOEBE ROBERTSON.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *Southside Virginia Families, Volume 2.  Page 162.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=a7tx6lhj-CkC&lpg=PA162&dq=Buller%20Herbert&pg=PA162#v=onepage&q=Buller%20Herbert&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *James P. C. Southall. “Origins of the Cocke Families of Virginia.” The William and Mary Quarterly 9, no. 1 (1929): 49–59. https://doi.org/10.2307/1920377.
