1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rowland Ward's will, admitted to probate on Oct. 23, 1800, in Amelia County, Virginia.  He named in his will the following persons:  son Edward, executor; daughter- Martha Jones; daughter-Margaret Jones; daughter A
2 CONC nn Jones: grandson Henry Ward; granddaughter-Prudence Jones; grandson - Richard Henry Jones.  He set free the following slaves: Peter, Isham, Marsha, Little Rachal, and gave them the land in Nottaway County, Virginia, that he had 
2 CONC purchased from Nathaniel Robertson and William May Porter. 
