2 PLAC Little Rock, Pulaski County, Arkansas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Watkins Cocke was the son of Richard Cocke, 17xx-1829,and Mary (Watkins) Cocke, who at one time owned a large estate in the Valley Hill district, part of which became the property of Samuel Grundy.  His patern
2 CONC al grandparents were: Stephen Cocke, Sr. and Amy (Jones) Cocke, who immigrated to Washington County, Kentucky from Nottoway Country, Virginia.  John Watkins Coke's mother was the niece of Frances (Watkins) Walton, wife of General 
2 CONC Matthew Walton.
2 CONT
2 CONT J. W. Pope married Elizabeth Pope, 1815-1835, who was the daughter of the Hon. John Pope and Elizabeth (Johnson) Pope.  His bride was the niece of Katherine (Johnson) Adams, First Lady of the United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At on time John Watkins and Elizabeth (Pope) Cocke were owners of the Walton House farm on Bardstown Road on the north side of St. Catharine (once St. Magdeline's) Motherhouse.  After the death of his wife, John Watkins Cocke move
2 CONC d to Little Rock, Arkansas where he became a prominent lawyer.  In 1844 he and Daniel Ring became co-executor to the will of his father-in-law, Hon. John Pope, who was from 1829-1835, during the administration of President Andrew 
2 CONC Jackson, the Territorial Governor of Arkansas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On page 774 of St. Rose Sacramental Register IV, it says that John Watkins Cocke died in Arkansas and was re-interred in St. Rose Cemetery on March 16, 1851.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Elizabeth have no marriage record in Washington County, Kentucky and I have not learned how they were converted to Roman Catholicism.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/104418971/john-watkins-cocke Find A Grav
2 CONC e Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 14 2019, 20:02:34 UTC''
