1 NOTE John Fletcher Watkins died between 27 January 1857 when his Will was written and 2 April 1859 when it was filed in Rusk Co. Texas.( I find that he died 10 Feb 1859) He married in Anson County, NC and they moved to Spring Lake in M
2 CONC arengo County and then to Wilcox County.  It was probably after Sarah's death that he moved to Rusk County, Texas where his estate inventory showed that he owned more than 2100 Acres of land. They had eleven children.(From the Bib
2 CONC le of Mary Ann Watkins Devan-in her own handwriting.) Only eight children were listed in John's Will. Catherine Watkins wriotes that the greatest portion of the information on the john Fletcher Watkins family was contained in a bo
2 CONC ok, Kimbrough, Dumas and Related Southern Families by Margaret Kimbrough Mulkey, Naples, Florida, 1977. The book contains a photographic copy of the Bible page listing the birth of the Watkins children, as well as a copy of the wi
2 CONC ll of John Watkins.  It is interesting to note that one of the securities for William F. Watkins (executor) was Isaac Dansby who had married Seraphina Watkins (1831-1869), daughter of James L. Watkins (brother of John Fletcher Wat
2 CONC kins). The book con- tains an extract of an 18 Dec 1901 letter from Thomas J. Watkins(son of Mumford D. Watkins) of Anson County, NC to Mrs. R. W. (Alice Dumas) Henderson.
