1 NOTE James Lamartin Watkins was a twin to Calvin Gaston Watkins. James L., together with his brothers Brackett and John Fletcher Watkins, was a part of a migration from the Flat Fork section of Anson County, NC to Alabama. They went by
2 CONC  wagon train. This took place between 1820's to 1840's.  Some of our other relatives, Allens and Threadgill families were with the Watkin families. They wanted to have better virgin soil, and more land.  They were in the same gene
2 CONC ral area of Marengo County, Alabama. In a letter written by one of the Allen family members, John Gray Allen, brother to Thetis Allen, James Lamartin Watkins was described as "a good neighbor".
1 CHAN
