1 NOTE Brackett O. Watkins and Family were living in Marengo Co., Alabama, having moved from Anson Co. NC, as did two of his brothers.  In Jan of 1841 John Gray Allen stayed with them and bought some land in AL. Brackett's wife was Dolly
2 CONC  Curtis. Mrs Nancy R. K. Curtis Boatright was a sister of Dolly Curtis. John Gray Allen met and married Mrs Boatright after her divorce. Marengo County Will Book A, page 283, shows will of Brackett O. Watkins dated 19 April 1840, 
2 CONC probated 12 July 1842. The will makes reference to three children. Military service records show that Bracket O. Watkins was in the Confederate service, but late in the war changed allegiance and served with the Union Army. Some o
2 CONC f this information for Brackett and his family was found in a book by Pauline Gandrud and in "The Dumas Families, Vol I by John H. Wilson, 1212 W. El Paso Street, Fort Worth, Texas (1986).
