1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1771 Carroll County Arkansas, USA Death: 	Feb. 14, 1856 Boone County Arkansas, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT b. Crooked Creek, Carroll/Boone County, Arkansas, American Colonies d. Crooked Creek, Boone County, Arkansas
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Soldier, Indian Fighter, Farmer, Peace Officer (Constable/Sheriff).
2 CONT
2 CONT Fought in the 1793/94 Cherokee Indian War. Was in the Indian campaigns around Ft Mims, Alabama. Private in Captain Bartlett Marshall's Company, Tennessee Militia and was drafted in Hawkins County, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mustered into service at Knoxville, Tennessee in September or October of 1793 he continued in actual service for three months and was honorably discharged at Knoxville, Tennessee in the latter part of l793. Fought in the Second Cr
2 CONC eek Indian War and the War of 1812-14 at the Battle of Horsebend.
2 CONT
2 CONT Private in Captain Anthony Metcalf's Company of the 2nd Regiment 5th Battalion of Tennessee Militia (Colonel McCrory commander) in the war with the Creek Indians. Volunteered as a substitute in place of John Hays who was drafted i
2 CONC n Smith County, Tennessee and served for a three month term.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mustered in at Fayettesville, Tennessee September or October of l813. In early January 1815, Jacob, under General Andrew Jackson's command, fought the British at the Battle of New Orleans. Dismissed at Huntsville, Alabama and hono
2 CONC rably discharged early part of l815 in Smith County, Tennessee. 
2 CONT
