1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the fall of 1814, Lt. George Turney of the third West Tennessee Militia regiment, packed 300 pounds of gear: uniforms, food, provisions for his horse, etc.  He and a servant embarked with their regiment, probabl
2 CONC y at Nashville, as part of a flotilla, headed south via the Cumberland, Ohio and Mississippi Rivers.  Their mission was to defend New Orleans, the gateway to the Mississippi River Valley, against capture by the British in the War 
2 CONC of 1812.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They were part of Major General William Carroll’s division.  The whole defensive force was under the command of Major General Andrew Jackson.  All his five brothers, sons of Henry and Catherine Turney, fought for General Jackson a
2 CONC s well.  George fought in the Battle of Mobile, Battle of Horseshoe Bend and the Battle of New Orleans. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Then, on the morning of January 8, 1815, the British assaulted the American line three times.  All these assaults were repulsed.  General Pakenham was killed in the third assault.  The British suffered 2,037 casualties, the Americ
2 CONC ans only seventy-one.
2 CONT
2 CONT The news of victory, one man recalled, ‘came upon the country like a clap of thunder in the clear azure vault of the firmament, and traveled with electromagnetic velocity, throughout the confines of the land.’
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
