1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Smith Co., TN with his parents, but by 1818 he and his family weere living in Cotaco County (Morgan after 1821).  He and his brother Joseph were among the first land owners in 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Turney was listed in the 1830 Census Index for Morgan Co., AL
2 CONT
2 CONT He is listed in an article as a Pioneer.  Article was found on Ancestry.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sergeant , 2nd Regiment Tennessee Mounted Volunteers.this unit comprised the sixty-day volunteers enlisted by William Carroll to fill the rapidly dwindling ranks of Jackson's army decimated by the desertions of December 1813.Fough
2 CONC t the Red Sticks Jan 1814
2 CONT
2 CONT "Daniel Watson Turney didn't have a will. His estate went through probate with his son George B. Turney as the administrator. There is no doubt that George B. was Daniel Watson's son. I carefully read through the over 150 original
2 CONC  pages of the probate and George B. Turney's signature was all over them. All of Daniel Watson's estate, slaves and possessions were all sold off to family members and neighbors and others. I have posted a few copies of the docume
2 CONC nts but I haven't had a chance to post everything. I believe they should show up on my link to George B. Turney. Although I don't believe any longer that William R Turney was Daniel Watson's son, I believe he was very close to the
2 CONC  family possibly a nephew. When George B Turney died apparently without a will also, William R Turney served co administrator over his estate along with George's brother in law James McGlothery. Honestly there wasn't much paperwor
2 CONC k in that file. George died after the Civil War and I just don't think much was left of his estate. But those original records are available at the Morgan County Archives. Some of those original documents were very difficult to re
2 CONC ad.
2 CONT
2 CONT I also visited Cook Cemetery where Daniel Watson Turney and Mildred are buried along with most of their children. The stones are over 150 years old and not very easy to read. I'm pretty sure the land where the cemetery is located 
2 CONC was originally Daniel Watson's. I don't know where George B is buried but it is hard to believe he would be buried anywhere else.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I have a book on the Bain family. I will look up your John Wesley Bain and see what family connection he has to Mary Polly Bain Turney, wife of William R Turney. Her father was David Bain. There are so many John Bains and Mary Bai
2 CONC ns I have them all confused."
2 CONT
2 CONT Doug Turney--17 Aug 2017  dltinokla
