2 CONT '''LE GRANDE, ALEXANDER''' DAR  Ancestor #: A069087 [https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A069087 DAR]
2 CONT
2 CONT Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): PATRIOTIC SERVICE Birth:  12-25-1732    GOOCHLAND CO VIRGINIA Death:  ANTE 3-21-1822     PRINCE EDWARD CO VIRGINIA Service Source:  ABERCROMBIE & SLATTEN, VA REV PUB CLAIMS, VOL 3, P 791 Service Desc
2 CONC ription:  1) RENDERED MATERIAL AID
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE Created: 2002-03-27 23:23:55.3, Updated: , By: Conversion 1) County: PRINCE EDWARD CO - State: VIRGINIA
2 CONT
2 CONT SPOUSE Number Name 1) LUCY WALKER  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Alexander Le Grande''' was born on December 25, 1732, in Goochland County, Virginia, USA. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-61161664 Jean Pierre LeGrand] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-61161710 Jane Magdalen LeG
2 CONC rand]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander married [https://www.geni.com/profile-59993400 Elizabeth Lucy LeGrand (Walker)] on November 23, 1757, in Cumberland, Virginia, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34653217283 Judith Ann Michaux Fitch];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568186 Josiah LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-17345392 Baker LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568326 Sarah Wilson];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-2751701 Margaretta Drusilla Lancaster (LeGrand)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568306 Alexander Legrand, II];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568317 Jane LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568318 Susan Woodson];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568322 Lucy Cox];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568324 Nancy Snead Binford (LeGrand)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 	January 25, 1822 , in Prince Edward County, Virginia, USA, and possibly was buried in Old City Cemetery, Lynchburg, Lynchburg City, Virginia, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Served as a Land Processional for Vestry from 1763-1767
2 CONT * Prince Edward County Court issued him a permit for a Flour Mill in 1795 on the Appomattox River. 
2 CONT * Petitioned the General Assembly in 1795 to establish a town on a tract of land he owned (Near Hampton-Sydney College) which thought would be a proper place for an island town. The request was granted, authorized by the trustees,
2 CONC  James Morton, Josiah Le Grande, Baker, Le Grande, and others, to lay off 25 acres into 1/2 acre lots with convenient streets, to this town given the name of Germantown, The name survives in a road leading to the site. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References and Notes'''
2 CONT
