1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Sanbourne Woodson''' was born on September 11, 1707 in Curles, Henrico County, Virginia, British Colonial America. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-67638576 Joseph Woodson] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-760702
2 CONC 11 Mary Woodson (Sanbourne)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanbourne married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34792200856 Elizabeth Woodson (Michaux)] in June 1728 in Cumberland County, Province of Virginia, Colonial America. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-76070235 Captain Hughes Woodson, Sr]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanbourne married [https://www.geni.com/profile-38883145 Charity Woodson Burch (Cheadle?)] before November 18, 1745 in Cumberland County, Virginia, Colonial America. Together they had the following 5 children named in their father
2 CONC 's will:
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Captain-Hughes-Woodson-Sr/6000000007273335622?through=6000000007273425418
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-76066504 Jesse Woodson]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-76073218 Mary Ann Woodson]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-39068763 Sarah Roberts (Woodson)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-76074722 Jane Bramlett (Woodson)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on June 28, 1756 in Cumberland County, Virginia, British Colonial America and was buried in June 1756 there. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT His name was not "John" Sanburne/Sanburn/Sanbourne just Sanburne/Sanburn/Sanbourne
2 CONT He did not marry Elizabeth Hughes https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Woodson/6000000007273266627
2 CONT
2 CONT Sanburne  (Sanbourne) Woodson was born 11 Sep 1707 in Curles, Virginia to parents Joseph Woodson and his first wife, Mary Sanbourne.  His grandmother, Mary (Tucker) Woodson https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Woodson/6000000013261538
2 CONC 033?through=6000000005966071364, in her will proved 1 Aug 1710 in Henrico county names “my grandson Sanburn, child of my daughter Mary, wife of Joseph Woodson.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Adventures of Purse and Person pg. 719 Sanburne Woodson (Joseph4, John3, John2, John1)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will==
2 CONT 13 Nov 1755 Cumberland County VA Will Book 1 1749–1792 page 115 116 Sanburn Woodson Will
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God amen I Sanburn Woodson of Cumberland County and Parish of Southam being Weak in Body but in perfect Memory Praised be God, do make this my last Will and Testament as follows with Imprimis I give and bequeath in 
2 CONC the following manner and form
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I leave to my loving Wife Charity Woodson during her natural life one hundred and fifty acres of land with the Plantation where I now live, and after her demise to my Son Hughes Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give the remaining part of my Land to my son Hughes Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath to my five Children Hughes Woodson and Sarah Woodson, and Jane Woodson and Jesse Woodson and Maryann Woodson to every and each of them twenty five Pounds Current Money when they come to Lawful age that is 
2 CONC to say to the age of twenty one to be paid by my Executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give and bequeath to Wife Charity Woodson to her and her hand for ever all the rest of my estate Real and Personal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Imprimis I institute and appoint my Loving Wife Charity Woodson my Executrix.   In Witness whereof I hereon set my Hand and Seal the thirteenth Day of November and in the year of our Lord 1755.    Sanburn Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research ==
2 CONT DNA from 2017 has brought changes to the thought of Sarah Shores as a daughter of Sanburne Woodson. The following information was copied from FamilySearch originally posted by Contributor Karen Xaramillo copied from LH88-6JC and L
2 CONC X7Z-1T1:
2 CONT
2 CONT "There has been some suggestion that Sarah Woodson daughter of Sanbourne Woodson is the incorrect Sarah of the Thomas Shores relationship.  If you have any data to prove differently I would love to see it. This would be the forum 
2 CONC  for discussions.... It is possible that Sarah Lloyd might be an alternative choice. Sarah Woodson d/o Sanbourne Woodson appears to have married Olive Branch Roberts and not Thomas Shores. This information would say that Sarah Woo
2 CONC dson daughter of Sanborne Woodson died in 1846. Legacy Sources from Ancestry are not helpful as they remain undocumented. Information on Sarah Lloyd is scarce. We do know that one of Thomas shores descendants named her daughter " 
2 CONC Sarah Lloyd". Autosomal DNA testing of Shores descendants have recently revealed connections to the Woodsons of Fluvanna Virginia and with family connections to the  Cocke family there. The "Shores' of Fluvanna have well documente
2 CONC d history there and are cousins to the Shores of Loudoun Virginia.As such, a much better possibility is that Sarah Woodson is one from that Clan of Woodsons living in the Henrico/ Fluvanna Virginia area.... Josiah Woodson is one o
2 CONC f three brothers that as of today are possible parents for Sarah Woodson wife of  Captain Thomas Shores  of Loudoun Virginia.... As always a work in progress.
2 CONT
2 CONT The reason Sarah Woodson wife of  Captain Thomas Shores has been attached to Josiah Woodson is that recent DNA findings of 2017 has connected the descendants of Thomas and Sarah to the Woodsons of Henrico/ Fluvanna Virginia. These
2 CONC  findings also connect this family as having a relationship to the Cocke family that lived there as well. Captain Thomas Shores is cousin to the Shores Clan in Fluvanna. John Woodson Sr. had several  documented sons that could hav
2 CONC e been Sarah Woodsons father.... and more work is being done to filter it out....Sarah Woodson w/o Capt. Thomas Shores has been placed in many genealogies as the daughter of Sanbourne Woodson. That appears to be incorrect, as the 
2 CONC balance of evidence now shows that the daughter of Sanbourne Woodson was married to another man and died in 1846." 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will he names his five children 
2 CONT # Hughes,  
2 CONT # Sarah,  
2 CONT # Jane,  
2 CONT # Jesse and  
2 CONT # Maryann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charity was the mother of Sarah (Roberts) and probably Jane, Jesse and Maryann. 
2 CONT Per the Family Bible, Sarah dies in 1846 at the age of 99 years, which means she was born 1747.
2 CONT 18 Nov 1746 Goochland Co VA Deed Book 5 page 238 239 Sanburn Woodson to Robert Walton At A Court held 19 May 1747 Charity the Wife of Sanburn Woodson relinquished to right of dower. Looking at the deed book, like the recorder of t
2 CONC he deeds recorded multiple wives relinquishes dower in land after the fact. https://www.familysearch.org/records/images/image-details?page=1&am......
2 CONT See Discussions on the profile(s)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108795250/sanburne-woodson (Bio erroneously calls wife Elizabeth the daughter of Stephen Hughes. Awaiting correction) ~ 9 Oct 2022
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Joseph Woodson in ''Adventurers of Purse and Person'' v 3 4th Ed page 719 No info provided in the book on number 85 Daughter Elizabeth other then their name.  ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000196950004863 docu
2 CONC ment attached]) Woodson pedigree adds son Snag.  Woodson, loc.cit., omits Snag and adds daughter Lucy.
