1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander CUNNINGHAM died in 1779 in Prince Edward County, Virginia. (274) Parents: Alexander CUNNINGHAM and (unknown) BELL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: Judith CUNNINGHAM, William CUNNINGHAM, Josiah CUNNINGHAM, Elizabeth CUNNINGHAM, Susannah CUNNINGHAM, Jacob CUNNINGHAM, Nathanial CUNNINGHAM, John M. CUNNINGHAM, Paul Michaux CUNNINGHAM.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Alexander CUNNINGHAM was born about 1650 in Virginia.(2) He was born in York County, Virginia.(387) Some information taken from "The Mecklenberg Signers and their Neighbors" by Worth, where he notes that: "Alexander Cunningham mov
2 CONC ed to Goochland County with the DANIEL family and where his children intermarried with a French Huguenot family named Michaux. . . "
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/collaborate/LKXY-ZVG cites
2 CONT **HISTORICAL GENEALOGY OF THE WOODSONS AND THEIR CONNECTIONS, By Henry Morton Woodson, Memphis, TN, 1915: pg 34:
2 CONT **Lyman Chalkley ,Chronicles of the Scotch-Irish in Virgina (1745-1800) Baltimore Genealogical Genealogical Pub Co. 1966.  “On Nov.17 1773 David Cunningham and  Ann deeded land to Alexander (Vol III p.536) On November 19, 1774 he 
2 CONC is mentioned along with wife Ann as one of eleven children in Davaid Cunninghams will.(Vol III p. 150)?? On Mar 16 1777 he attested to sale of land(Vol III p. 557). On Mar 19 1782 John Cunningham is referred to as Alexander's admi
2 CONC nistrator (Vol II p 390 Also Vol I p.224) His estate was appraised by Samuel McCutchan, Wat. Cunningham and David Trotter on April 10 1782 in Augusta Co.VA. (Vol III p161)”
2 CONT ** MARRIAGE: from Genealogies of Virginia Families Vol 4
