2 CONT 1750–1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Minter Evans
2 CONT 1753–1830
2 CONT
2 CONT DR. . ELIZABETH MICHAUX MORGAN-MINTER was born circa 1725 in Virginia to Anthony Morgan & Olive Judy Michaux-Morgan. Elizabeth was the GRANDDAUGHTER of the well known Dr. Abraham Michaux & wife Suzanne Rochet-Michaux who escaped p
2 CONC ersecution in France for their "Huguenot" Christian Faith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth's Grandmother, Suzanne Rochet, was "The Little Nightcap" who's story of escaping religious persecution in France after the Edict of Nantes was Revoked, is printed in French in Suzanne's own handwriting in the Michaux Fam
2 CONC ily Bible. The Bible is on display at the Library of Union Theological Seminary, Richmond, VA, (the Bible was published in 1659). "The Little Nightcap" story has been reprinted in English several times in historical publications.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married John Oliver Minter, Sr. in 1743 at Cumberland County, Virginia, and they had EIGHT Children of record:
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Minter-Womack (1744-1840),
2 CONT Anthony Morgan Minter (1747-1807),
2 CONT Phillip Evans Minter (1748-1796),
2 CONT Elizabeth Minter-Burns (1749-1813),
2 CONT Joseph Oliver Minter Sr. (1750-1823),
2 CONT Agnes Minter-Evans (1753-1830),
2 CONT Jane Minter-Riddle (1761-1817), &
2 CONT John Oliver Minter Jr (1762-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth passed away circa 1797 in Chatham County, North Carolina, and was buried in The Minter Family Cemetery on their plantation property located at Haw River Township near the intersection of the Haw & Deep Rivers, in the pro
2 CONC ximity of present day Moncure, Chatham County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT REFERENCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hadley, Wade Hampton, Horton, Doris Goerch, Strowd, Nell Craig, 1976, "Chatham County 1771-1971, Second Edition," Moore Publishing Co: Durham, NC, p.410.
2 CONT John Minter & wife Elizabeth Morgan moved into Chatham County about the time it was organized (1771).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. 29 May 1932, Atlanta Georgia Newspaper, "People Who Think," GENEALOGY DEPARTMENT; Minters, and inter-Married Lines, Were Pioneers in Early Georgia History, by Lilla Odem.
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE:
2 CONT 1. 29 May 1932, Atlanta Georgia Newspaper, "People Who Think," GENEALOGY DEPARTMENT; Minters, and inter-Married Lines, Were Pioneers in Early Georgia History, by Lilla Odem.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Drews, Toby. (1981), "Genealogies of Virginia Families: from The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography," Vol. IV, Healy - Pryor, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc.: Baltimore, MD, p. 363-364.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Fretwell, Shela S., 1988, "Abstracts of the Cumberland County, Virginia, Court Order Books from May 1756 to June 1762, p. 132. (Married before 1760).
2 CONT Court Order Book entry: 27 October 1760, p. 280:
2 CONT "An indenture of release between Anthony Morgan of the first part, John Minter & Elizabeth Minter, his wife, daughter of Anthony Morgan of the second part, Benjamin Clopton and Agness Clopton, his wife, also a daughter of Anthony 
2 CONC Morgan of the third part, and Jacob Michaux eldest son and heir at Law of Abraham Michaux, late of the County of Henrico, deceased, of the fourth and last part. The receipt indorsed are acknowledged by Anthony Morgan, John Minter,
2 CONC  & Benjamin Clopton and recorded. Elizabeth & Agness being first privately examined, also acknowledged the Indenture."
2 CONT
2 CONT CEMETERY:
2 CONT The Minter Cemetery is on the Plantation Property, Haw River Township (proximity of Moncure), Chatham County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Son's Will, Joseph Oliver Minter, Will Bk. B, p. 108, 25 September 1822:
2 CONT "The graveyard where my father and mother's buried with others of the family, which is one eigth of an acre."
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Deed for Estate of Joseph Minter, Deed Bk. AB, p. 401, 4 November 1828:
2 CONT John Farrar, Executor of Joseph Minter's (deceased) Estate to Charles J. Williams, states the meets and bounds of 1005 acres on the North side of the Deep River "with exception of the graveyard which occupies and is limited to one
2 CONC  quarter of an acre."
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Deed from Charles J. Williams to John A. Williams, Deed Bk. AE, p. 464, 31 December 1839:
2 CONT States the meets & bounds for 800 acres on the North side of the Deep River, "with the exception of the graveyard which occupies and is limited to one quarter of an acre."
2 CONT
2 CONT Little Nightcap Story:
2 CONT 1. Written in French in the front of the Michaux family bible, Preserved at the Library of Union Theological Seminary, Richmond, VA.
2 CONT Bible published in 1659.
2 CONT 2. Published in 1888 by Rev. William Dennis Morton, D.D. in the "Central Presbyterian."
2 CONT 3. Republished on April 12, 1916, in "The Presbyterian of the South."
2 CONT 4. Republished in 1981 in "Genealogies of Virginia Families: from The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography," Vol. IV, Genealogical Publishing Co, Inc.: Baltimore, p. 318.
2 CONT
