1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 5 JAN 1743 AND 13 JUL 1753
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Burks II was the son of Samuel Burks and Mary Davis. He was born c.1712 in Albemarle County, Virginia and died before July 1753 in Albemarle County, Virginia. He married Elizabeth (unk) and had eight childre
2 CONC n. He owned land along the Pedlar Creek which was in Albemarle County when he bought it (Albemarle Dd Bk III, p. 219), but later became a part of Amherst County.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Burks II and wife Elizabeth:
2 CONT # George Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/George-Burks/6000000003650200406?through=6000000019763767580
2 CONT # Mary Partree Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Smith/6000000000890005317?through=6000000178532752822
2 CONT # Richard Burks https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Burks/6000000019763888088?through=6000000032891009856
2 CONT # David Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/David-Burke/6000000100246656013?through=6000000178532752822
2 CONT # John Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Burks/6000000032891479719?through=6000000178532752822
2 CONT # Samuel Burks III  https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Burks-III/6000000178532752822
2 CONT # Charles Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Burks/6000000003650288183?through=6000000019763767580
2 CONT # Million “Milley” Burks  https://www.geni.com/people/Milliam-Mitchell/6000000003650258540?through=6000000019763767580
2 CONT # Elizabeth Burks https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Shoemaker/6000000186065801831
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT *http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~harrisonrep/Harrison/d0072/g0000067.html#I12345 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Samuel Burks, Jr., wrote his will on 5 January 1743 and it was presented in Albemarle court on 13 July 1753. Samuel named his wife, Elizabeth, and his nine children:
2 CONT (1) David, a son who was under age 21 in 1743
2 CONT (2) Richard
2 CONT (3) John
2 CONT (4) Charles
2 CONT (5) George
2 CONT (6) Samuel
2 CONT (7) Elizabeth, a daughter under age 21 in 1743
2 CONT (8) Mary Partree, a daughter under age 21 in 1743
2 CONT (9) Million, a daughter under age 21 in 1743
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Samuel Burks
2 CONT
2 CONT IN THE NAME OF GOD AMEN: I Samuel Burk Jr. of Albemarle County being sick and weak, but of perfect mind and memory, thank Almight God for it, do this fifth day of January, One Thousand Seven hundred and forty-three, make constitut
2 CONC e and ordain this my last will and testament in manner and form following to wit:
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath unto my sons '''David Burk''', '''Richard Burk''', '''John Burk''' and '''Charles Burk'''...to be equally divided between my said sons, when David shall attain the age of twenty-one years, my eight hundre
2 CONC d acres of land I hold on Pedler River.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my son '''George Burk'''...one hundred and fifty acres of land I now dwell on.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my son '''Samuel Burk'''...my entry of one hundred acres of land I hold on Tye River.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my daughters, '''Elizabeth Burk'''...'''Mary Partree Burk''' and '''Million Burk''' and to their heirs, when they shall marry or attain twenty-one years, twenty five pounds current money of Virginia to each of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my loving wife Elizabeth and to her heirs forever, fifty acres of land an entry I hold on Watt's Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I lend my said wife so long as she continues my widow and no longer, my negro man Adam and all the rest of my estate real and personal for the maintenance and bringing up of my children but in case my wife Elizabeth should m
2 CONC arry or when she departs this life then...all my estate lent her shall be equally divided between all my children before mentioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT My will is that my estate shall not be appraised. I do nominate...my wife, Elizabeth Burk and David Mims Executors...Samuel (X) mark Burk, Jr. (seal) Signed, sealed, published and declared this above writing to be his last will an
2 CONC d testament, in the presence of us: Wm. Meggenson, James Freeland Jr., James Spears, William Howle-(by his mark)
2 CONT
2 CONT "At a court held for Albemarle County the thirteenth day of July, 1753 this last will...of Samuel Burk deceased was presented...on the motion of Elizabeth Burks one of the Exeutors...on which she with William Meggenson and William
2 CONC  Cabell her securities...acknowledged their bond for...execution of the said will. 
2 CONT This will further proved in March 1754. Teste: John Nicholas, Clerk
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
