1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children of ELIZABETH ADAMS and ACHILLES MOORMAN are:
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. WILLIAM MOORMAN, b. 1746; d. January 25, 1829; m. JUDITH VENABLE.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A080096  DAR Ancestor # A080096]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to his Last Will and Testatment, owned a plantation in Breckenridge County, KY with many slaves. Also owned horses, cattle, sheep, hogs, furniture, farm tools, cows and calves.  Owned slaves by the following names: David
2 CONC , Dan, George, Jacob, Washington, Betty, Sooky, Rebekah, Milley, Eliza, Isaac, Carolina, Burrell, Fanny, Nat, Zarilda, Lucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 3 times.  1st wife: Jane Haden.  2nd wife: Judith Venable.  3rd wife: Elizabeth Miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Jane, Hugh Lewis, Ann Nancy, Lucretia, Jesse V., Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
