2 CONT
2 CONT Carrington enlisted as a Private on 22 July 1861 at Abingdon. He was a member of Company H in the 37th Regiment of Virginia Infantry. The Presbyterian was promoted to Chaplain. The son of Paul and Emma Cabell Carrington apparently
2 CONC  also served in the First Virginia Cavalry, but no record was found. Carrington was a lawyer before becoming a minister. He held the pastorate at Greenwich from 1883 to 1889.
