1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Judge Asa Dickinson Watkins'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asa_D._Watkins
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/115295916/asa-dickinson-watkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia State Senator Asa Watkins was a native of Prince Edward and resident of Farmville. He married Nannie Elizabeth Forbes in 1886. Judge Watkins came from a long line of distinguished men. His father was a Judge. He grandfath
2 CONC er was aptly termed one of the most impressive men in Virginia. These Watkins, the first in Virginia, came from Wales in the 17th century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This Watkins received his early education at public school in Farmville, then attended nearby Hampden-Sydney. He went on to study law at the University of Virginia. He commenced practice in Farmville. Among the offices he held for
2 CONC  his community are deputy clerk of the court, deputy treasurer, deputy sheriff, Commonwealth Attorney, and judge. He did much to improve the training of teachers in Farmville. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Democrat and Presbyterian.
