1 NOTE {geni:about_me} July 6. - Mrs. Delia Kingsbury Venable, widow of Col. T. B. Benable, died in New York Wednesday, July 3rd, st the advanced age of 284 years. She left one daughter, Mrs. T. R. Southerland, at whose home she died, al
2 CONC so one sister, Mrs. Florence Pugh, and two grandchildren, who aecompanied the remains to Oxford. burial was in Oxford in Elmwood eemetery, where she was laid to rest by the side of her husband. The deceased was a member of the Pre
2 CONC sbyterian church. The Mrs. Venable was well known in Raleigh, where she resided a number of years. Her home in Oxford will long be remembered for her genuine hospitality.
