3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John B. Hollis served in the Union Army, Co. B., 2 Tennessee Mounted Infantry, Sergeant.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bell was reassigned to the 12th Union Cavalry at a rank of 1st Lieutenant. He commanded a company which served in a guerrilla capacity harassing Confederate troops. The Lawrence County Historical Society records an incident w
2 CONC hen Lt. Hollis led his men on a mission to free Union prisoners being held in the jail at Lawrenceburg. The jail was burned, but Lt. Hollis and several of his men werre captured. Since they were southerners in Union uniforms, they
2 CONC  were tried as traitors and sentenced to be executed. They were taken to Pine Bluff just west of Lawrenceburg the night before their scheduled execution. Lt Hollis and his men somehow got their sentries engaged in a drinking bout,
2 CONC  and when the guards were sufficeiently drunk, all the prisoners escaped.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT John B. Hollis
2 CONT The Lawrence Democrat 31 Jan 1917
2 CONT On January 4, 1917, John B. Hollis, aged 73 years, 4 months and 7 days answered the call to another world. As a gentleman, citizen and farmer he stood among the very best in the county. He was wise in council, calm in judgment, an
2 CONC d faithful to the discharge of all duties.
2 CONT He fought for the Union during the dark days of the Civil War as 1st. Lieutenant in the 2nd. Tennessee, and lived and died devoted to the same principles.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21016018/john-bell-hollis Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 11 2023, 16:38:58 UTC''
