1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Father of James Venable Crute. Husband of Louisa Vaughan Crute.
2 CONT
2 CONT Venable Crute 
2 CONT Birth: 1800 in Mecklenburg Co.,VA 
2 CONT Death: OCT 1880 in Mecklenburg Co,VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John Lampkin Crute b: 1 MAY 1756 in Northumberland Co.,VA 
2 CONT Mother: Rebeckah Smith b: in Nottoway Parish,Amelia Co.,VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Louisa V. Vaughn b: 1814 in VA
2 CONT Married: 25 SEP 1833 in Mecklenburg Co.,VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #  Samuel V. Crute b: 1835
2 CONT #  John L. Crute b: 1837
2 CONT #  Martha W. Crute b: 1839 in Prince Edward Co.,VA
2 CONT #  Anna Eliza Crute b: 16 MAR 1840 in Mecklenburg,VA
2 CONT #  James Venable Crute b: 2 NOV 1843 in Mecklenburg Co.,VA
2 CONT #  Matilda C. Crute b: 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT The Farrier family sold this cemetery land to Venable Crute, who willed it to his son James Venable Crute, who in turn left it by will to his son James E. Crute.
2 CONT
2 CONT DESCRIPTION:
2 CONT
2 CONT This cemetery is well kept and enclosed by a wire fence.  There are many graves 
2 CONT that have been here for more than a century, yet only one has a marker.
2 CONT
2 CONT HISTORICAL SIGNIFICANCE:
2 CONT
2 CONT This cemetery was started by the Farrier family, who settled near Boydton very early and built up quite extensively near Boydton and later sold to Mr. Venable 
2 CONT Crute.
2 CONT
2 CONT The inscription on the one visible tombstone is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT In memory of
2 CONT Elizabeth H. Cobbs
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Cobbs
2 CONT of the city of Raleigh, N.C.
2 CONT who departed this life
2 CONT on the 14th day of September 1821
2 CONT in the 32nd year of her age
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/36535395/venable-crute Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 17 2022, 14:04:45 UTC''
2 CONT
