1 TITL Capt. (CSA)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Enlisted as a 1st Sergeant in Captain William H. Easley's Company of Cavalry (Black Walnut Dragoons)
2 CONT
2 CONT July 1863 signs as 1st Lieutenant commanding company.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wounded 24 May 1864
2 CONT
2 CONT Promoted 12 Dec 1864 to Captain
2 CONT
2 CONT The 3rd Regiment, Virginia Cavalry was organized with independent companies and entered Confederate service on July 1, 1861. The regiment was formed with eleven companies, later reduced to ten. It was also called 2nd Regiment unti
2 CONC l October 1861. It surrendered on April 9, 1865. The commanders were Colonels Thomas F. Goode, Robert Johnston, and Thomas H. Owen; Lieutenant Colonels William R. Carter, William M. Feild, and John I Thornton; and Majors Henry Car
2 CONC rington and Jefferson C. Phillips.
2 CONT
2 CONT Company H (Catawba Troop) - many men from Halifax County
2 CONT
2 CONT No. 117. Report of Colonel Thomas H. Owen, Third Virginia Cavalry, commanding Wickham's brigade. HEADQUARTERS WICKHAM'S CAVALRY BRIGADE, October 25, 1863. MAJOR: I have the honor to make the following report of the part taken by W
2 CONC ickham's brigade in the late movement toward Manassas: ... Lieutenant Clement Carrington, of the Third Virginia Cavalry, who acted as aide-de-camp, deserves credit also for coolness and gallantry in the discharge of his duties. In
2 CONC  conclusion, I am happy to be able to say that the casualties in battle were moderately few, compared with those of the enemy (and the number of prisoners, horses, and equipments, carbines, pistols, sabers, &c., captured). My loss
2 CONC  being as follows: Killed, 17; wounded, 129 (4 mortally); missing, 8. All of which is respectfully submitted. THOS. H. OWEN, Colonel, Commanding Wickham's Brigade* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/114486230/clement-
2 CONC carrington Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 13 2020, 3:55:11 UTC''
