1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hugh Blair Grigsby, the historian, was the most talented literary to ever live in Charlotte County.  He was born in Norfolk, Virginia, in 1806 and did not move to Charlotte until 1840. November 19, 1840, Hugh marri
2 CONC ed Mary Venable Carrington, daughter of Colonel Clement Carrington of "Edgehill."
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended Yale College from 1824 to 1826 and studied law.  In 1829 he passed the bar, but due to deafness he was never able to pursue his profession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Instead, he became a prolific writer and history is indebted to him for his contributions.  His best works were those written on the Virginia Convention of 1776, 1788 and 1829-1830, which depict the outstanding men and events of t
2 CONC he Commonwealth between 1770 and 1850.  As a member of the 1829-1830 convention from Norfolk he wrote first hand sketches of its participants.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was very interested in education and in 1871 was elected third Chancellor of the College of William and Mary.  He held this position until his death in 1881 at "Edgehill."
2 CONT
2 CONT A few days before his decease he was heard to say, "I desire to live, yet I feel submissive to the Divine will." An offering from his friend, the Honorable Robert C. Winthrop of Massachusetts, a box of exquisite white flowers reac
2 CONC hed him in his last moments, and served to decorate his grave. His remains rest beneath a chaste and stately marble obelisk; erected by his widow, in Elmwood cemetery, Norfolk, VA., it bears the following inscription: "HUGH BLAIR,
2 CONC  LL.D. Born Norfolk, VA. "November 28, 1806; Died at "Edgehill" Charlotte County, VA., April 28, 1881. President of the Virginia Historical Society; Member of the Virginia Convention; 1829-30; Chancellor of the College of William 
2 CONC and Mary" A biographical sketch of Hugh Blair Grigsby can be found in the "Virginia Historical Collections" volume ix.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/74007478/hugh-blair-grigsby Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 3 2021, 17:33:09 UTC''
