1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA with the rank of LIEUTENANT COLONEL.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A134964  DAR Ancestor # A134964]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Daniel Wilson & Martha Branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT * 1)  ELIZABETH FINNEY  
2 CONT * 2)  JUDITH FRIEND  
2 CONT * 3)  PURIFEE BARRETT  
2 CONT * 4)  SARAH WALTHALL
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *The descendants of Captain Thomas Friend, 1700-1760, Chesterfield County, Virginia [https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/13669/dvm_GenMono002404-00002-1?backurl=&ssrc=&backlabel=Return#?imageId=dvm_GenMono002404-00012-0 AncestryI
2 CONC mage] Page 137 [https://archive.org/details/descendantsofcap00frie/page/137 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !BIRTH-MARRIAGE: GREGORY ANCESTRY Chart by Martha Gregory O'Brien (from DuBose)
2 CONT DESCENDANTS OF CAPT. THOMAS FRIEND 1700-1760, Chesterfield, VA, p.137
2 CONT Pedigree charts from Meriwether Hurt to Katherine Stokes Hart, January 2015
2 CONT e-mails from Kathy Emmel, 2/13/13; JMSHowe to Kathy on 2/14/13
2 CONT MARRIAGE: "The Walthall Family - A Genealogical History of the Descendants of William Walthall of Virginia" by Malcolm Elmore Walthall, 1952, pub. C. D. Walthall, 1963, p. 26.
2 CONT CHILDREN: Willson paper by Sallie JACKSON Stokes (from Judy S. Barnes) p2
2 CONT DEATH:  Will of Thomas Branch Willson, written 16 Nov 1800, proved 25 Dec 1800
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Branch Willson of Amelia Co., VA  was born 21 Oct 1730 (Meriwether lists b. 21 Oct 1739; "Desc. of Capt T.F.," p. 137 says b.1730), the son of Daniel Willson and Martha BRANCH Willson of Henrico Co., VA.
2 CONT Thomas Branch Willson married (1) Elizabeth Finnie on 28 Feb 1760, in Amelia Co., VA.  They had children:
2 CONT Daniel Willson m Elizabeth Anderson
2 CONT Lucy Willson (born 1762) m 1781 William Gray
2 CONT Rebecca Willson (born 1765) m Mr. Gray
2 CONT (one of these Grays lived at UVA; Brockenbroughs descended from)
2 CONT
2 CONT After his first wife's death, Thomas Branch Willson married (2) on 2 Dec 1774, Judith Friend (daughter of Capt. Thomas Friend and Frances Cox) of Chesterfield Co., VA.  They had one son:
2 CONT Thomas Friend Willson (born 1775) m Ann "Nancy" Anderson
2 CONT After his second wife died about 1776, Thomas Branch Willson married (3) on 27 Nov 1777, Purifer/Purifee (Purefoy) BARRETT Booker.  They had one daughter:
2 CONT Purifer Barrett Willson (born 1779) m Charles Broadfoot
2 CONT Thomas Branch Willson married 4th, Sarah Walthall (re: Kathy Emmel's e-mail, 2/13/13).
2 CONT
2 CONT *************
2 CONT Thomas Branch Willson was appointed Major of 1st Battalion of Amelia County Militia on 23 Oct 1777 and Lt. Col. of the First Battalion of Amelia Co., VA Militia on 23 April 1778 (Order Book 1776-1780, Amelia Co., p. 75 and 119).  
2 CONC He was appointed Colonel on 28 May 1778 (re: Kathy Emmel's e-mail 2/13/13).
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` ` ``
2 CONT E-mail from Kathy Emmel, 11 Feb 2013:
2 CONT "I originally joned the DAR under my Grandma Mattie's number and ancestor (Lt. Col. Thomas Branch Wil[l]son).  But I have since found two supplemental ancestors:  Roger Gregory (who provided beef to the troops) and Col. Nathanial 
2 CONC Wilkinson (who served in the VA House of Delegares from 1768-1795). . . . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT ...on the DAR website, Thomas Branch Wil[l]son has his rank listed as Lieutenant Colonel. I also looked through the DAR Lineage Book (printed in 1913!) and there are a number of members who list him as Lt. Col. and he is their anc
2 CONC estor also. So I think the DAR website is where I originally saw his title listed.
2 CONT
2 CONT I can't find anything that might prove that George Cox or Daniel Willson (born in 1761) were involved with the Revolutionary War effort. I think they would have been about 16-20 years old at the time of the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Well - here's some really good news! I went back into the DAR website and checked Daniel Willson again and there he was! Already in the database. This Daniel is actually the one who was married to Martha Branch and was the father 
2 CONC of Thomas Branch Wil[l]son. (Not Daniel, the son of Thomas Branch Wilson, born in 1761) I bought the paperwork of the original DAR member on the DAR website so I'll have to work out the geneology. But I'm sure he is in my line! So
2 CONC  now I have found three supplementals (how fun! I can buy a pin - I think they look like feathers - with the names engraved on them. Well, I can buy them after I submit the paperwork and prove the link!)
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `
2 CONT Kathy Emmel e-mailed 2/13/13:
2 CONT I just noticed that Thomas Branch Wil[l]son's 4th wife was named Sarah Walthall, and George Cox (the son of George Cox married to Mary Batte) was named Mary Walthal Friend!  I wonder how that fits together?!
2 CONT By the way, the four wives were listed in the DAR database."
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` ` `
2 CONT From: "jenniehowe2@cox.net" <jenniehowe2@cox.net> 
2 CONT To: "Emmel, Kathy" <Kathyemmel@yahoo.com> 
2 CONT Sent: Wednesday, December 9, 2015 11:49 AM 
2 CONT Subject: Willson wills you attached in your last e-mail 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Kathy, 
2 CONT I just want to be Sure I have the right wills for the correct Willsons: 
2 CONT The Amelia Court record 25 Dec 1800 is the will of Lt. Col. Thomas Branch 
2 CONT Willson (born 1730, died Nov-Dec 1800). 
2 CONT His fourth wife was Sarah Walthall (married1782).  Since she's not mentioned in 
2 CONT his will, she must have died before 1800? 
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the estate settlement debts, etc. listed in Amelia August Court 1829 are 
2 CONT for Daniel Willson (1761-Oct 1816) who married Elizabeth Anderson.  This Daniel 
2 CONT is the son of the above Thomas Branch Willson and first wife Elizabeth 
2 CONT Finnie.  Right? 
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` ` `
2 CONT Date: Wed, 9 Dec 2015 20:04:33 +0000 (UTC)
2 CONT From: Kathy Emmel <kathyemmel@yahoo.com>
2 CONT To: "jenniehowe2@cox.net" <jenniehowe2@cox.net>
2 CONT Subject: Re: Willson wills you attached in your last e-mail
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Jennie - yes, you are correct on everything! Interesting that the settlement debts happen so long after Daniel Wilson died in 1816. I don't see any wives mentioned in Thomas's will - he must have outlived them all! (Or wore the
2 CONC m out!)
2 CONT Kathy
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` ` ` ` `
2 CONT (e-mail from Kathy Emmel, 7 Dec 2015; typed by JMSHowe, 15 Dec 2015):
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Thomas Branch Willson (21 Oct 1730 - Nov/Dec 1800)
2 CONT married 1st in 1760 Elizabeth Finnie; 2nd in 1774 Judith Friend; 3rd Purifee (Barrett) Booker; 4th in 1782 Sarah Walthall
2 CONT wrote will 16 Nov 1800; will proved 25 Dec 1800
2 CONT Amelia Co., VA Will Book 6, pages160-161
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen.  I Tom Branch Willson of 
2 CONT Amelia County being weak in body but in perfect mind &
2 CONT memory do make and ordain this to be my last Will & Testament
2 CONT in manner and form as follows. (viz.)  Imprimis  I give and be-
2 CONT queath unto my son Daniel Willson all the land I am now 
2 CONT possessed of and on Which I now live also a Negroe Man
2 CONT named Johnny and a Negro wench named Doll and one 
2 CONT Waggon and Guns, One large Walnut Table and one Dozen of
2 CONT Oak split bottom Chairs unto him and his Heirs forever.
2 CONT Item  I give and bequeath to my son Friend Willson one Black
2 CONT Walnut Desk, also six black Walnut Chairs and one arm Chair
2 CONT ditto and a feather Bed and Furniture to him and heirs forever.
2 CONT Item  I give and bequeath to my daughter Purifee Barrott Booker
2 CONT Broadfoot all the residue of my Walnut Chairs to her & to her Heirs
2 CONT forever.  It is further my Will and desire that I give to Sally Kinge
2 CONT one sorrel Mare one Trunk, one pair of Sheets and one pair of Blankets
2 CONT and one Small Dressing Table to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT Also, It is my Will and desire that after my just debts are
2 CONT paid that the residue of my personal Estate be equally divi-
2 CONT ded between my son Daniel Willson, my daughters, Lucy Gray,
2 CONT Rebecca Gray and Purifer Barrott Booker Broadfoot and to
2 CONT them and Their Heirs forever.  It is my particular will
2 CONT and desire my Estate may not be appraised nor any Inventory
2 CONT taken thereof.  And Lastly I ordain constitute and appoint
2 CONT my son Daniel Willson Executor of this my Last Will and Testament
2 CONT revoking and disannuling all former Will and Wills heretofore
2 CONT by me made and ratifying and confirming this to be my
2 CONT Last Will & testament. In Witness whereof I have here-
2 CONT unto affixed My hand and seal this sixteenth day of
2 CONT of November one thousand eight Hundred
2 CONT Signed sealed published and declared by
2 CONT the Testator to be his Last Will & Testa-
2 CONT ment in presence of 
2 CONT J. W. Hewlings
2 CONT Philips Dunnavant Jr.
2 CONT John (his X mark) Sadler
2 CONT Wm. Warriner
2 CONT John Clark
2 CONT John Hollaway
2 CONT John Pride Jr [Sr?]
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` `
2 CONT December 25th 1800
2 CONT At a court held for Amelia County the day of De
2 CONT cember 1800.  This Last Will and Testament of Tom
2 CONT B. Willson deceased was exhibited into Court and
2 CONT proved by the oaths of Philip Dunnovant Jr., John Hal-
2 CONT loway and J. W. Hewlings  three of the witnesses there-
2 CONT to sworn to by Daniel Willson the Exor therein named 
2 CONT and ordered to be recorded.  And on the motion of the
2 CONT said Daniel who entered into and acknowledged Bond 
2 CONT together with Claiborne Anderson, Peter Jones (P) and John
2 CONT Wily his securities in the penalty Twenty five thousand
2 CONT Dollars as the Law directs  Certificate is granted him
2 CONT for obtaining a probate thereof in due Form.
2 CONT Test - 
2 CONT James Townes CofC
2 CONT
2 CONT ` ` ` `
