2 CONT Orange County was created by act of assembly August 1734, from the westernmost portion of Spotsylvania County.  This act was directed to take effect on January 1, 1734/5 and the boundaries of the new county of Orange were defined 
2 CONC as "all that territory of land adjoining to, and above the said line [i.e. the line as established by act of May, 1730, dividing St. George's Parish, Spotsylvania into two parishes to be known as St. George's and St. Mark's; St. M
2 CONC ark's being above the said line, or to the west thereof.  Henning IV., 305] bounden southerly, by the line of Hanover county, northerly, by the grant to the Lord
2 CONT
