1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA  with the rank of CAPTAIN.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A067954  DAR Ancestor #  A067954]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Mar 19 1730 - Rocky Spring, Goochland Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Sep 21 1795 - Rocky Spring, Goochland Co., VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Walter Leake, Judith Leake (born Mask) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Mary Christian (born Leake), John Leake, William Leake, Christian Johnson (born Leake), Elizabeth Coleman (born Leake), Samuel Leake, Mask Leake, Elisha Leake, Judith Christian (born Leake) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Nancy Anne Leake (born Minter) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Anne Leake (born Fenton) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Anne Leake (born Foster) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Lucy Jones (born Leake), Judith Woodson (born Leake), Susannah Leake, Walter Leake, Josiah Leake, John Mask Leake, Christian Scruggs (born Leake), Samuel D. Leake 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Josiah inherited the old goochland homestead of his father Walter Leake. Josiah's will was probated in Goochland County in 1795 and is recorded in the Goochland County Will Book 16, at p. 475. Josiah served as a captain of the loc
2 CONC al militai in the Revolutionary War. He was eventually promoted to this rank in July 1777, according to 'McAlister's Virginia Militai in the Revolutionary War'. In addition to his marriage to Ann Fenton, various sources indicate t
2 CONC hat he may have married at least two other times. It is believed that he is buried in the Leake Cemetery located in Goochland County, Virginia. -http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/v/a/l/Kathy-Valeu/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0290.ht
2 CONC ml Josiah T. Leake was the son of Walter Leake and Judith (Mask) Leake.  He was married three times and had children by all three wives.  His first wife was Ann (Fenton) Leake, by whom he had Lucy (Leake) Jones, Judith (Leake) Woo
2 CONC dson, and Susannah (Leake) Leake.  His second wife was Ann (Minter) Leake, by whom he had Walter Leake and Josiah Leake II.  His third wife was Mrs. Ann Foster, by whom he had John Mask Leake, Christian (Leake) Scruggs, and Samuel
2 CONC  D. Leake.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=5752315 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2016, 6:32:12 UTC''
2 CONT
