1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gay Leake Pendleton Simmons FORT WORTH - Gay Leake Pendleton Simmons, 73, a loving wife, mother, grandmother and sister, died Saturday, June 2, 2001, in Fort Worth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside service: 11 a.m. Wednesday at Greenwood Memorial Park. The Rev. Michael Fry of St. Andrews Episcopal Church will officiate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials: May be made to Cook Fort Worth Children's Medical Center or to Vitas Hospice through All Saints Hospital. The family wishes to extend their deep and sincere appreciation to the staff of Vitas Hospice for their kind hear
2 CONC ts and gentle hands while Gay was in their care.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gay Leake Pendleton Simmons was born Jan. 5, 1928, in Fort Worth. She was a member of St. Andrews Episcopal Church, the Junior League of Fort Worth, the Assembly, the Fort Worth Dental Auxiliary, the Fort Worth Lecture Foundation 
2 CONC and Ray Reimers Bible class.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is preceded in death by her husband, Dr. James H. Simmons, in 1983, and her son, James Hunter Simmons, in 1960.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: Sister, Jane Pendleton Stephens of Wichita Falls; daughter, Gay Simmons Holsapple and husband, Rex, of Lincoln, Neb.; sons, Thomas Pendleton Simmons and wife, Cerelle, of Aledo and James Hampton Simmons Jr. and wife, Er
2 CONC icka, of Ashland, Ore.; grandchildren, Ariel Simmons, Laurel Simmons, Hunter Simmons, Jane Holsapple and Emily Holsapple; and a host of other relatives and many friends all who loved her dearly. Greenwood Funeral Home 3100 White S
2 CONC ettlement Road, (817) 336-0584 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Greenwood Memorial Park and Mausoleum  Fort Worth Tarrant County Texas, USA 
