1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Wilson Miles Cary (CSA)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7170604/wilson_miles-cary
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Lucious and Lucy Cary. His widowed mother brought him to Virginia as an infant. Wilson Miles Cary attended William and Mary College. While a student, he enlisted in Company C of the Thirty-second Virginia Infantry, serv
2 CONC ing until the surrender at Appomattox. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He returned to college and received an appointment as a civil engineer. He became a well-known merchant in Richmond. He was a deacon at the Second Presbyterian Church and a member of the Westmoreland Club. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife, Anne Elizabeth Sublett was born 24 July 1846 and died 14 October 1875. Two of their children were Hunsdon, an attorney and Emily who married Thomas Marshall, Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to his second wife, Lilias Blair McPhail for 31 years. She was born 28 August 1852 and died 24 August 1936. Three of their children were Lucius Falkland, Emily Samson and Lilias Blair.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Wilsom Miles Cary
2 CONT Birth Place	Mississippi
2 CONT Enlistment Date	28 Feb 1861
2 CONT Enlistment Place	Williamsburg, Virginia
2 CONT Enlistment Rank	Comm Sergt
2 CONT Muster Date	28 Feb 1861
2 CONT Muster Place	Virginia
2 CONT Muster Company	C
2 CONT Muster Regiment	32nd Infantry
2 CONT Muster Regiment Type	Infantry
2 CONT Muster Information	Enlisted
2 CONT Rank Change Date	28 Feb 1862
2 CONT Rank Change Rank	4th Corporal
2 CONT Muster Out Date	8 Apr 1865
2 CONT Muster Out Place	Appomattox Court House, Virginia
2 CONT Muster Out Information	Surrendered
2 CONT Side of War	Confederacy
2 CONT Survived War?	Yes
2 CONT Notes 1862-12-20 Detailed, Hospital Duty; 1863-11-01 On rolls; 1864-12-21 Detailed, (Quartermaster Department)
2 CONT Additional Notes 2 Rank Change 2 Date: 30 Jun 1862; Rank Change 2 Rank: Private
2 CONT Title	The Virginia Regimental Histories Series
