2 CONT 448. Edward Lindsay 1 was born 2 BETWEEN 1574 AND 1606 in England. He died 3 in 1677 in At Sea. [Parents]
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: [Br?derbund WFT Vol. 5, Ed. 1, Tree #2180, Date of Import: Apr 29, 1999]
2 CONT Edward Lindsay came from England to Avalon, Newfoundland in 1627 with George Calvert, who was Lord Baltimore and Secretary of State under King James I. He went with Calvert to Jamestown, Virginia, in 1629, and then returned to Eng
2 CONC land until 1632, when he came to Maryland. He lived near Port Tobacco in Charles Co., Maryland.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: He was a sea captain sailing between England, the West Indies, and Maryland. He was lost at sea in 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Child]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 464. Edward Dorsey 1 was born 2 BETWEEN 1605 AND 1639 in England. He died 3 BETWEEN 1666 AND 1722. Edward married 4 Ann Howard BETWEEN 1630 AND 1676 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: [Br?derbund WFT Vol. 5, Ed. 1, Tree #2180, Date of Import: Apr 29, 1999]
2 CONT Edward Dorsey or Darcy was descended from Norman d'Areci, who came to England with William the Conqueror. (Eudora L. South, "Cousin Vachel")
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Edward Dorsey lived with his wife in Norfolk Co., Virginia, in 1642, having come from England sometime earlier. He came to Maryland with Robert Bullen in 1661. He was prominent in early colonial affairs.
2 CONT (KG Lindsay, "Grandpas, Inlaws & Outlaws")
2 CONT
2 CONT 465. Ann Howard 1 was born 2 BETWEEN 1613 AND 1640. She died 3 BETWEEN 1667 AND 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: [Br?derbund WFT Vol. 5, Ed. 1, Tree #2180, Date of Import: Apr 29, 1999]
2 CONT Ann Howard was descended from the Duke of Norfolk.
2 CONT (KG Lindsay, "Grandpas, Inlaws & Outlaws")
2 CONT
