2 CONT Dear Ms Martin
2 CONT
2 CONT I have checked in Joseph Foster's 'Alumni Oxonienses, 1500-1714', a printed
2 CONT register of all those who matriculated (were formally admitted to the
2 CONT University) between those years. There was an entry for a John Woodeson
2 CONT (Woodsonne) which is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Woodeson, John (Woodsonne), of Bristol, gent. He matriculated from St John's
2 CONT College on 1 March, 1604-5, aged 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT He does not seem to have graduated and it is unlikely that we would have any
2 CONT further information regarding John Woodeson in the University Archives. If you
2 CONT would like further information about his time at the College, I suggest you
2 CONT contact St John's as they hold their own records. The Archivist at St John's
2 CONT is Dr Malcolm Vale who can be contacted on 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yours sincerely
2 CONT
2 CONT Jennifer Birnie
2 CONT Archives Assistant
