1 TITL Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Lewis''' was born abt 1660 in Henrico Co., Va. or possibly Wales. He married Elizabeth Woodson c1680-90 in Henrico County, Va. He is found in the Henrico County records settling the estate of his father,
2 CONC  as well as purchasing land during this time. While no record is found of his marriage, it is proven by a settlement of land on William's sons, Joseph and William, by Robert Woodson, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this settlement the boys are listed as Robert's grandsons. William also appears as a witness at one of the first Quaker weddings in Henrico County. His will can be found in the Henrico County records. It was an oral will witnes
2 CONC sed by his brother-in-law, George Payne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://lewis-genealogy.org/genealogy/Lewis/Henrico.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT William Lewis married Elizabeth Woodson.  They were the parents of Joseph Lewis of Henrico Co VA who married Elizabeth Pleasants
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Executor for his father's will and guardian of his sister Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Elizabeth Woodson. His sister Sarah married Robert Woodson, Jr,, Elizabeth Woodson's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrico County Will Book - Will of William Lewis (oral will) 24 Dec 1706
2 CONT >To two sons William and Joseph Lewis, 200 acres at Three Runs, with a parcel on White Oak Swamp and Deep Run, to be divided
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
