1 NOTE Taken from an old Scrapbook, ca 1890, "Kentucky Genealogy From The Long
2 CONT Ago, " Kentucky Explorer, Volume 10, Number 6, November, 1995, p. 99. By
2 CONT permission. Mason County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Moss was commissioned Captain of militia in Goochland County, in
2 CONT 1760 and Major in 1770. He served in the Revolutionary War and died in
2 CONT 1780 from the effects of wounds received in battle. He was married by the
2 CONT Rev. John Clay (father of Henry) to Jane Ford, daughter of Thomas and
2 CONT Katurah Wynne Ford. His father, James Moss, came from England about 1719
2 CONT to Va., where he married Elizabeth Henderson, whose ancestors came from
2 CONT Scotland. Maj. Moss was the father of Dr. James W. Moss and Katurah L.
2 CONT Moss who married Gen. Jas. Taylor of Kentucky. Dr. James W. Moss, of
2 CONT Goochland, married Mary, daughter of Josiah Woodson, of Dover, Goochland
2 CONT Co., Va., a Major in the Revolutionary Army, and removed to Maysville, Ky.
2 CONT about 1804 and died in 1817; by his wife, Elizabeth Woodson, member of the
2 CONT House of Burgesses from Goochland; by his wife Dorothea Randolph (married
2 CONT Oct. 28, 1751), the sister of Susanna Randolph who married Carter H.
2 CONT Harrison and aunt to Thomas Jefferson. She died Jan. 18, 1790. He was a
2 CONT son of Josiah Woodson, who died in 1736 (by his wife, Mary Royal), son of
2 CONT John Woodson, of Curles in Henrico, (by his wife Judith Tarleton, a
2 CONT daughter of Steven Taarleton, who died in 1687), eldest son of Robert
2 CONT Woodson, son of Dr. John Woodson, who emigrated from Dorsetshire, England,
2 CONT prior to 1629.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Virginia Genealogist, Vol. 20, 1976.
2 CONT Genealogies of Virginia Families, From the William and Mary Quarterly Historical Magazine, Volume V, Thompson-Yates (and Appendix), Baltimore, Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc, 1982.
2 CONT Goochland Historical Society Magazaine, Spring 1975.
2 CONT Notes on Peter Field Trent, LDS Film # 6019060.
2 CONT Louise Goode Shannon, The House of Goode, (Dogwood Printing, P.O. Box 716, Ozark Mo. 65721, 1997).
2 CONT "Marriages of Some Virginia Residents 1607-1800" Dorothy Ford Wulfeck Vol II, Genealogical Publishing Co. Inc, Baltimore, 1986
