1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 2-591
1 NOTE She lived twenty-five years longer than her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEED BETWEEN JUDITH COX & WILLIAM WATSON
2 CONT CUMBERLAND CO., VA 1759
2 CONT DEED BK 2, PAGES484,485
2 CONT
2 CONT THIS INDENTURE made this twenty eighth Day of May in the Year of our lord Christ One Thousand seven hundred and fifty nine Between Judith Cox Executrix of the Last Will and Testament of Stephen Cox dec'd and William Watson Witnefs
2 CONC eth that the said Judith Cox for and in Consideration of the sum of Fifty Pounds to her in hand paid the Receipt whereof she doth hereby Acknowledge and thereof and Livery part thereof doth Acquit and discharge the said William do
2 CONC th Bargain and Sell and y these Presents doth bargain and sell unto the said William one Tract or Parcel of Land containing by Estimation four hundred acres more or less To have & to hold the aforesaid Land with its Appurtenances 
2 CONC unto the said William his Heirs and Afsigns To the only use and behoof of him the said William his Heirs and Afsigns forever which aforesaid  Land and Premises lying and being in the County of Cumberland granted to Stephen Cox and
2 CONC  Bounded as follows Beginning at a White Oak thence new lines to a white Oak in William Kents line North two hundred and twenty eight Poles to pointers thence West thirty one Poles to a Black Oak Thence South two hundred and eight
2 CONC y nine Poles to Pointers and on William's line the same Course one hundred and ninety one Poles to the first Station which Lands and Premises the said Judith doth hereby Warrant and Defend as Executrix aforesaid unto the said Will
2 CONC iam and his Heirs by these presents In Witnefs whereof the said Judith hath hereunto set her hand and Seal this twenty eighth day of May One thousand seven hundred and fifty nine.
2 CONT Singed Sealed & Delivered 
2 CONT In Presence of 
2 CONT Warren Walker
2 CONT Josiah Cox
2 CONT MEMORANDUM that on the Day and Year within mentioned Quiet and Peaceable Possession of the within Lands and Premises were Delivered by the said Judith unto the aforesaid William
2 CONT                                                                                                         Judith Cox
2 CONT Warren Walker
2 CONT Rec'd of the within mentioned William Fifty Pounds the Consideration 
2 CONT Money within mentioned this 20th May 1759
2 CONT Warren Walker                                                                                  Judith Cox
2 CONT At a Court held for Cumberland County the 20th Day of May 1759 this Indenture with the Memorandum of Livery and Seizen & Receipt Indorsed were acknowledged by Judith Cox & party thereto and by the Court ordered to be Recorded
2 CONT                                                            Teste Thompson Swann Clk
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL OF JUDITH COX
2 CONT CUMBERLAND CO., VA
2 CONT WILL BK 2, PG156
2 CONT
2 CONT IN THE NAME OF GOD AMEN I Judith Cox of Cumberland County do make & Ordain this my last will & Testament in manner & form following Imprimes I recommend my Soul to Almighty God that gave it & my body to the earth to be decently bu
2 CONC ried at the discretion of my Executor I do appoint my Son Josiah Cox my Executor and after he has paid my just Debts I do Give to him my whole Estate to dispose of at his discretion amongst my other Children as Witnefs my hand and
2 CONC  Seal this 27 day of June 1774
2 CONT Sealed and Signed                                                                     her
2 CONT In presents of                                                                    Judith     ) Cox (S.S)
2 CONT Frederick Hatchers                                                                       mark
2 CONT William Gray
