2 CONT Henrico, Virginia Wills & Deeds 1714-1718, pages 56-59 (begins on image 42)
2 CONT NOTES
2 CONT Henrico, Virginia Wills & Deeds 1714-1718, pages 56-59.
2 CONT The will of John Woodson of Henrico County was written on 25 November 1715 and proved in court on 5 December 1715 by James Cocke, Arthur Markham and Matthew Dod.  Family members named in the document are his:
2 CONT *son, Tarlton Woodson
2 CONT *son, Jacob Woodson
2 CONT *son, John Woodson
2 CONT *son, Robert Woodson
2 CONT *son, Josiah Woodson
2 CONT *son, Stephen Woodson
2 CONT *daughter, Judith Woodson
2 CONT *daughter, Elizabeth Woodson
2 CONT *brother, Benjamin Woodson.
2 CONT Another legatee is Josiah Paine, son of George and Mary Paine (whose relationship to the testator is not given).
2 CONT The testator gives away enslaved individuals as follows:
2 CONT *to his son, John Woodson -- Dick.
2 CONT *to his son, Robert Woodson -- Winter.
2 CONT *to his son, Jacob Woodson -- Bess, a girl.
2 CONT *to his daughter, Judith Woodson -- Judy, a girl.
2 CONT He desires that an enslaved man called Old Dick will fall "to him of my four sons, Tarlton, John, Robert or Jacob, that will give the most for him & the product to be equally divided among my eight children".
2 CONT The testator mentions several other unrelated individuals.
2 CONT Subscribing witnesses are James Cocke, Arthur Markham, Edward East, Barth. Newcome, and Matthew Dod.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE
2 CONT Inventory of the estate of John Woodson, deceased, presented to the Court by Tarlton Woodson, a Quaker - Henrico, Virginia wills & deeds 1714-1718, pages 81-85 (includes enslaved people)
2 CONT 23 April 1716
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-89P6-SL1C?lang=en&i=53
