1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elizabeth''' (if she existed) was born about 1668 in Henrico County, VA. She died June 4, 1691 in Henrico County, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: unknown.  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Lewis-of-Henrico-County/6000000084058525845?through=6000000002228246933 (1641-1687) and his wife Sarah did not have a daughter https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Woodson/60000
2 CONC 00002228246933.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #  On 10/21/1687 in Henrico County, VA. to Robert Woodson (1660-1729); he married 2nd to Elizabeth's sister [sic: unknown] the widow Sarah (Lewis) Willis, and 3rd to Rachel Watkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 children include [SIC: this list needs review!]
2 CONT # Stephen Woodson was born 1682 in Henrico County, VA. He died 1735 in Henrico County, VA.
2 CONT # Joseph Woodson was born 1685.
2 CONT # Robert Woodson was born 1687.
2 CONT # Agnes Woodson was born before 1689.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Woodson was born 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Woodson Jr. , who married Elizabeth one of the orphans of John Lewis Sr. , decd. summoned to ye next Crt. to discharge the Secty. (he having as it is allegded recd. his wives portion). p. 38.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT See https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lewis-3777
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was created from a clerk's TYPO. Henrico. In 1691 - Robert Woodson, Jr married Sarah Lewis On 1 Dec 1796 - the clerk's MISTAKE lists Robert's wife as Elizabeth - as one of heirs of John Lewis. Sarah (Lewis) Woodson is st
2 CONC ill alive until about 1710. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Whether this Elizabeth existed is uncertain—she may be a case of mistaken identity. According to Tidewater Virginia Families (quote): Elizabeth Woodson was the daughter of Robert and Elizabeth Woodson. ... Elizabeth is believed to
2 CONC  have married William Lewis. He was very likely the son of John Lewis, Sr. and the brother of Elizabeth who married Robert Woodson, Jr. William and Elizabeth had at least two children, William and Joseph Lewis, to whom their grand
2 CONC father, Robert deeded land.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is WRONG That source goes on to say that Robert Woodson Jr, son of Robert and Elizabeth Woodson (quote): married Sarah Lewis, the daughter of John Lewis, Sr. Their license was returned to the Henrico court in October 1692. It
2 CONC  seems that this was his second marriage, as there was an earlier entry in the Henrico court records. Robert Woodson, Jr., who married Elizabeth, one of the orphans of John Lewis, Sr., deceased was summoned to the April 1688 court
2 CONC  to discharge the secretary (he having alledgedly received his wife's portion of John Lewis' estate).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT However, there is nothing else to indicate that John Lewis had a daughter named Elizabeth. His inventory dated 2 Dec 1689 names only three heirs. According to Weisiger's wills of Hernrico County (quote): Accounts of estate of John
2 CONC  Lewis, dec'd, divided into three parts, and have given to the relict (now wife to Samuel Trottman) one third, to William Lewis (son and exec.) one third, and to Sarah, daughter of the dec'd, one third is to be held in possession 
2 CONC of her guardian William Lewis. A later entry said (quote): I Robert Woodson, Jr. acknowledge to have received of my brother in law William Lewis, my full share of what is due my wife Sarah, one of the orphans of John Lewis, dec'd.
2 CONC  [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In any event, the Elizabeth of this profile was clearly not daughter of John Lewis and could not be the mother of any children of Robert Woodson who were born before 1692 when he married Sarah Lewis.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/knight/167/
2 CONT
2 CONT I also have another copy of a periodical entitled "Historical Genealogy of the Woodsons and Their Connections".
2 CONT
2 CONT >In this periodical there is an entry which reads:37 Elizabeth, 4 was  undoubtedly born in Henrico, as her father lived and died in that county.It appears that her father had two daughters named Elizabeth--one by each wife--the el
2 CONC der sister married John Povall and athis one married John Knight and settled in Lunenburg county he died and his will was proved March 12, 1772, and names wife Elizabeth and ten children.The will was witnessed by Miller Woodson an
2 CONC d Thomas Jeffres. (See Wm. and Mary Qtly., Volume X, p.46.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, Sarah to Joseph Parsons, Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT >By Rachael Watkins, his second wife, Jonathan, and daughters, Elizabeth and Judith. Elizabeth married John Knight, and Judith married John Cook, and she was mother to all the money-making Cooks.
