1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed husband 
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-Francis-Willis/6000000015081430967?through=6000000005965685253.
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Willis-1148
2 CONT
2 CONT >The following passage ignores the will of Francis Willis' namesake benefactor, who is inaccurately described as his "father". It also states that the elder Francis' wife was Susan Lewis who later married Robert Woodson, Jr. of He
2 CONC nrico County. This is not true, as the marriage record is for Robert Woodson Jr. and Sarah Lewis, the daughter of John Lewis deceased. She was not a widow. Her father had passed away several years earlier while she was apparently 
2 CONC still a minor since her brother William served as her guardian. …
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT Updated 28 January 2026
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sarah Lewis''' was born 1669 / 1675 in Henrico County, Virginia and died there before November 1710.  She was the daughter of John Lewis of Henrico  and Sarah, who later married Samuel Trotman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Lewis married 10/1692 in St. John's Church, Henrico County, Colony of Virginia  to  Robert Woodson, born 1660 in Henrico, VA; died Feb 1729 in Henrico, VA, son of Col. Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris.  He was the widower
2 CONC  of Elizabeth, and married Rachel Watkins third.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lewis-249 and then edited 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Lewis was the '''only daughter''' of a John Lewis who died before Apr. 1688 of Henrico Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was born circa 1675 at Henrico County, VA, and was "a dozen or thirteen years of age" when her father's estate was settled in 1689. A typo of "Elizabeth" as the wife of Robert Woodson, Jr is found (see below) in a court reco
2 CONC rd after the marriage of Sarah Lewis to Robert Woodson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah's mother (not named) had married Samuel Trotman before October 1688 in Henrico
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in October 1692, at St. John's Church, Henrico County, VA, Robert Woodson Jr, son of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris; after obtaining a license on 11 Nov 1691; 
2 CONT
2 CONT children (surname WOODSON):[8][9][10][11]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children (dates uncertain) 
2 CONT # Stephen c.1682- m. Mary Woodson, daughter of Joseph Richard and Mary Jane Woodson
2 CONT # Joseph c.1685- m. Elizabeth Mattox
2 CONT # Robert c.1687-
2 CONT #  Elizabeth c.1689- m. John Povall
2 CONT # Sarah c.1692-  m. Joseph Parsons
2 CONT # Mary c.1695- died unmarried 
2 CONT # Agnes c.1697- m. Richard Williamson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah died before Nov 1710 at Henrico County, VA, when her husband asked to be "liberated" from the Henrico County Quaker community to marry again.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, Sarah to Joseph Parsons, Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT >By Rachael Watkins, his second wife, Jonathan, and daughters, Elizabeth and Judith. Elizabeth married John Knight, and Judith married John Cook, and she was mother to all the money-making Cooks.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===old notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT children of Robert Woodson and Sarah Lewis: [this list needs review!]
2 CONT # Sarah Woodson, born 1692 in Henrico, VA.
2 CONT # Mary Woodson, born 1695 in Henrico, VA; died 1774.
2 CONT # Jonathan Woodson, born 1696 in Henrico, VA.
2 CONT # Judith Woodson, born 1700 in Henrico, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
