2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, '''Sarah to Joseph Parsons''', Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT MARRIAGE
2 CONT Married ca March 1717/18 Sarah Woodson b ca 1712 Va Sarah Woodson is shown to be the daughter of Robert Woodson Jr and Sarah Lewis in her father's last will and testament recorded February 1729, Henrico County Va in February 1729,
2 CONC  married Joseph Parson per page 539, Genealogies of Virginia Families from William & Mary College Quarterly Historical Magazine
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH'S PARENTS Robert WOODSON: (b. 1658, "Curles", Henrico Co., Virginia, d. bef Feb 1728/29, "Curles") 
2 CONT Sarah's father, Robert Woodson Sr, was the son of Robert Woodson I (b. 1634 Flowerdew Hundred Plantation, Henrico Co., Virginia (now Prince George Co., Virginia), d. 1716 Henrico) & Elizabeth Ferris (b. 1638 James City Co., Virgin
2 CONC ia, d. 1689 Henrico).  
2 CONT This Robert Woodson I was the son of Dr. John Woodson & his wife Sarah. Elizabeth Ferris was the daughter of Richard Ferris (b. 1596, d. 1637 Henrico) & Sarah Hambleton.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/120685830/sarah-parsons
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  1692 Henrico County Virginia, USA  Death:  1750 Henrico County Virginia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  Robert Woodson (1660 - 1729) and Sarah Virginia Lewis (1669 - 1710)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:  Joseph Parsons (1690 - 1770)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown 
2 CONT
