2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Knight was born about 1710 in Virginia. John married Elizabeth Woodson, in Lunenburg County, Virginia. Elizabeth Woodson was born in 1713 in Henrico County, Virginia. John died in Lunenburg County, Virginia sometime between w
2 CONC riting his will 7 Sept 1771 and the probate date of 12 March 1772. Elizabeth died in Lunenburg County, Virginia after 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT John’s will, covering six pages, lists what his eleven children have already received and what he feels is due them. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 11 children of John Knight (d 1772) and his wife Elizabeth Woodson were: 
2 CONT # Jonathan (born in Goochland County, Virginia, married his cousin Judith Woodson, daughter of Joseph Woodson (1715-?) and Elizabeth Mattox), 
2 CONT # John, 
2 CONT # Peter (married Coleman Mason. Peter’s daughter, Nancy, married Coleman Knight, son of Charles Knight; witness to consent Richard Mays and Peter Robertson Dec 14, 1787. His daughter Molly married James Barnes: Witness to consent 
2 CONC Coleman Knight, Isaac Holmes and George Bagley Jan 28, 1788), 
2 CONT # William, 
2 CONT # Joseph married Jerusha Cone,
2 CONT # Rachel married William Dudley 8-12-1784, 
2 CONT # Charles married Mary Smith (Their son, Coleman married Charles' brother Peter’s daughter Nancy), 
2 CONT # Woodson, 
2 CONT # Elizabeth married Thomas Sturdivant 27 Dec 1784 by Rev. John Meglamore, 
2 CONT # Judith (b. ca 1739 m before 1776 in Amelia Co., VA to George Bagley (b. 1739-d 1795 in Nottoway Co., VA),
2 CONT # Mary (Polly) married Joseph Lea,
2 CONT
2 CONT *and his granddaughter, Lucy Cook.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=GSYjAQAAIAAJ&lpg=PA142&ots=MyetAlxhOJ&dq=Elizabeth%20Woodson%20knight&pg=PA55#v=onepage&q&f=false page 55] of The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11 edited by Lyon Gardiner Tyler, Richard
2 CONC  Lee Morton.  "Woodson Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT >Robert (son of first Robert) married Sarah Lewis. Had sons, Stephen, Joseph and Robert; and daughters, Elizabeth, married to John Povall, Sarah to Joseph Parsons, Mary died a maid, and Agnes married Richard Williamson.
2 CONT
2 CONT >By Rachael Watkins, his second wife, Jonathan, and daughters, Elizabeth and Judith. Elizabeth married John Knight, and Judith married John Cook, and she was mother to all the money-making Cooks.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/knight/167/
2 CONT
2 CONT I also have another copy of a periodical entitled "Historical Genealogy of the Woodsons and Their Connections".
2 CONT
2 CONT >In this periodical there is an entry which reads:37 Elizabeth, 4 was  undoubtedly born in Henrico, as her father lived and died in that county.It appears that her father had two daughters named Elizabeth--one by each
2 CONT wife--the elder sister married John Povall and athis one married John Knight and settled in Lunenburg county he died and his will was proved March 12, 1772, and names wife Elizabeth and ten children.The will was witnessed by Mille
2 CONC r Woodson and Thomas Jeffres. (See Wm. and Mary Qtly., Volume X, p.46.)
2 CONT
