2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed husband 
2 CONT
2 CONT > “https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Mims/6000000007370538103?through=6000000004169790304 married Judith Woodson about 1732 probably in Goochland County, Virginia.” (Quote by Ann Blomquist in 2002: “Benjamin Mims’ wife's name h
2 CONC as been widely reported to be Judith Woodson, but (to date, 2002) no records have been found to support this. The VA Woodson family is well documented and no Judith Woodson who married a Mims is included in their genealogies. ”)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Named in the Will of Robert Woodson written 6 July 1729:
2 CONT
2 CONT >daughter Judith (one negro girl named Nanney, one feather bed, spotted silk rug, and all thereunto belonging to her, one seal skin trunk)
2 CONT
