1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A129221  DAR Ancestor #: A129221]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Netherland, daughter of Wade Netherland and Mary Lightfoot, married Tucker Woodson, son of Joseph Richard Woodson and Mary Jane Woodson Woodson, in Feb 1762 at Cumberland, Virginia.  He was Sarah Hughes widower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her death of 12 DEC 1775 at Goochland was recorded in The Douglas Register.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Tucker Woodson and Mary Netherland:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Wade Netherland Woodson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Tucker Woodson, Goochland Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT Milly, Jule, Lewis, Lidy my negroes to be free at my death. All my furniture, beds, desk, tables, wh.....in the hands of Samuel Woodson to be equally divided between Wade N. Woodson, Ben. Woodson, Henry Woodson, Tarleton Woodson a
2 CONC nd John P. Woodson my sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Roderick Payne, Mary Pollock, Margaret Payne. Dated Nov. 20, 1792. Proved Sept. 21, 1795. Vol. 16, p. 484.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pollock & Margaret Payne made oath that the testator declared on the 18 day May 1795 that the children Jack & Sucky of Milly the execution thereof should likewise be free at his death as well as her future increase which was 
2 CONC ordered to be entered on record.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Grandfather, I am proud of your contribution to the American Revolution and of our Liberty.  Along with your son, Tucker Woodson II you signed the Albemarle Declaration of Independence.  Thank you for your contribution to my 
2 CONC freedom and the freedom of every American today.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
