2 CONT Married in Curles, Henryco County Virginia to Sarah Woodson on 6-1-1688, the daughter of Robert Woodson & Elizabeth Ferris.  He married 2nd to Mary Watkins in 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Edward was born around 1665, likely in Charles City County in the Colony of Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sarah Woodson around 1688 and by 1704 they were living on about 150 acres in Henrico County. He was a carpenter and a farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward was also a Quaker and helped build the Curles Meeting House in 1701. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after the death of his wife Sarah, Edward married Mary on 8 January 1717. She was the widow of Henry Watkins.  Edward & Mary had no children together. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1722, he was contracted to build the new meeting house in White Oak Swamp. In the meantime, they held the monthly meetings at his house. By July 1724, per a letter of condemnation, Edward was kicked out of the Society of Friend
2 CONC s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward died before May 1742 in Henrico County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward and Sarah had 8 known children together:
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Edward married Sarah Woodson around 1688 and by 1704 they were living on about 150 acres in Henrico County. He was a carpenter and a farmer.  Edward was also a Quaker and helped build the Curles Meeting House in 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1722, he was contracted to build the new meeting house in White Oak Swamp. In the meantime, they held the monthly meetings at his house. By July 1724, per a letter of condemnation, Edward was kicked out of the Society of Friend
2 CONC s. 
