2 CONT
2 CONT I Joseph Mosby of Prince George County "desirous to settle that small estate the Almighty hath been pleased to bless me with between my wife and child and that no quarrels or disputes may happen amongst them after my death", that 
2 CONC my body be decently intered after the manner of the Church of England , To Wife œ15 sterling as lyes in her fathers hands and six pistolls (pistoles) that is in John Smiths hands and two mars and thirty wt. of feathers & chest and
2 CONC  table, two chairs & entry of land for 200 acres on the "land Brooks ." To daughter Mary , one negro named Nan , one negro named Roger , feather bed and furniture, 6 dishes, six plates 1 doz. of spoons 1 tankard, 1 salt sellor, wa
2 CONC rming pan, two earthen Jugs, 1 chest 4 cows & calves & 4 sows, 500 acres of Land lying upon Hungary Branch . If my daughter dye without Heirs of her body lawfully begotten then all to return to my brother Hezekiah Mosby ; my daugh
2 CONC ter to be under the care of her mother till her mother marries or dyes and then said daughter to be under care of my sister Agnes Binford and what Estate she has till she comes to the age of fourteen years old. To brother Jacob Mo
2 CONC sby , one Gray Colt belonging to a Bay Mair bought of John Woodlief . Estate not be appraised. Wife my whole & sole Executrix. Dated 19 Jany. 1726/7 . Witnesses Joshua Woodleif , Jacob Mosby . Recorded 13 June 1727 . Vol. 1713-172
2 CONC 8, p. 1014.  
