2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Woodson''' was born about 1706 in Henrico county, Colony of Virginia, son of Benjamin Woodson (1666 - 1723) and Sarah (Porter) Woodson (~1668 - 1723).   John died about 1790 in Goochland County, Virginia, United States age
2 CONC d ~84.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is seen as John Woodson IV, a genealogy nickname? 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Mary  Miller (~1710 - 1775) on 10 August 1731 in Lancaster county, Colony of Virginia. She was the daughter of John Miller (abt. 1680 - 1717) & Margaret Carter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary (Woodson) McCraw (1736 - ~1813) m. Francis McCraw
2 CONT #  Anna (Woodson) Easley (~1736 - >1801) m. Warham Benskin Easley Sr. (DAR)
2 CONT # Sarah (Woodson) Hatcher (~1740 - ~1813) m. Frederick Hatcher, (DAR)
2 CONT # Captain Miller Woodson Sr. (1745 - 1830); m. Mary de Graffenreidt (DAR)
2 CONT # John ‘Poplar Foot’ Woodson, Jr.  (~1747 - 1810 m. 1) Joanna Booker 2) Elizabeth Raine Venable (DAR)
2 CONT # Judith (Woodson) Michaux (1747 - 1803) m. Joseph Michaux 
2 CONT # Susannah (Woodson) Ligon (~1750 - 1828) m. William Ligon  (DAR)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Revolutionary War Service
2 CONT State of Service: VA Qualifying Service: Patriotic Service DAR #: A129205
2 CONT Birth: abt 1696 / Henrico / VA Death: abt 1790 / Cumberland / VA
2 CONT Patriotic Service Description: Patriotic Service VA- Member of the Committee of Safety, Cumberland Co Feb-Nov 1775[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Military Service 
2 CONT
2 CONT This man?
2 CONT
2 CONT List of the Colonial Soldiers of Virginia
2 CONT *Captain Woodson of the Virginia Regiment, the Sandy Creel Expedition against the Shawnees in the Ohio Valley, 1759, under the Command of Major Andrew Lewis.
2 CONT *John Woodson, Gent. served in the Virginia Colonial Militia rising to the rank of Colonel well before the Revolutionary War. At the outbreak of the Revolutionary War, due to his age and infirmities, he resigned his Commission and
2 CONC  recommended that it be granted to Lieut. Robert Lewis, a grandson of his previous Commanding Officer and close friend. John Woodson was then commissioned as County Lieutenant of Goochland Sept. 20 1779 and also appointed Goochlan
2 CONC d County Sheriff on 19 Oct 1776.
2 CONT *Pages 845, 846:Woodson, John, referred to as Colonel when paid for supplies furnished Capt. Roger Thompson's Co. of Minute Men Oct. 10, 1776; Appted Sheriff Oct 19, 1776; rec. as County Lieutenant of Goochland Sept. 20 1779; on s
2 CONC ame day Robert Lewis rec. as Colonel in his stead; resigned as County Lieutenant Aug. 20, 1781. Woodson, John, Goochland Militia, oath as Lieut. Sept 20, 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Deeds
2 CONT
2 CONT *16 Jul 1733, John Woodson, Jr. to Joseph Woodson Jr. for £16, 260 acres in Goochland, being part of a tract patented in names of William Woodson, Benjamin Woodson, Jr., Joseph Woodson, Jr., Robert Woodson, and John Woodson, Jr., 
2 CONC lying on branches of Deep Cr.; wit: Aug’t Webber, Jas. Woods, Jr. James Daniel; signed John Woodson, Jr. rec. 4 July 1733 [5]
2 CONT *15 Mar 1734, Appraisal of improvement on John Woodson’s land at a branch of Deep Cr., called Watson’s Cr. value £313/10/0; signed Richard Parker, Joseph Woodson, Anthony Hughes, Joel Chandler; rec. 18 Mar 1734 [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth and and death dates estimated.  The dates seen at DAR / SAR seem inaccurate.  
2 CONT * Have not seen Will data.
2 CONT * Birth, death, location data may be conflated with other men called John Woodson.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Woodson-112 “Know all men by these presents that we, '''John Woodson, of the county of Goochland''', and William Miller of the county of Lancaster, are held and firmly bound unto our Sovereign Lord,
2 CONC  King George ye second, in ye sum of fifty pounds, current money of Virginia, to be paid to our s’d Sovreign Lord, his heirs or successors; to ye w’ch Payment, wel and truly to be made, we bind ourselves, our heirs, Ex’ors and Adm
2 CONC ’rs jointly and severally firmly by these presents. Dated this Tenth day of August 1731. The condition of this obligation is such that, whereas there is a License desired for a marriage Intended between the above bound John Woodso
2 CONC n, and Mary Miller of ye county of Lancaster aforesaid. If, therefore, there is no Lawful cause to Obstruct the s’d marriage, then this obligation to be void; otherwise to remain in full force and virtue.”
2 CONT * https://sarpatriots.sar.org/patriot/display/324327 Spouse: Mary Miller.  Children: Nancy Ann; Sarah/Sara; Miller; Susanna; John Jr; Anna/Anne;
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/78006753/john-woodson
