1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A086043  DAR Ancestor # A086043]
2 CONT
2 CONT PAINE, JOHN Ancestor #: A086043
2 CONT Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): PATRIOTIC SERVICE
2 CONT Birth:  12-4-1713    HENRICO CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Death:  7-28-1784     GOOCHLAND CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Service Source:  WILLIAM & MARY QUARTERLY, SER 1, VOL 5, P 254; VA MAG OF HISTORY, VOL 5, P 217,  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_members_of_the_Virginia_House_of_Burgesses List of Members of the Virginia House of Burgess]
2 CONT Service Description:  
2 CONT 1) MEMBER OF COMMITTEE OF SAFETY, GOOCHLAND CO
2 CONT 2) MEMBER OF HOUSE OF DELEGATES, 1781
2 CONT 3) SERVED IN THE HOUSE OF BURGESS 1752-1768, and probably other years
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE
2 CONT 1) County: GOOCHLAND CO - State: VIRGINIA
2 CONT
2 CONT SPOUSE
2 CONT Number Name
2 CONT 1) X ARCHER  
2 CONT 2) JEAN SMITH CHICHESTER  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN PAYNE Proved September 23, 1773 Book 5 page 400 Son: John Payne, 1 shilling and no more. Land to be equally divided between Daniel Payne, Mark Payne and Edmond Payne,  my three other sons [Note: unnamed in this will] Wife: Ha
2 CONC nna Payne, sole executrix Witnesses: David Harris, Joseph Harris and John Harris Signed: John (o) Payn [sic]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://frontporchrockernews.blogspot.com/2006/02/paynes-of-pittsylvania-county-virginia.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Payne Family Cemetery at "The Cottage" on Ivy Creek #658
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. John Payne of "White Hall" in Goochland Co., was born in 1713 and was a member of the House of Burgessess 1752-88. During the Revolutionay War, he was a Lt. Col. of Militia and a member of Goochland's Committee of Safety. In 
2 CONC 1775, hissecond son Archer, married Martha Dandridge, daughter of British Capt. Nathaniel West Dandrige and Dorothea Spotswood Dandridge [daughter of Gov. Alexander Spotswood]. Archer's half-brother, Col. Phillip Payne, resided at
2 CONC  "Airy Mount", on Seneca Creek near Marysville and married, Elizabeth, a sister of Martha Dandridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Archer and Martha D Payne had 11 children. Three of their daughters married sons of Col. John Bolling [b. 1700, and a member of the House of Burgessess for 30 yrs]; John Bolling owned 20,000 acres, adjoining Nicholas Davies, in th
2 CONC e presentBoonsboro & Peakland sections of Lynchburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Ruth H Early, the third son of Archer Payne, John Robert Dandridge Payne, married Susan Bryce and "lived for may years in Lynchburg". Archer's oldest daughter also married a Bryce. Archer's second son, Alexander Spotswood Payn
2 CONC e, marriedCharlotte Brice, another daughter of Archibald Bryce, of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1840, Alexander Spotswood Payne moved to "the Cottage", on Ivy Creek, Campbell Co., with a farm comprising some 700 acres. In "Campbell Chronicles & Family Sketches" 1927, Ruth Early described her visit to the "old family buryi
2 CONC ng groundat 'The Cottage'" as being nine graves marked by tombstones with inscriptions. It is unknown how many additional graves were there. Some records indicated that "The Cottage" was built in 1795, others state it as 1826. It 
2 CONC is unknown who founded the cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The cemetery was located near the residence on property presently occupied by Dr. Robert Bowen. Prior to the 1964/5 development of the Ivylink subdivision, the cemetery was sought to be relocated. However, only the tombstones were
2 CONC  removed to the Presbyterian Cemetery in Lynchburg. Surveyed & Researched by Revely Carwile, Jr., 1999. Campbell Co. Family Cemeteries, Vol. VIII
2 CONT
2 CONT As listed by Ruth Early & Julia Asher, the tombstones of nine graves existed at the original location. At least 13 graves from Ivy Creek were re-interred into the Presbyterian Cemetery in Lynchburg. Many of these have the original
2 CONC  stones &footstones, although some have new marked
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT 1. Archer Payne,   b. 1748, Goochland County, Virginia     d. Aft 1785, New Market, Goochland County, Virginia 
2 CONT 2. Robert Payne,   b. Bef 1750, Goochland County, Virginia   d. 17 Dec 1770, Goochland County, Virginia -  
2 CONT 3. John Payne,   b. Bef 1742, Goochland County, Virginia    d. 21 Dec 1795, Goochland County, Virginia
