1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Smith was born after  1676 and died Abt 1755. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of  John Smith and Hannah Daft. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Peter Harris, (b abt 1668 d 1704), son of Peter Harris & Mechell, in 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Harris , Jr. and Mary Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT *John Harris was born aft 1695 and died Unknown.  Married Ann.
2 CONT *Peter Harris III was born ABT 1696, and died ABT 1771.  Married Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT * Marriage 26 JUN 1695 St. John's Church,Henrico,Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/harris/21369/
2 CONT Has 
2 CONT >1. The marriage for the son Peter Harris, Jr. (to Mary Smith) has a date of 26 June 1695.(I've not seen the original reference myself, which is said to be a record from St. John's Church in Henrico Co., VA:  ftp://ftp.rootsweb.co
2 CONC m/pub/usgenweb/va/henrico/vitals/marriages/1699.txt). This places Peter, Jr.'s birthyear as being most likely sometime after ca. 1665 and is thus consistent with a birthyear for him in the 1670's as is commonly given.
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._John%27s_Episcopal_Church_(Richmond,_Virginia)_
2 CONT
2 CONT >Exact locations of the church buildings at Varina are unknown. A third or fourth church building was built a few miles east of Varina Farms on a plantation known as "Curles", some twenty miles east of the present city of Richmond
2 CONC , in the current Varina District of Henrico County. The only relic of that church still surviving is the bowl of the baptismal font, which today is used at St. John's. 
2 CONT
