1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From https://www.unc.edu/~rowlett/families/smith_charles_city.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >11 Jacob Smith is the shadowy founder of the family. The only thing known for sure about him is that sometime after 1643 he bought from Edward Martin a tract of 200 acres in Diggs Hundred, Charles City County. This was at the wes
2 CONC tern end of the county, and the boundary of the tract was on Turkey Island Creek, the Henrico County line. Court records from Charles City County survive from around 1660; the absence of Jacob from these records probably means he 
2 CONC was dead by that time.
2 CONT
