1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1726
2 PLAC Amelia Co VA.
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1762
2 ADDR
3 STAE VA
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Was the daughter of George Moore of Amelia County.  Was probably the sister of Ann, who married Samuel Morton, ThomasÕs cousin, (son of his uncle John).
2 CONT
2 CONT Some people seem to think that the Catherlin Morton over age 45 listed as head of household in 1800 census for Person County, NC is this one with 1 male & 1 female 16-26, 1 male & 1 female 10-16, 2 females under 10.  I find this h
2 CONC ighly unlikely.  Certainly that any of the members listed with her would be any of her children. Even if one is actually age 26, that would mean Cicily had a child at age 48 in 1774.  Not impossible, but unlikely.  Certainly by 17
2 CONC 85 in Prince Edward County, when her husband Thomas was in the census, the household was listed as containing 3 whites - supposedly Thomas, his wife Cicily, and their youngest child.  Would that perhaps have been Icy or Susannah?
2 CONT
2 CONT Also there are claims that a Catherine Morton appears on a tax list for Person County, NC in 1799 and again in 1802.
