1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR Ancestor #: A046317
2 CONT https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/default.cfm
2 CONT
2 CONT Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): LIEUTENANT
2 CONT Birth:  1749    HANOVER CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT Death:  7-16-1798     RUTHERFORD CO NORTH CAROLINA
2 CONT Service Source:  GWATHMEY, HIST REG OF VA IN THE REV, P 315
2 CONT Service Description:  1) FIRST LIEUTENANT, MECKLENBURG MILITIA
2 CONT
2 CONT EDWARD6 GOODE (EDWARD5, THOMAS4, JOHN3, RICHARD2, RICHARD1) was born 1749 in Henrico Co. Va..  He married MARY TURPIN, daughter of SUSLEY TURPIN and SARAH REDFORD.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About EDWARD GOODE:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 1: Served in Revolutionary war under Capt. Benjamin Lincoln.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 2: Fought in Battle of Savannah and Yorktown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 3: 1781, Appointed 1st Lt. in the Militia of Mecklenburg Co. Va.
