1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * FUQUA, MOSES  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A042682  DAR Ancestor #: A042682]
2 CONT * Service:  VIRGINIA    Rank(s): CAPTAIN, PATRIOTIC SERVICE
2 CONT * Birth:  CIRCA 1738    AMELIA CO VIRGINIA
2 CONT * Death:  ANTE 12-19-1814     GREENUP CO KENTUCKY
2 CONT * Service Source:  GWATHMEY, HIST REG OF VA IN THE REV, P 292; VA MAG OF HIST & BIO, VOL 36 PP 257, 259; ABERCROMBIE & SLATTEN, VA REV PUB CLAIMS, VOL 1, PP 113,177
2 CONT * Service Description:  1) CAPT OF CAMPBELL CO, MILITIA; ALSO 2ND LT, BEDFORD CO, MILITIA
2 CONT * 2) FURNISHED SUPPLIES, TOOK OATH 1780
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Moses FUQUA:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth    1738  , Amelia Co, VA   
2 CONT
2 CONT Death    13 October 1814  , Greenup Co, KY   
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial      Family Ground on Ohio River, Greenup Co, KY   
2 CONT
2 CONT Census  1810 Greenup Co, KY census   
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses married Judith Woodson about 1759, residing in Virginia for almost forty years when they moved to Greenup, County, Ky., about 1797 to 1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Campbell County, Virginia, on February 8, 1782, Moses Fuqua produced a commission from the governor of Virginia as a Captain and took the oath of office.  On October 3, 1782, he received a certificate calling for payment for se
2 CONC rvices to the Continental (Revolutionary) Army for supplies, arms, teams, etc.
