2 CONC (now in the occupation of Morton), both tracts brought by Morton or Thomas Jones and Edmund Manion. Also six slaves, mulatto Jack, Negro Dick, Cofee, Harry, Sam, and Will, and six horses, four mares, two year old colt, thirty head
2 CONC  of cattle, twenty sheep, twelve feather beds and furniture, and three guns. (Signed) Wm. (W) Morton. Wit: Henry Willis, Junr., James Porteus, Jno. Christopher, John Newport. 27 July 1739. Proved by James Porteus and John Newport.
