1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Watkins-996
2 CONT
2 CONT The origin of John Watkins is unknown according to John Stutesman, who wrote an article, " John Watkins of Henrico County, 1743," however "assertions have been made" that he was a grandson of the Henry Watkins, Quaker farmer in He
2 CONC nrico County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Watkins-996
2 CONT
2 CONT John Watkins wrote his will on 28 July 1743 and signed it "W." It was probated on the "first Monday in May 1744" at Henrico County, Virginia.[1]. John's will appointed executors, his "wife Elizabeth" and son John; the witnesses we
2 CONC re Henry and Ann Stokes, and "Honour Sullavent"
2 CONT
2 CONT John married to Elizabeth Unknown.[1] Our only records of her do not give her maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, four sons and four daughters, (in the order mentioned in John's will):
2 CONT
2 CONT *David
2 CONT *Isaiah
2 CONT *John
2 CONT *Nathaniel
2 CONT *Lucy Perkins
2 CONT *Constant Woodson
2 CONT *Elizabeth Watkins
2 CONT *Joyce Watkins
2 CONT
2 CONT John left his son, John, "all my carpenter's and cooper's tools" and the 150 acres in Henrico County "whereon I now live."[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT # Stutesman, John H., John Watkins of Henrico County, 1743. Tidewater Virginia Families, Volume 4 Number 4, pp. 223-226, Web. accessed October 3, 2014 http://www.tidewatervirginiafamilies.com/watkins.html 
2 CONT
