1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/b/o/t/Terrell-G-Bottoms/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0246.html
2 CONT
2 CONT John E. Bottom Jr. (son of John B. Bottom and Elizabeth Watkins) was born Bet. 1684 - 1686 in Varina Parish, Henrico Co., Va., and died July 02, 1737 in Henrico Co., Va..He married Elizabeth on 1706 in Henrico, Va..
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for John E. Bottom Jr.:
2 CONT WILL:Provided July 2, 1737 Henrico County, Va.
2 CONT In the name of God amen this Second Day of July 1737.I John Bottom of Henrico County being very sick & weak in body but of perfect mind & memory thanks be given unto God.Therefore calling to mind the mortality of my body & knowing
2 CONC  it is appointed for all man____to die.I do make & ordain that this my last Will & Testement that is to Say princapilly {sic} &____of all I give & recommend Soul into the hands of God that gave it life.For my Body I recommend it t
2 CONC o the Earth to be buryed {sic} in a Christian like & decent mannor {sic} at the Riferation {sic} of my Executors, nothing doubting but at the general resurrection I shall receive the same again by the mighty power of God, & his to
2 CONC uching Seals wordly fate, wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me this life I give diviss (sic) & dispose of the same in the following manner & form Imprimis. {sic} I give unto my '''two youngest sons John Bottom & William Botto
2 CONC m''' & their heirs forever one hundred acres of land to be divided between them.ITEM I give unto '''my son Thomas Bottom''' sixty acres of Land of my plantation to him & his heirs forever.I further give my son Thomas two cows & tw
2 CONC o heiffers {sic}, one feather bed & furniture, one iron pot & one gun.ITEM I give & bequeath unto '''Elizabeth my Dear beloved wife''' all the Remainder of lands, cattle, goods, moveables & immovables, whom I likewise____ & ordain
2 CONC  with my son Thomas Bottom to ____ Sole Exectutor of this my last Will & Testament.In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seal the day & year above written.John m Bottom (seal} Signed, sealed, published, pronownced {sic}
2 CONC  declared by this John Bottom at his last Will & Testament in presence of us...Richard Truman Francis F. Brothers Edward E. Marrit At a court held for the Henrico County the first Monday in September 1737 this will was presented b
2 CONC e theexecutor upon oath & proved by the oath of his ____ & thereupon admitted to Record. Bowlore coche____.
2 CONT JOHN's '''daughters Sarah & Sussannah''' were not named in his will, but they were named in his son John's will in 1781.He was not married & left his estate to his two sisters. 
2 CONT ----
