1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT His first wife died 22 Sep 1680, and two years later on 10 Aug 1682, James Taylor married Mary Gregory of Rappahannock and they had
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mary (2), b. 29 Jun 1688, m1. Edward Watkins, m2. Henry Pendleton, d. 10 Jun 1770 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Taylor-1601
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born on 29 June 1688 in that part of New Kent County that would become King and Queen County, Virginia in 1691, the daughter of James Taylor and Mary Gregory.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1701 when she was just thirteen, she married Henry Pendleton and bore him six known children, four sons and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary Pendleton
2 CONT # Edmund Pendleton
2 CONT # James Pendleton
2 CONT # Nathaniel Pendleton
2 CONT # Isabella Pendleton
2 CONT # John Pendleton
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary also had the following child:
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown Pendleton
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Watkins second wife was Mary Bishop TAYLOR PENDLETON (m.Abt 1723). They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # C) . Mary WATKINS (b.22 Mar 1726 d.13 Nov 1805-Chesterfield County,VA) | sp: Jordan ANDERSON (b.1723 m.15 Sep 1748 d.1805)
2 CONT # D) Sarah Elizabeth WATKINS (b.Abt 1726 d.Abt 1750-Chesterfield County,VA) | sp: "Sir" John CLAY (b.1721 m.Abt 1740 d.1762)
2 CONT # E) Edward (Jr.) WATKINS of Cumberland County, VA (b.Circa 1726 d.1812/1813-Powhatan Co.,VA) | sp: Rhoda THOMPSON (b.1732 m.17 Apr 1759 d.1827)
2 CONT # F) Martha WATKINS (b.Henrico County,VA) | sp: Francis MOSELEY (d.1782/1783)
2 CONT # G) Judith WATKINS | sp: Thomas BASS (b.1725 d.1804)
2 CONT # H) Frances WATKINS | sp: Richard MOSELEY (m.1803)
2 CONT # I) George (son of Edward) WATKINS | sp: Rebecca THOMPSON
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1779, when she was in her early nineties, or possibly on 10 June 1770, shortly before her eighty-second birthday, Mary died of unknown causes in Bowling Green, Caroline County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Taylor is recorded (without the middle name Bishop) in the Erasmus Taylor family Bible as having been born 29 Jun 1688. She married Henry Pendleton and died 10 Jun 1770.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT This Mary had a younger sister named Mary who was born 15 Nov 1686 and died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT "James I was married twice. We know this from bible records also online at the Library of VA website. His first wife was the mother of James Taylor II. Her name is not given in these records or any other records (but is often list
2 CONC ed with no sources as Frances? Walker?). The second wife of James I was Mary Gregory. The descendants of James Taylor I are from James Taylor II, his sister Sarah and from the surviving children he had with Mary Gregory–Anne, Mary
2 CONC , Edmund and John. James Taylor II married Martha Thompson. Sarah Taylor married Robert Powell. Ann Taylor married Edward Eastham, Jr. Mary Taylor married Henry Pendleton and Edward Watkins. Edmund Taylor married Sara. And John Ta
2 CONC ylor married Catherine Pendleton (the sister of Henry)."
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ann_blomquist&id=I06975
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=241735511-1-6833&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-d6a115dba9afb3087b24d0ee500d524a&mrid=406a9a81885d64a7158b49c6f6155d51 MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] via mother [http://www.geni.com/profile-34653934874 Mary Bishop Thomas (born Gregory)] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 2 2015, 16:05:46 UTC''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth: 	Jun. 29, 1688 Caroline County Virginia, USA Death: 	Jun. 10, 1770 Caroline County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) A comment by Deborah Barber (contributor #47746291) states in her note of 10/30/16 that there is NO document for Mary's middle name of Bishop. However, the "U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900" shows her name as 
2 CONC Mary Bishop Taylor, so it shall remain.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2)I have declined an edit request to change her surname from Pendleton to Watkins. The Watkins marriage was a second marriage for both. Mary is buried in the same cemetery as her first husband, Henry Pendleton, and not with Edward
2 CONC  Watkins. Both spouses are linked to her memorial. 
2 CONT
