2 CONT >Edward Watkins, born about 1676; died 1771 in Cumberland County, VA. Edward Watkins was a brother of Thomas “of Swift Creek” Watkins, as written by Mr. Francis N. Watkins of Farmville in 1859. He is also discussed in several othe
2 CONC r publications, best recollected as the great-grandfather of Henry Clay. The best I have been able to determine, Edward had three wives, the name of only the second known. He did not name a wife in his will, and it is not believed
2 CONC  he had any children by his third wife
