1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography ==
2 CONT John  Johnson III was born about 1732 in St Paul, Hanover, Virginia Colony, son of John Johnson II and Elizabeth Ellyson. <ref> [http://www.andersoncounty.scgen.org/library/Carl%20Ellison/CGE-02a.pdf Anderson County, SC GenWeb] ''
2 CONC Allison,-Ellison Scottish Cousins''</ref> John Johnson died August 31, 1816 in Lynchburg, Virginia, United States (Ivy Creek).<ref>[https://archive.org/details/ourquakerfriends00bell/page/44 Our Quaker Friends of ye olden time] ''
2 CONC Author: James Pinkney Pleasant Bell. Publisher:  Lynchburg, Va., J.P. Bell company, 1905. Page: 45.''</ref>
2 CONT John, who was born in Hanover Co., Virginia also lived for a time in Amelia Co., Virginia , where his father, John Johnson is said to have died and been buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Parents ===
2 CONT John Johnson was the son of Johnson-2064|John Johnson and Elizabeth Ellyson   <ref name="Hinshaw">[https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015051447657;view=1up;seq=264 Encyclopedia of American Quaker genealogy Vol VI] ''Auth
2 CONC or: William Wade Hinshaw. Publisher: Ann Arbor Michigan, 1950. Page: 252.''</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage ===
2 CONT John married Lydia Watkins in 1754 in Campbell County, Virginia Colony.  <ref name="Hinshaw" /><ref> [https://archive.org/details/ourquakerfriends00bell/page/12 Our Quaker Friends of ye olden time] ''Author: James Pinkney Pleasant
2 CONC  Bell. Publisher:  Lynchburg, Va., J.P. Bell company, 1905. Page: 12.''</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT
2 CONT The recorded children of John and Lydia Johnson are:
2 CONT #Judith Johnson, b: 1755.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #Susannah Johnson, b: 1757.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #James C Johnson, b 1758.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #Samuel Johnson, b: 1761.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #Joseph Johnson, b: 1763.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #John Johnson, b: 1766.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #Thomas Johnson, b: 1769.  <ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT #Jonathan Johnson, b: 1771.  <ref name="Hinshaw" /> and
2 CONT #Lydia Johnson, b: 1779.	<ref name="Hinshaw" />
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Aged about 84 years∼John was a son of John Johnson II and Elizabeth Ellyson. He married Lydia Watkins on 13 Jul 1754, Hanover, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is a grandson of John Johnson I and Lucretia Elizabeth Massie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: James Clark Johnson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy Vol. VI Cedar Creek Monthly Meeting Page 252
