1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Garret Johnson BIRTH	1708 New Jersey, USA DEATH	8 Mar 1766 (aged 57–58) Hopewell, Mercer County, New Jersey, USA BURIAL	 Pennington Methodist Church Burial Ground Pennington, Mercer County, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108571815/garret-johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Photo	 Robert Johnson 1750–1831
2 CONT
2 CONT Garret was born about 1707/08 based on his age at death (58 years). He was the son of Rutger Johnson and Annetje Gerrits, who settled in West New Jersey by 1699 and purchased a large tract in what is now Princeton in 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT Garret was devised his father's plantation on the Delaware River in 1748. He and his brother John were co-executors of their father's will. Garret was overseer of the River Road in 1742-3. His own will mentions land in Virginia. H
2 CONC e died, presumably, in Hopewell Twp., old Hunterdon (now Mercer) Co., NJ, where he resided at the time of making his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will, he named wife Judith. It is possible that she was Judith Watkins considering the 1761 marriage of a Garret Johnson and Judith Watkins recorded in the Richmond, VA, Quaker meeting records. If this is the case, Judith w
2 CONC as not the wife of Garret's older children, who were born in the 1730s-40s.   
2 CONT Family links:   Parents:   Rutger Johnson (1669 - 1749)   Annetje Gerrits Johnson (1676 - 1754)  
2 CONT  Children:   Robert Johnson (1750 - 1831)*  
2 CONT  Siblings:   Eve Johnson Hoff (1701 - 1757)*   John Johnson (1704 - 1752)*   Ann Johnson Updike (1705 - 1762)*   Winifred Johnson Hoff (1705 - ____)*   Garret Johnson (1708 - 1766)   Mary Johnson Schenck (1715 - 1767)*   Elizabeth
2 CONC  Johnson Couwenhoven (1716 - 1789)*  
2 CONT *Calculated relationship  
2 CONT Inscription: GARRET JOHNSON  DEPARTED THIS  LIFE MARCH [8TH] AGE 58 1766  
2 CONT Note: Heartfelt thanks to Patricia Stalter for creating this memorial, and to Patricia and Richard C. Burd for the gravestone images.  
2 CONT Burial: Pennington Methodist Church Burial Ground  Pennington Mercer County New Jersey, USA Plot: Right front section, 8th row from fence, 5th stone from wall  
2 CONT Maintained by: Joseph R. Klett Originally Created by: P. Stalter Record added: Apr 15, 2013  Find A Grave Memorial# 108571815
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Garret Johnson BIRTH	1708 New Jersey, USA DEATH	8 Mar 1766 (aged 57–58) Hopewell, Mercer County, New Jersey, USA BURIAL	 Pennington Methodist Church Burial Ground Pennington, Mercer County, New Jersey,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108571815/garret-johnson
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FindAGrave's page on Garret Johnson: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108571815/garret-johnson]:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Garret was born about 1707 or '08 based on his age at death (58 years). He was the son of Rutger Johnson and Annetje Gerrits, who settled in West New Jersey by 1699 and purchased a large tract in what is now Princeton in 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT Garret was devised his father's plantation on the Delaware River in 1748. He and his brother John were co-executors of their father's will. Garret was overseer of the River Road in 1742 and '43. His own will mentions land in Virgi
2 CONC nia. He died, presumably, in Hopewell Twp., old Hunterdon (now Mercer) Co., NJ, where he resided at the time of making his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will, he named wife Judith. It is possible that she was Judith Watkins considering the 1761 marriage of a Garret Johnson and Judith Watkins recorded in the Richmond, VA, Quaker meeting records. If this is the case, Judith w
2 CONC as not the wife of Garret's older children, who were born in the 1730s and '40s.
