2 CONT Daniel, William, jurist, b. in Cumberland county, Va., in 1770; d. in Lynchburg, Va., 20 Nov., 1839. He was a member of the Virginia house of delegates, and gained reputation as an orator by his defense of the "Resolutions of '98"
2 CONC  He became circuit judge and ex-officio member of the old general court of Virginia. His judicial opinions are high authority, and some of his sayings are proverbial in his neighborhood."
2 CONT
2 CONT source: Appletons' cyclopaedia of American biography, Vol. II, New York, D. Appleton and Company, 1887
