1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is assumed that John Clyborn married Mary Sheppey sometime around 1680 because court records of 2 Apr 1688 mentioned their orphaned son, John, as age six or seven. John, Jr. was placed with his aunt, Martha Shep
2 CONC pey, wife of Edward Stratton, Jr. Their son, Thomas, aged three or four on 1 Apr 1688 was to be raised by his aunt, Elizabeth Sheppey, and her husband Jeremiah Brown. Nothing more is known about Thomas Clyborn. As no provision is 
2 CONC made for Thomas in his uncle Jeremiah Brown's will, Lolita Bissell thought that he had probably died by 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Sheppey Clyborn marries, as her second husband, Thomas Newcomb by 1 Aug 1687. She is dead by 1 Apr 1688 when her sons, John, Jr. and Thomas are placed with her sisters.
