1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Betty-132
2 CONT
2 CONT Second wife believed to be Martha Thrower.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will of Thomas Bettey
2 CONT
2 CONT Written 6 March 1798; Proven 23 July 1798
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God amen. I Thomas Bettey of the County of Brunswick being in low state of health and calling to mind that it is appropriate by God for all men to die I do make and ordain this to be my last will and Testament first
2 CONC  of all I give my soul to God who gave it me and I desire to be decently buried by my executors that will hereafter mentioned. I desire that all of my just debts be first pade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - Lend unto my loving wife '''Patsey Betty''' during her life my plantation whereon I now live also one negro man Toney one Feather bed and furniture two cows and calves one mare three years old this spring and Eight hoggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I give unto my son '''Robert''' Bettey one negroe boy named Isaac and the little colt one Feather bed and furniture six hoggs also my tract of land I bought from Edward Walker to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I give unto my two daughters '''Gennet''' Bettey and '''Patsey''' Bettey one negroe girl named Anna to them equally divided to them and their heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I also give to my Daughter '''Gennet''' Bettey one Feather bed and furniture to her and heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I give my son '''Thomas''' Bettey my Land and Plantation whereon I now live and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I gave my son '''William''' Bettey one negro boy named John to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I gave unto my son '''John''' Bettey six shillings to him and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I gave unto Daughter '''Charlotte Lewis''' six shillings to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I desire that my woman Pegg should be sold to pay for the land I bought of Edward Walker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I desire that all of my Estate that I have not mentioned should be equally divided between my son Thomas Bettey, Robert Bettey, Gennet Betty and Patsey Bettey. I gave it to them and their heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item - I do appoint my Brother John Bettey and my son William Bettey Exors to this my Last Will and Testament. Witness my hand and seal this 6th day March and in the year of our Lord one thousand seven hundred and ninety eight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed, sealed, and delivered. Thomas (his X) Bettey (seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Benjamin Ivie Thomas Parham Chas. Collier
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://southernrootsandbranches.wordpress.com/2014/08/24/captain-william-batey-1760-1836/
2 CONT
2 CONT >Captain William Batey was born on his parents’ plantation on May 1,1760 in Brunswick County, Virginia His parents were Thomas Bettey and Martha Patsey Thrower Bettey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Beatty Project places him in Lineage 64:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.bp2000.org/wrappers/pages.php?ID=127
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 William Batte b: Abt. 1678 in VA d: Bet. December 09, 1754 - January 11, 1755 in VA ........ +Mary Stratton d: Bef. 1755 in VA m: May 1704 in VA - Henrico Co
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Thomas Batte/Bettey d: Bet. March 06 - July, 1798 in VA......... +Martha Patsey Thrower<br/>
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * 8 William (Capt.) Batey (was part of L002...) b: May 01, 1760 in VA - Brunswick County - Lawrenceville - near Meherrin River d: January 11, 1835 in TN - County
2 CONT ** ......... +Anne Bass b: August 23, 1773 d: August 03, 1854 in TN - Rutherford County m: January 21, 1798 in VA - Brunswick Co
2 CONT ** ......... *2nd Wife of William (Capt.) (L64) Batey:......... +Mary Betty b: Bef. 1772 m: December 24, 1787 in VA - Brunswick Co
2 CONT * 8 Martha Patsy Batey b: June 09, 1787 in VA - Brunswick Co d: July 22, 1860 in TN - Giles Co......... +Nathan Hicks Bass b: May 07, 1779 d: October 10, 1860 m: January 31, 1805 in VA - Brunswick Co
2 CONT * 8 Robert Batte
2 CONT * 8 Thomas Bettey
2 CONT * 8 John Batte
2 CONT * 8 Ginette Batte......... +Joshua Rickman
2 CONT * 8 Charlotte Batte......... +Harbert Lewis
2 CONT
2 CONT This person is NOT any relation to the BATTE family  of Prince George County, Virginia (which was part of Charles City County, prior to 1703.  See the R. Bolling Batte papers, which are in the Virginia State Library, and can be fo
