1 NAME Richard /Ward/
2 GIVN Richard
2 SURN Ward
2 _MARNM Ward
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1750
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of North Carolina
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 OCT 1788
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Soldier, farmer
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Will of Richard Ward  of Warren County, NC, written December 7, 1787 and proved in Warren County, August Court, 1788  left land to be equally divided between sons Richard Ward, Presley Ward and Benjamin Ward when B
2 CONC enjamin comes of age (21).  Wife - Ann Ward was to have free usage of the land and Negroes to raise their children, until son,Benjamin came of age.  Then the Negroes were to be divided between his wife Ann, son Benjamin Ward, son 
2 CONC Richard Ward, son Presley Ward, daughter Martha Ward, daughter Ann Ward, and daughter Betsy Linda Ward.   Wife Ann Ward was named executrix and Benjamin Ward, Jr. (Richard's brother) and John Liles Ward (Richard's brother) were na
2 CONC med as executors.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The inventory of the estate of Captain Richard Ward taken 4 Aug. 1788 listed 800 acres of land, and 8 Negroes.  The eight Negroes were:  a man -Billy, a woman -Massey, a woman - Linda, a girl - Sukey, a boy -Giddy, a girl - Molly 
2 CONC and a girl - Lucy.   A notation said Captain Benjamin Ward, Sr. claims Billy and Linder;  and Sukey is claimed by Presly Nelms, Sr.    (My note - Presly Nelms, Sr was Mrs. Ann Ward's father.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The sale of the estate of Richard Ward (d. 1788) shows a plat of land - 266 acres which was 1/3 part of Richard Ward's land laid off for widow Ann Ward by Wm. Campbell, surveyor.  The plat of Mrs. Ward's land was recorded.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Warren County, NC, Will Book 5, page 31. 
