1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The will of her father, Benjamin Ward, recorded in Nov. Court, 1788, Warren County, NC (to which Marcellus Jordan and the widow Elizabeth Ward were Executor and Executrix), left the following slaves to Martha and h
2 CONC er husband Marcellus Jordan  - Hannah, Ben, Frank, Anthony, Sall and Ruth and their increase.   They were  to go to the children that Martha and Marcellus had after the death of Martha and Marcellus.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surviving children born to Martha and Marcellus Jordan signed an agreement in 1819 listing the slaves as - Hanah, Bess, Frank, Anthony, Sall, Ruth and their increase - Daniel, George, Luster, Peter, Charles, Moses, William, Di
2 CONC nah, Martha, Violet, Nanny, Marina and Hannah.  (19 in all).  The surviving children of Martha and Marcellus Jordan were: Benjamin Jordan, Richard Jordan, Elizabeth Jordan (wife of John Wortham), Charlotte Jordan (wife of William 
2 CONC Montgomery, Nancy Jordan (wife of David Levy), and Burchet Jordan (wife of Gabriel Macon). 
