2 GIVN John
2 SURN Cocke
2 NSFX CSA
2 _MARNM Pope
2 NICK John Pope Cocke
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Mater Dolorosa Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Owensboro
3 STAE Kentucky
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1830
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Kentucky
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 OCT 1866
2 ADDR
3 STAE Kentucky
3 CTRY United States
1 TITL Maj.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} CSA <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT His birth name was John Pope Cocke, he shorted his name to John Pope at the request of his grandfather, Gov. John Pope.∼John Pope Cocke at the request of his grandfather, Governor John Pope (#7781373), and as a condition of Govern
2 CONC or Pope's will, he shortened his name to John Pope in 1851. (See Find A Grave, Maj. John Pope #31378267)  He served in the Civil War on the staff of General William Hardee (CSA) and after studying law at William & Mary  was an att
2 CONC orney in Owensboro, Ky.  He owned 474 acres of land located on the Ohio River about 6 miles below Owensboro.  He married in 1850, Theresa “Trecy” Ann Smith (1830-79), daughter of Dr. John B. (1800-73) and Mary Palmer Smith (1802-3
2 CONC 6), of Springfield, Ky.  Their ten children were “Mary” Elizabeth Johnson (1851-91); John, Jr. (1852-d.yg.); Katherine (1853-); Rosamond (1854-80); Agnes (1856-1906); Henrietta Theresa (1858-62); John, III (1860); Etta (1861-65); 
2 CONC John, IV (1863-75); and Susan Harriett Pope (1866-1906) who married Morgan Gary, of Grayson County, Ky., and they had one child, Eugene McAdams Gary. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Pope (1853-) married Dr. George Harbin, of Memphis.  A son, Walter Harbin, lived in San Antonio. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Pope (1856-1901) married in 1870, Cyrus Wilson Coy, of Bardstown, Ky.  Their seven children were John Pope (-1917) who was an electrical engineer; Vivian Pope who lived in Washington, D.C.; Irene; Joseph Arthur who lived in 
2 CONC Cincinnati, married and had one son, John Pope Coy; Dennis (d.yg.); Elizabeth who married Fred Newton Gibbs, of Little Rock; and Anna Rudd Coy who married June Bracy, of Little Rock.  Irene Coy married Robert Palmer Cox, of Madiso
2 CONC nville, Ky., and had three children, Robert Palmer, Jr., Vernon and Elizabeth Cox. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Pope's wife, Theresa Smith, died in 1879 from yellow fever while serving as a nurse and is buried in Memphis Cemetery. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT See Edward Pope McAdams, Some Ancestors of Eugene Perrot McAdams and Mary Elizabeth Pope McAdams of Hawesville, Ky. (Louisville, 1936), II: 51, 256-259; Eugene Pope McAdams, A McAdams Family History (Charlotte, N.C., 1989), 179.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31378267/john-pope-pope Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 14 2019, 20:02:34 UTC''
