1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wife Of Major N. S. Hill Dies In Washington Stricken With Apoplexy a Week Ago, Date: Friday, October 30, 1903   Paper: Baltimore American (Baltimore, MD)   Page: 16   Mrs Mary Pope Hill, wife of Major Nicholas S. H
2 CONC ill, managing director of the New Carrollton Hotel and the merchant's Club, died last evening at the home of her daughter, Mrs George M. Bolling, on M Street, Washington, D. C.  Mrs Hill was stricken with apoplexy a week ago while
2 CONC  on a visit to her daughter.  She suffered a second stroke yesterday and death resulted. Major Hill was summoned to his wife's bedside yesterday by telegraph.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Hill was 69 years old, and one of the most estimable women of Baltimore.  She was a Miss Pope before her marriage and belonged to one of the oldest and also one of the foremost families of Kentucky.  She was greatly beloved by
2 CONC  all who knew her, and the news of her death will prove a shock to Baltimore.  The heartfelt sympathy of the leading business, professional and financial men of the city will go out to the bereaved husband.  No one man in Baltimor
2 CONC e is better known or more highly respected than is Major Hill.
2 CONT ****
2 CONT
2 CONT Mortuary Notice Date: Saturday, October 31, 1903   Paper: Sun (Baltimore, MD)   Volume: CXXXIII   Issue: 168   Page: 6 Mrs Mary Coke Hill, wife of Major Nicholas S Hill, managing director of the New Carrollton Hotel and the Mercha
2 CONC nt's Club, died Friday evening at the home of her daughter, Mrs George M Bolling, 1808 Riggs Place, Washington.  Death was due to apoplexy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Hill was stricken Friday of last week while entertaining some friends in the drawing room of her daughter's home.  Her physician, Dr Larkin Glasebrooke, of Washington was summoned and Major Hill was notified.  Major Hill went 
2 CONC immediately to Washington, accompanied by Dr. W S Thayer.  Mrs Hill recovered somewhat, but about Wednesday night she became unconscious and remained so until she died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Hill was 69 years old and a native of Springfield, Ky. She was the daughter of the late, John Coke, of Kentucky.  The Major met her during the Civil War and they married in Arkansas in 1863? (can't read). Major Hill being at t
2 CONC hat time commissary of the Trans-Mississippi Department of the Confederate Army.  Major and Mrs Hill came to Baltimore immediately after the close of the war and have lived here ever since.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides Major Hill and her daughter--Mrs Bolling--Mrs Hill is survived by another daughter, Mrs Mills, wife of Dr James J Mills, 833 Park avenue--and a son -Mr Nicholas S Hill, Jr., Water Engineer of New York City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Hill's body will be brought to Baltimore this morning on the train arriving at Camden Station at 9:30.  The funeral will then proceed to the Cathedral, where a requiem mass will be celebrated at 10:15 o'clock.  The interment w
2 CONC ill be in Bonnie Brae Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The active pallbearers will be the following nephews of Mrs Hill. Messrs Richard S Hill and F Snowden Hill, of Prince George's county, Joseph Kent Hill and Samuel Brooke, Jr of Annapolis, and messrs Charles McHenry Howard, R. E. L
2 CONC ee Marshall, William Hammond, Dr Eugene McE Van Neas and Benjamin C Howard.
2 CONT
2 CONT **** Mortuary Notice Date: Sunday, November 1, 1903   Paper: Sun (Baltimore, MD)   Volume: CXXXIII   Issue: 169   Page: 6 Mrs Mary Coke Hill The funeral for Mrs Mary Coke Hill wife of Major N S Hill, manager of the New Carrollton 
2 CONC Hotel, who died in Washington on Thursday, took place yesterday morning from the cathedral, where a requiem mass was celebrated at 10:15 o'clock by Bishop Curtis, assisted by Rev William T Russel, Cardinal Gibbons was in the sanct
2 CONC uary.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were a large number of handsome flora tribute including a cross of roses from the employees of the Carrollton.  The interment was in Bonnie Brae Cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/121922050/mary-watki
2 CONC ns-hill Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 14 2019, 20:02:34 UTC''
