1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: He served in the U. S. Army in the Mexican War with his brother John Dejarnette Fletcher Watkins.  He then served in the Confederate Army in the Civil War between the States.  He was killed in 1862 in the Battle of Shar
2 CONC psburg.  At that time, he had a discharge from the Army either for age or Medical reasons in his pocket. He chose to stay with his group and die in Bloody Lane. His wife, Flora McBryde lived on until 1867.  At this time, the two y
2 CONC oungest children went to live with their aunt and uncle , Phoebe Jane Watkins Allen and her husband George W. Allen. The two children were John Sidney Watkins  born in 1854 and William Stokes Watkins born in 1855..
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: He was killed in 1862 in the Battle of Sharpsburg.
2 CONT Sources; Watkins Cem., Film # 860336-Page 42
2 CONT 1850 Census Anson Co., NC Film # 893720
2 CONT 1880 Census Anson Co., NC Film # 448,363
2 CONT #38251 Mar. of John Sydney Watkins
2 CONT Film C-A2L Part 1
1 CHAN
2 DATE 29 APR 2022
3 TIME 08:33:48
