1 NOTE He served in Company C. 1st Regiment of NC Volunteers.
2 CONT He served in the U. S. Army in the Mexican War.He enlisted in Concord 15 Jan 1847. After serving in Mex. they were mustered out at Smithville(present day Southport)NC, on 7 Aug 1848. He was 5'5", grey eyes, dark hair. A farmer at 
2 CONC age 19. A letter said he fell dead in the field while working.
2 CONT Information: Film # 0018105-1850 Census of Anson Co. NC
2 CONT              Film # 803887-1860 Census of Anson Co. NC
2 CONT              Film # 552621-1870 Census of Anson Co. NC
2 CONT              Film # 1,247,168 1900 Census of Anson Co. NC Film # 018158 Book C. Page 11. Will of Mumford Dejarnette Watkins in Anson Co. NC. He died while plowing in the field behind the home place in the Flatfork section of Anson
2 CONC ville, Anson Co. NC.
2 CONT Bap also 19 Jun 1971 OK End. 13 Oct 1971.OK
