1 NOTE One granddaughter stated that the "R" represented Romulus. (Not confirmed) After Confederate service in the Civil War, he returned to Stanly County, NC where he married and where their first three children were born. Later, they m
2 CONC oved to Montgomery County where the remaining children were born. Culpepper Jr. was a successful farmer, and served for a time in the North Carolina General Assembly. There was a recession in the late 1880's and early 1890's in No
2 CONC rth Carolina and other States as well, so the family sold out and moved to Putnam County, Florida circa 1891. In that decade, Florida was their best hope. They did establish deep roots and comfortable homes there, from which their
2 CONC  descendants have scattered to many places.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAY 2022
3 TIME 18:51:45
