1 NAME John /Looney/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Looney
2 _MARNM Looney
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1782
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 16 MAY 1846
1 TITL Chief
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This John Looney served in the War of 1812 three different times, was wounded in the hip or thigh and also attained the rank of Capt. before being discharged. He served in the same unit as his son, Henry Looney, an
2 CONC d they settled in early Alabama in St. Clair County where there is now a historical Looney log home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please do not confuse either of these Capt. John Looney with the Cherokee Indian Chief who also went by that name and who is buried in the National Cemetery in Washington, D.C. under this same title, i.e., Capt. (Note: he actually
2 CONC  served as a Private during the Creek War / War of 1812 and was wounded through the shoulder).There has not been any documentation of a family connection found between this Cherokee Chief and the other Looney family members mentio
2 CONC ned who were Scot-Irish descent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref: http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/renfro/1938/
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Stewart Cooper Jr's pedigree chart:  John Looney Jr, born about 1774, died before 1/15/1827 in St. Clair Co., Alabama
