1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KLLX-DN4 FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 10 2019, 9:04:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Hannah Turney
2 CONT
2 CONT 'The following is the will of Hannah Turney. She was the wife of Peter Turney and they were the first Turneys in Van Buren County. They arrived about 1834 with their children. One son, Russell was born after they arrived.
2 CONT
2 CONT State of Arkansas, Van Buren County, September 18th A.D. 1862
2 CONT
2 CONT Know all men by these present that I, Hannah 'Turney of county and state aforesaid, being of sound mind and  memory do make this my last will and testament, revoking all others.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st. It is my will and wish that all my just debts and funeral expenses be paid off.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd. It is my will that my son Daniel have all my household and kitchen furniture with the house I now live in with so much of the  land as to enclose the garden and orchard in back to the line.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd I give unto my two sons, Russell and William Turney, all the land west of the branch running by the stable. William to have in the fork of the branch and Russell to have his --- west of William's.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th All the rest of my land as shown in the deeds to be divided between my sons Henry, Joseph, and --- Turney.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5th. All my daughters to have an equal share of my stock of all kinds except Elizabeth Gadberry to whom I give five dollars to be paid by my executors. My sons not to have any part of my stock.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6th. I have hereby nominated and appointed William Cullum my executor. Given under my hand and seal her mark
2 CONT X Hannah Turney
2 CONT
2 CONT Attest: Andrew J. McMakin James Lowrey
2 CONT
2 CONT Will provided by Mary Turner Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT TURNEY HANNAH; Vol. AR0520.182, Land Ofc. Batesville, 10-JUL-48, Doc.# 2787, Cash Entry-, Part #1: NESE, Sec.14, Township, 11 N, R 12 W, 37.360 acres
2 CONT
2 CONT TURNEY, HANNAH; Vol. AR0560.094, Land Ofc. Batesville, 01-MAR-55, Doc.# 5163, Cash Entry Part #1:SENE, Sec. 14, Township, 11 N, R 12 W,40.000 acres
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1850 census she is in Sugarloaf Township, Van Buren Co., Ar  with 8 of her children, plus three Bailey grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Hannah Spurlock was born in 1796 in Washington, Virginia, her father, David, was 33, and her mother, Hannah, was 26. She married Peter A Turney and they had 18 children together. She also had two sons from another relationshi
2 CONC p. She died on September 12, 1862, in Van Buren, Arkansas, at the age of 66. Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175883078843label=@S133@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=600000017
2 CONC 5882890997label=@S402@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175883078828label=@S636@
