2 CONT ** Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZLM-LX8 FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 10 2019, 9:04:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Turney born 1815 TN was s/o Peter and Hannah  Turney - they arrived VBC AR spring 1835 from what was then Smith Co TN, later  it was Dekalb right on border with Cannon Co Tn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Fletcher Gray (Graywolf@@aol.com)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Van Buren County Ark.
2 CONT
2 CONT 244 Turney, Henry   35 M Farmer    TN
2 CONT Matilda 25 F                 Ar Isaac J  13 M                Ar  Wm A  11 M                Ar John W  9 M                Ar Peter G  7 M                Ar Joseph    1 M                Ar
2 CONT
2 CONT Look at the age of Matilda she is twenty-five. Look at the oldest child, 13 years of age. I would say that this Matilda is a second wife for Henry. I would go far as to say that Joseph is the only child of Matilda and Henry. This 
2 CONC Matilda I have no idea who she is. There are no Reavis's listed in the 1850 Census in Van Buren
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Van Buren County Giles Twp
2 CONT
2 CONT 632     640   Henry Turney,   46 M  Farmer    Tn Susan  "Polk"     33 F                  Tn   Joseph               12 M                 Ar Benjamin           10 M                Ar Charles               10 M                Ar Jaco
2 CONC b                    8 M                Ar Thos                     8 M                Ar Henry                   2 M                Ar
2 CONT
2 CONT Here in 1860 he had remarried to Susan. Joseph has shown up now as being the oldest child. The older children have moved on. Note a double set of twins. I would say the first set belong to Matilda and Henry and the Second set belo
2 CONC ngs to Susan and Henry. Confusing huh. I would look at the possibility that Susan was married to a previous Turney before Henry who knows. It will take some hard research on this one. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 Van Buren County  No listing on Henry Turney.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 Van Buren County  No listing on Henry Turney
2 CONT
