1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Residence''': Giles Township, Van Buren, Arkansas, United States - 1860
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Arkansas, United States - 1870
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Van Buren, Arkansas - 22 Dec 1880
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KLLX-D2Z FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 10 2019, 8:51:40 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT It was always thought that his middle name was Albert, but Mary Turney Miller found a reference to it being Abraham Adams, and since we recently discovered his mother’s maiden name was Adams, it makes sense.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Civil War for the Confederate Army.  It is though that he was in the 10th AR INF CAV CSA, with other members of the Turney family, where they fought in the battle of Shiloh.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was an A.A. Turney that was a Private - Age 24, Enl 30 June 1862 at Van Buren, AR.  This was in Company D 36th Arkansas Infantry Regiment of the Confederate States of America.
2 CONT
2 CONT BLM Land Records - General Land Office Records;  Homestead Cert. No. 4734, Patentee Name(s): Abraham A. Turney.  Patent issued by President Grover Cleveland was dated 01/26/1889.  Sect. 24, 11N, 12W.
2 CONT
2 CONT TURNEY, ABRAHAM A:Vol. AR0380.117, Land Ofc., Little Rock, 26-JAN-89, Doc. #4734, Misc. Doc. #11626. Homestead Original; Part #1: S NE, Sect 24, Twp 11 N, R12 W,
2 CONT -Part 2, NWSE , Sect 24, Twp 11 N, R12 W, 120.000 acres
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 25, 1864 Amanda and Abraham sold a piece of property to John M. Bailey for a sum of two hundred dollars (page 236) and On December 6, 1865 the sold anther lot to Levi Bittle for four hundred and fifty dollars (p. 240).
2 CONT
2 CONT Obit.Jan 20 1904, Arkansas Methodist
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham was in Company D commanded by McRae, under General Sterling Price, under Holmes. Price's battalion went straight through the middle against Battery C of the Union Army. Submitted by nfcarlson Source Link: https://www.geni.
2 CONC com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882890979label=@S295@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882890980label=@S304@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882890997label=@S4
2 CONC 02@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882891002label=@S461@ Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882890857label=@S311@
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Albert Turney had two sons from a previous marriage when he married Amanda Gray. They were: Tommy, who was mentally deranged and confined at home,and Little John, who was child-like.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Roy Edwin Thomas
2 CONT Abe grew up at Higden, now Cleburne Co., AR before the Civil War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:Mary Turney Miller, Berrien Springs, MI. Place of death and all of Abraham A. Turney' s ancestry from Mrs. Miller. 7/13/97, JQN. Her data came from a consensus of several Turney researchers. Abraham was buried in Turney Cem
2 CONC etery. Further data from Cleburne Co. Historical Society gives DOB 6 Nov 1832, and said Abe was buried in the Higden-McLehaney Cemetery. This is probably just an alternate name for the same cemetery named in his individual record.
2 CONC  Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175882890826label=@S33@
