1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Core Biographical Facts
2 CONT Birth: February 1808 in Washington County, Kentucky. (Some family trees incorrectly state North Carolina due to her parents' origins).
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: She was the daughter of David Mize (1785–1831) and Hannah Peters (1789–1852).
2 CONT Marriage: Married John Hunter Neely on January 24, 1839, in Illinois. (Though they married in 1839, she helped raise his older children from a previous union and bore several of her own, totaling a blended household of roughly 12 
2 CONC children).
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Passed away in 1880 in Iola, Grimes County, Texas, just a few months after her husband.Burial: She is buried alongside her husband in Zion Cemetery in Iola, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Kentucky to Illinois Move
2 CONT Her family moved from Kentucky up to Pike County, Illinois, where she met and married John after his service in the Black Hawk War.The Wagon Train to Texas: Around 1845, Lila, John, and a massive group of extended family packed th
2 CONC eir belongings into wagons and traveled southwest into the Republic/early State of Texas, settling in the wooded areas of Grimes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Records: She can be physically tracked by name on the 1850 and 1860 Federal Census records for Grimes County, Texas, where she is listed managing the household, spinning wool, and raising livestock alongside her husband
2 CONC .
2 CONT
