1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Epperson-87
2 CONT
2 CONT John Epperson was born in St. Peter's Parish in New Kent, Virginia, the son of William Epperson, and baptised on 19 Sep 1703.[1] He married Elizabeth Michaux, and they had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Epperson (1729- )
2 CONT # Elizabeth Epperson (abt.1731- )
2 CONT # David Epperson (1734-1799)
2 CONT # John Epperson (1736-1817)
2 CONT
2 CONT John died and was buried in New Kent, Virginia, in Feb 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John, son of William Epperson was baptised the 19th September, 1703.; U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900 Record ; Name: John Epperson ;Gender: male;Birth Place: VA  ;Birth Year: 1703  Spouse Name: Elizabeth ?  Numb
2 CONC er Pages: 1  ID: I4001 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: John EPPERSON Sex: M Birth: 19 SEP 1703 in New Kent Co., VA Birth: 1703 Death: 20 FEB 1736/37 in New Kent Co., VA Event: Updated 2002 Burial: FEB 1736/37
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ydna  Group - E M35 Group per FTDNA = see Avatar.https://www.geni.com/projects/E-M35-Y-DNA/10447
2 CONT
2 CONT Disconnection Needed::Elizabeth Ann Epperson born after her marriage date.Elizabeth Ann Epperson is under 12 years old for the birth of her child Susanna Epperson.Mary Epperson born after the death of her mother Elizabeth Ann Eppe
2 CONC rson.Peter Apperson born after the death of his mother Elizabeth Ann Epperson.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/218944736/john-epperson Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 12 2021, 21:00:55 UTC''
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Epperson-87
2 CONT * "The Story of David Epperson and his family of Albemarle Co, Virginia" by Brinkman page 13
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Epperson was born in St. Peter's Parish in New Kent, Virginia, the son of William Epperson, and baptised on 19 Sep 1703.[1] He married Elizabeth Michaux, and they had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Epperson (1729- )
2 CONT Elizabeth Epperson (abt.1731- )
2 CONT David Epperson (1734-1799)
2 CONT John Epperson (1736-1817)
2 CONT John died and was buried in New Kent, Virginia, in Feb 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT Many variants of the family name are encountered: Epperson, Eperson, Eppeson, Epecen, Apperson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note from John Epperson, 5 Jun 2014: The Eppersons were originally from France by way of Holland and Wales. England. When they arrived in the 'New World' They must have had atrocious accents and/ or the scribes of the time didn't 
2 CONC hear so good. Since many people didn't read or write, the name somehow got changed from Epperson to Apperson (and some scribes also left out the English double 'P').
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ St. Peter's Parish Register, p. 10.
2 CONT Brinkman, Edna E. The Story of David Epperson and his Family, of Albemarle County, Virginia. Hinsdale, IL: Edna Epperson Brinkman, 1933.
2 CONT Family Tree for John Epperson Sr. FamilySearch Family Tree database; contributed by various users.
2 CONT St. Peter's Parish Register, New Kent County, Virginia, British Colonial America. St. Peter's Episcopal Church website.
2 CONT Turman, Robert E. Genealogy Newspaper Columns of Robert E. Turman. (Ed. by Bettie Anne Cummings Cook). Evansville, IN: Tri-State Genealogical Society and Willard Library, 1981.
2 CONT Virginia Births and Christenings, 1584-1917, Christening of David Apperson, St. Peter's Parish, New Kent, Virginia, 22 Jun 1735; Birth: 27 May 1735. Father: John Apperson; Mother: Elizabeth. FamilySearch database.
2 CONT Virginia Births and Christenings, 1584-1917, Christening of John Eppeson, St. Peter's Parish, New Kent, Virginia, 19 Sep 1703. Father: Wm. Eppeson. FamilySearch database.
1 FAMS @F6000000001212537978@
