1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p14/46/87/a3/d6/534448614ad8d812/41586fb2-779a-4647-9e75-07752933fbd0_original.jpg?hash=79f85b2aaaa430e362a40430409224ea63ebe6412dfbb9e25d90a522c4d41a1f.1795075199
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL New Kent, CA flag 
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/us-va-nk.html
3 CONT
3 CONT Description of the flag
3 CONT
3 CONT I came across a photograph of the flag of New Kent County, Virginia, flying in front of the county courthouse (www.courthouses.co/wp/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/2061VM13-660x438.jpg).
3 CONT
3 CONT New Kent County is in eastern Virginia, a suburb of Richmond. It was settled in 1654 when it was separated from neighboring York County. The county got its name because the majority of the original settlers had moved there from Ke
3 CONC nt Island, Maryland, after being forced out by Lord Baltimore following the establishment of Maryland as a separate colony. Kent Island, in turn, had been named after Kent, England. (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Kent_County,_Virginia
3 CONC )
3 CONT
3 CONT The flag of New Kent County, Virginia, features the county seal centered on a white field. The seal shows a scene with a meeting between a white settler, a Native American, and a black man, originally depicted as a slave, but sinc
3 CONC e 1865 re-cast as a freeman. The scene also includes a house, and elements of the local farming and hunting economy (deer, pumpkins, wheat, etc.). Arched across the top of the seal are the words "NEW KENT COUNTY" and "ESTABLISHED 
3 CONC 1654." Arched below the scene is the county motto, "PRIDE IN THE PAST - FAITH IN THE FUTURE."
3 CONT
3 CONT Randy Young, 9 November 2014
