1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT David Epperson was born on 27 May 1734 in St. Peter's Parish. New Kent County, Virginia, the son of John Epperson and Elizabeth Michaux. He was christened on 22 Jun 1735. [1]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of David Epperson and Hannah Thompson:
2 CONT
2 CONT David Epperson - b. ca. 1753, Albemarle Co., VA; d. Oct. 1777, hospital at Valley Forge, PA, of a lingering illness; m. Judith Maupin (d. 1816; dau. of Gabriel Maupin) - Albemarle Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis / Franklin (?) Epperson - b. ca. 1756; d. Aug. 1784, of war injuries
2 CONT
2 CONT Thompson Epperson - b. 1757, Epperson Mountain, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle Co., VA; d. June 9, 1836, Franklin Co., GA; m. Mary Israel (b. ca. 1755, Albermarle Co., VA; d. Nov. 6, 1843; dau. of Michael Israel and Sarah Graves) 
2 CONC - Sept. 22, 1782, Amhearst Co., VA;
2 CONT
2 CONT James Epperson - b. Albemarle Co., VA;  m. Mary --(?); signed the Albemarle County Declaration of Independence - April 21, 1779; sold his property in Albemarle Co. - 1795
2 CONT
2 CONT John / Jonathan Epperson - b. Albemarle Co., VA;  m. Elizabeth Bowen - Dec. 22, 1788; served in 14th Virginia Regiment
2 CONT
2 CONT William Epperson - b. ca. 1762, Albemarle Co., VA; m. Nancy Hicks - June 21, 1788
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert / Robin(?) Epperson - m. Lucy Oberlick - March 1805, Madison Co., KY
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Epperson - b. July 14, 1766, Albemarle Co., VA; d. Dec. 15, 1852, Oxford, IL;  m. Sarah Lamb Love (b. March 10, 1772, VA;  d. April 23, 1853, Oxford, IL)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Epperson - m. James Gardner
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Epperson - m. William Beauchamp Proctor
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Epperson - m. Jonathan Langford (1st cousin; son of Thomas Langford and Elizabeth Thompson)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Epperson - m. --(?) Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Jane Epperson - m. John Burch / Burke - Jan. 17, 1786
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of David Epperson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Albemarle County, VA Will Book 4; p. 33.
2 CONT
2 CONT transcribed by Mchael Vaughn Sims May 19, 2002 
2 CONT
2 CONT from a photocopy made by Doris Sketoe July 1982 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God, amen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I David Epperson of Virginia and County Albemarle, being through the mercy of God of sound mind and memory, do make appoint constitute and ordain this my last will and testament and desire it to be received by all as such. Imprimi
2 CONC s my soul I humbly bequeath to God who gave it me. My body I commit to the earth from whence it was taken to be decently buried at the discretion of my Executrix and executors hereafter mentioned.   My will is and I positively ord
2 CONC er that all my just debts and funeral expenses be paid out of my estate, my will is and I desire that my estate be neither appraised nor sold.  Item the 1st I lend unto my beloved wife all my estate real and personal during her na
2 CONC tural life.  Item the 2nd I give and bequeath unto my son Charles Epperson his heirs and assigns forever one half of my land so as to include the mantion [sic] spot whereon I now live.  Item I give and bequeath unto my son John Ep
2 CONC person his heirs and assigns forever the other half of my land.  Item 3d  I give unto my eleven children, viz, Robert, James, Thompson, William, John, and Charles Epperson, Judith Gardner, Elizabeth Proctor, Susanna Langford, Hann
2 CONC ah Freeman and Lucy Burke to them and their heirs and assigns forever, all my stock of every kind whatsoever and household and [kitchen?] furniture together with the rest of my estate whatsoever not heretofore divided to be equall
2 CONC y divided among them.  Lastly I do nominate and appoint my wife Hannah Epperson Executrix James Epperson and Jonathan Langford Executors of this my last will and testament.  In witness whereof I hereunto set my hand and seal this 
2 CONC twenty 2 day of February one thousand seven hundred and ninety nine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed, sealed and delivered 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the presence of Test. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hall 				David Epperson (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Hall 				his D mark
2 CONT
2 CONT Candis Hall 
2 CONT
2 CONT At Albemarle October Court 1799 
2 CONT
2 CONT This last will and testament of David Epperson dec’d. was produced unto court and proved by the oathes of John Hall Nathan Hall and Candis Hall witnesses thereto and ordered to be recorded. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Test. John Nicholas [Clerk? / Cal? / C. C. O?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Pursuant to the above order with under written commissioners did on this tenth day of Sept. 1799 proceed to divide the lands of [rest cut off by photocopy] 
2 CONT ----
