2 CONT Chronology of David Epperson / Apperson by Michael Vaughn Sims
2 CONT
2 CONT 1734 Born - May 27, 1734, New Kent County, VA; son of John Epperson and Elizabeth --(?)1 Baptized - June 22, 1734, Saint Peter’s Parish, New Kent County, VA2
2 CONT
2 CONT 1753 Married Hannah Thompson (b. ca. 1735; dau. of Robert Thompson 3) - ca. 1753, Albemarle County, VA Settled in Saint Anne’s Parish (later Fredericksville Parish), Albemarle County, VA located twenty miles southwest of Charlotte
2 CONC sville, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned a large plantation of one of the Blue Ridge Mountains of Virginia, which was called Epperson Mountain
2 CONT
2 CONT 1757 Birth of son Thompson Epperson - 1757, Epperson Mountain, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1776 Signed Dissenters’ Petition - 1776, Albemarle County, VA; petition made by colonists who wanted to be free from the Church of England Volunteered service in the 14th Virginia Regiment; volunteered for two months, returned hom
2 CONC e, then enlisted again Provided financial support to other volunteers who otherwise could not have entered military service without leaving their families destitute
2 CONT
2 CONT 1784 Received by bequeath all the property of son Francis Epperson
2 CONT
2 CONT 1784; viz - one mare, saddle and bridle, one crop of corn, two crops of tobacco See Will of Francis Epperson Provided lodging for the the circuit riding minister of Saint Anne’s Parish
2 CONT
2 CONT 1799 Died - October / December 1799, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA; buried Epperson family cemetery, Epperson Mountain, Albemarle County, VA At the time of his death, David Epperson and his children ownded a combined a
2 CONC creage of 1,400 acres on and bordering Epperson Mountain, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1800 Son John Epperson sold Epperson farm to James Durrett - 180016 David Epperson’s home and farm appear to have become part of the Blue Ridge Farm of Greenwood, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1802 Widow Hannah Thompson Epperson moved to Hawkins County, TN with son Charles Epperson
2 CONT
2 CONT 1814 Death of widow Hannah Thompson Epperson - ca. 1814, Richmond, KY
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Jun. 22, 1734 New Kent County Virginia, USA Death: Dec., 1799 Albemarle County Virginia, USA
2 CONT
