2 CONT David Epperson / Apperson  (1734-1799)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1734        Born - May 27, 1734, New Kent County, VA; son of John Epperson and Elizabeth --(?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized - June 22, 1734, Saint Peter’s Parish, New Kent County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1753        Married Hannah Thompson (b. ca. 1735; dau. of Robert Thompson) - ca. 1753, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled in Saint Anne’s Parish (later Fredericksville Parish), Albemarle County, VA located twenty miles southwest of Charlottesville, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned a large plantation of one of the Blue Ridge Mountains of Virginia, which was called Epperson Mountain
2 CONT
2 CONT 1757        Birth of son Thompson Epperson - 1757, Epperson Mountain, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1776        Signed Dissenters’ Petition - 1776, Albemarle County, VA; petition made by colonists who wanted to be free from the Church of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Volunteered service in the 14th Virginia Regiment; volunteered for two months, returned home, then enlisted again
2 CONT
2 CONT Provided financial support to other volunteers who otherwise could not have entered military service without leaving their families destitute
2 CONT
2 CONT 1784       Received by bequeath all the property of son Francis Epperson - ca. 1784; viz - one mare, saddle and bridle, one crop of corn, two crops of tobacco
2 CONT
2 CONT Provided lodging for the the circuit riding minister of Saint Anne’s Parish
2 CONT
2 CONT 1799        Died - October / December 1799, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA; buried Epperson family cemetery, Epperson Mountain, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of his death, David Epperson and his children ownded a combined acreage of 1,400 acres on and bordering Epperson Mountain, Saint Anne’s Parish, Albemarle County, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1802        Widow Hannah Thompson Epperson moved to Hawkins County, TN with son Charles Epperson - ca. 1802
2 CONT
2 CONT 1800        Son John Epperson sold Epperson farm to James Durrett - 1800
2 CONT
2 CONT David Epperson’s home and farm appear to have become part of the Blue Ridge Farm of Greenwood, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 1814        Death of widow Hannah Thompson Epperson - ca. 1814, Richmond, KY
