1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NORTH CAROLINA  with the rank of PRIVATE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A019107  DAR Ancestor # A019107]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Perrin Cardwell - Born 22 Dec 1751 in Virginia, son of Richard and Susannah ( Le Grand) Cardwell, died 25 Jun 1790 in Rockingham County, NC; married ca 1772 Rebecca <nowiki>------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT As a resident of Guilford Co., NC, Richard Perrin Cardwell served in the North Carolina Militia as a Private under Captain Alexander Hunter, Lieut John Davis and Ensign Samuel Hunter in the regiment of Lt Col James Martin on the 2
2 CONC nd Expedition to Cross Creek. Cross Creek was a port established at the head of the navigation of Cape Fear River that was combined with Campbellton in 1783 to become the town of Fayetteville, NC in Cumberland Co. [Ref: Revolution
2 CONC ary Army Accounts, Vol 50, pages 253, 255, 256: Division of Archives and Histiry, Raleigh, NC]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Perrin Cardwell first received land grants in Guilforf Co., NC in 1782 which included 400 acres between the Mayo River and Beaver Island Creek in the section of Guilford that became Rockingham Co in Dec 1785. He evidently 
2 CONC lived on the land for some time while the grant was being processed. A certified copy of records in the "Day Book" kept by his father, provided the dates for Richard Perrin and five children born to him and Rebecca. In 1966, the "
2 CONC Day Book" was owned by Glenn Davis of Royse City, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Ann Cardwell, born 10 Dec 1773
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Jonathan (Nathan) Cardwell, born 11 Sep 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sarah Cardwell, born 11 Dec 1777
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Joel Cardwell, born 17 Oct 1779, died 27 Dec 1847 Rockingham Co: married 4 Mar 1808 (MB) Rockingham Co, NC, Mariah Henrietta Scales, born 5 Mar 1779, died 18 June 1860, dau of James and Henrietta (Phillips) Scales. Joel and Mar
2 CONC iah Cardwell are buried in a family cemetery near the town of Mayodan in Rockingham Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Susannah Cardwell, born 1 Sep 1783
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Private in the North Carolina Militia during the American Revolutionary War
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
