1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please don't add Find-a-grave, many duplicates, and no correct information. Not correct graves or the location or the Church they attended.  Be careful with online ancestry trees, at this point, they're mixed up. W
2 CONC e  must review the Probated Wills only Please-
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Lucy LeGrand''' was born on December 15, 1742, in Goochland County, Virginia. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34724168367 William Walker] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-103934609 Judith Walker]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy married [https://www.geni.com/profile-17346136 Alexander , LeGrand, Sr.] on November 23, 1757 in Cumberland, Virginia, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34653217283 Judith Ann Fitch];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568186 Josiah LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-17345392 Baker LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-2751701 Margaretta Drusilla Lancaster (LeGrand)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568306 Alexander Legrand, Jr.];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568317 Jane LeGrand];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568318 Susan Woodson];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568322 Lucy Cox];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568324 Nancy Snead Binford];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-35568326 Sarah Wilson]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on October 15, 1825, in Cumberland County, Virginia, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes indicate Clover Hill Cemetery in Cumberland County.  Placing a memorial with her father in Whitehall Plantation Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
