2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.findagrave.com/cemetery/2593833/saunders-cunningham-alexander-cemetery]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Behind the garden and across "Dry Creek" is the graveyard where lie Major William Cunningham (Revolutionary Aide-de-camp to General Washington) and his daughter Nancy. Nearby are the graves of Colonel William Saunders, an officer
2 CONC  in the Revolution and a member from North Carolina of the Society of the Cincinnati, and Major Richard Alexander, an officer under Jackson in the war of 1812."
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Nancy Saunders Alexander (Cunningham)''' was born on December 27, 1777, in Sumner Co., TN. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762425026 William Cunningham] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762425027 Elizabeth W
2 CONC atkins]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy married husband 1)  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34692493495 Capt William Saunders] on January 13, 1795, in Caswell, North Carolina. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762423701 Ethelbert Watkins Saunders]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34747683136 Lafayette Saunders Judge]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy married husband 2)  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762425183 Maj. Richard Brandon Alexander] on February 28, 1808, in Smith, Tennessee, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762425185 Elizabeth W Alexander];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762425184 Richard Cunningham Alexander]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on December 1, 1839, in Smith Co, TN.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/159244897/nancy-c_-alexander Find A Grave Memorial] - 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
