1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=77125208
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH OLIVER MINTER was born circa 1750 in Virginia to John Oliver Minter & Elizabeth Michaux Morgan-Minter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph married Frances "Fanny" Hill-Minter circa 1784 in Chatham County, North Carolina, and they had EIGHT children that are known of: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abner Hill Minter (1785-1855),  John Morgan Minter (1792-1856),  Thomas John Minter (1794-1825),  Mary Minter-Farrar (1797-1877),  Elizabeth Minter-May (1800-1822),  Frances "Fanny" Minter-Hawkins (1802-1861),  Sarah Minter (1803-
2 CONC 1806), &  Hanna Minter-Farrar (1804-1843).
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph passed away in February of 1823 near Haywood, Chattham County, North Carolina, and was buried in The Minter Family Cemetery on their plantation property located at Haw River Township near the intersection of the Haw & Deep 
2 CONC Rivers, in the proximity of present day Moncure, Chatham County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT REFERENCES:
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL: 1. North Carolina State Archives, 1823, Will Book B, Joseph Oliver Minter, p. 108, Chatham County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: 1. 29 May 1932, Atlanta Georgia Newspaper, "People Who Think," GENEALOGY DEPARTMENT; Minters, and inter-Married Lines, Were Pioneers in Early Georgia History, by Lilla Odem - Reference to Joseph's Will; probated May 1823, o
2 CONC n record at Pittsboro, Chatham County, North Carolina.
2 CONT
