0 @I6000000063460189840@ INDI
1 NAME N.N.
2 GIVN N.N.
2 NICK Cleopatre
1 NAME Mother of Nicketti
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Leona M. Simonini claimed this (name unknown) woman was the daughter of  https://www.geni.com/people/Cleopatra-of-the-Powhatan/6000000000437769381?through=6000000063506039822 by her uncle, https://www.geni.com/peop
2 CONC le/Opechancanough-paramount-chief-of-the-Powhatan/6000000005937340015?through=6000000063460189840, and that she had a daughter Nicketti by a chieftain of the Cayugas tribe.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Historian Helen C. Rountree wrote:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Princess Nicketti is the name given to a Virginia Indian woman believed by some to have been the daughter of Opechancanough, a leader of the Powhatan Indians and the brother of the paramount chief Powhatan. While the name has bee
2 CONC n referenced almost exclusively on twenty-first-century genealogy websites by people claiming family relationship, no scholarly evidence exists that Princess Nicketti ever lived. A careful search of seventeenth-century records in 
2 CONC Virginia yields no one by that name, male or female. And no name of a child of Opechancanough was ever recorded in that century. The writings about her stem from a single published source: Alexander Brown's genealogy The Cabells a
2 CONC nd Their Kin (1939). Significantly, Brown calls Nicketti's story only a "very interesting tradition" and adds, "I cannot vouch for it[s accuracy]," but he had heard about her from several prominent Piedmont Virginia families. Subs
2 CONC equent writers have quoted Brown's text as fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * an alternate ancestry of Nicketti proposed here: Vest, Jay Hansford C. "Mormons and Indians in Central Virginia: J. Golden Kimball and the Mason Family's Native American Origins." Journal of Mormon History 40, no. 3 (2014): 127-
2 CONC 54. http://www.jstor.org/stable/24243806 [https://s3.amazonaws.com/photos.geni.com/p13/11/00/8a/24/53444848bd3aa5c1/433e7b62-ab35-4e1e-9383-df2a85109f66_original.jpg link to page 134]
2 CONT * https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=stevensp&id=I00715 cites Leona M. Simonini and calls her “Granddaughter and Niece of Chief Powhatan”
2 CONT
2 CONT *Rountree, Helen C. The Powhatan Indians of Virginia: Their Traditional Culture. Norman: University of Oklahoma Press, 1989. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Brown, Alexander. The Cabells and Their Kin. Richmond, Va.: Garrett and Massie, Inc., 1939. 
2 CONT * Biographical Genealogies of the Kentucky-Virginia Floyd Families, N. J. Floyd, 1912
