2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War Militia Officer, Frontiersman. Early figure in establishing Kentucky settlements; In July 1776 helped rescue three young girls kidnapped by Indians from Boonesborough, Virginia (later Kentucky) in group led by Da
2 CONC niel Boone. Commanded militia regiment for George Rogers Clark against British allied Indians in Ohio in the summer of 1780. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Killed in ambush by Indians. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son John Floyd and grandson John both became governors of Virginia. (bio by: Mike Maloney) 
