2 NOTE  A few things i keep in mind, that needs read a little closer.. of Col. J John Floyd, may. 1774. two NA, in a canoe holding passes from the commandant at Fort Pitt, came to warn him, and his men. that a war was on between whites, 
3 CONC and Shawnees, telling him and his men of a frightfull massacre, that had taken place. half of Floyds men wnt bck home, he stayed. even tho the NA gave news. Floyd himself pushed on giving concerns,, settlements were ruining ,hunti
3 CONC ng grounds.. of the Tawas, and Kickapoos.. All this has been found in his journals. and letters written. he wrote his boss Preston, of the failure of the Virginia convention, to take proper steps for the protection, of frontiers, 
3 CONC and regulation, of land sales.. And of the Pernicious activity,of Jack Jones,(GABRIEL JONES) who was head of the Harrodsburg banditti, of the Bryans, and other Tories.. 65 years, after he did this John Morehead, gave a Famous Addr
3 CONC ess, as follows...
3 CONT
3 CONT Alternatly a surveyor, a legislator, and a soldier, his distinguished qualities rendered him at once an ornament and a benefactor of the infant settlements. no individual among the early pioneers was more intelligent or better inf
3 CONC ormed more displayed on all occasions that called for it. had a bolder or more undaunted courage. his person was singularly attractive with complexion unusually dark, his eyes and hair were deep black and his tall spare figure was
3 CONC  dignified by the accomplishments of a well bred virginia gentlemen connecting himself to his company their principal surveyor. ( Floyd co. KY. named for him, Floyd river, Floyd park, etc.. If he would of been on his favorite Hors
3 CONC e Pompey(little chief) he would of lived that day.
