2 NOTE James John Floyd, better known as John Floyd (1750 – April 10, 1783), was a pioneer of the Midwestern United States around the Louisville, Kentucky area where he worked as a surveyor for land development and as a military figure. 
3 CONC  Floyd was an early settler of St. Matthews, Kentucky and helped lay out Louisville. In Kentucky he served as a Colonel of the Kentucky Militia in which he participated in raids with George Rogers Clark and later became one of the
3 CONC  first judges of Kentucky.
