2 CONT Notes for JEMIMA FLOYD:
2 CONT
2 CONT From B. Frank Reinauer III: Jemima Floyd appears to be one of Col. John Floyd's younger sisters. Anna M. Cartlidge gives her year of birth as 1753 (in Virginia). She married (1)ca. 1769, John Lemaster (b. ca. 1749; died 16 Sep 178
2 CONC 1 -- during Floyd's defeat); (2) bond posted 28 May 1784, Jefferson County, KY, James A'Sturgus, Jr. (b. ca. 1760; lived 1810 in Bullitt County, KY according to the census) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Jo Lee Brooks Potts, <Jo0608@aol.com>, writes in June 2001: " Dear Pat, Thank you for your website. I am a descendant of Jemima Floyd. Thank you." I asked her for corrections or additions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From Alex Luken: "Pat-- Jo Nell sent me this from something called the Lemaster book... 'I found them.... see the Lemaster book page 83. Issue 70 Eleazer Lemaster b abt 1749 d Sept 16-22, 1781 near Louisville, Ky., killed by India
2 CONC ns m abt 1768 Jemima Floyd b 1753 Amherst Co. Va. After the death of Eleazer Lemaster she m2 in Jefferson Co., Ky., May 28, 1784 James A' Sturgus Jr. by whom she has issue: Cynthia A'Sturgus who m Jan 23 1800 William Pope. Jemima 
2 CONC Lemaster received land grant of 400 acres on Beech Fork, Jefferson, Co. Ky May 10 1784.' " 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT This 400 acres might be the same as referenced here (courtesy of Alex Luken): 
2 CONT
2 CONT "At a Court held for Jefferson County, the 3rd of December, 1781. It appearing to the Court that the following Persons, are entitled by virtue of an Act of Assembly passed May last, to four hundred acres of land, each. Orders that
2 CONC  the County Surveyor lay off to them accordingly, viz: (among the many names listed is Jemima Lemaster)" 
2 CONT
