1 OCCU Planter
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nicholas Cabell''', son of William Cabell, MD and Elizabeth burks, was born October 29, 1750 in Goochland County, Virginia, and died at Liberty Hall Plantation, Amherst County, Virginia, on August 18, 1803. He i
2 CONC s buried near his father in the Liberty Hall Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas was a student at William and Mary College in Williamsburg in the years leading up to the American Revolution. He left school in 1775 and accepted a commission in 1776 as captain in the militia. He organized a company of M
2 CONC inute Men in Amherst County, leading them down the James River towards Williamsburg. In July 1778, he was promoted to lieutenant colonel and given the task of recruiting more militia. In 1779, he was elected to the General Assembl
2 CONC y, which started a twenty-year career in state politics. In 1780, he was promoted to full colonel of the militia and given command of the First Battalion. This battalion was present when Cornwallis surrendered at Yorktown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas married Hannah Carrington in 1772. Hannah was the daughter of George Carrington and wife Ann Mayo. She was born in 1751 in Cumberland County, Virginia and died in 1817 in Nelson County, Virginia.  The couple had eleven ch
2 CONC ildren, seven of whom reached adulthood. Nicholas and Hannah are both buried at Liberty Hill Cemetery, Warminster, Nelson County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas, being the youngest surviving son, had not received as much land as gifts from his father. At his father's death, however, the home plantation "Swan Creek," and the remaining Cabell land in Buckingham and Amherst counties
2 CONC  became his. Nicholas continued to improve and enlarge the plantation house. During the Revolutionary War, he renamed the plantation "Liberty Hill." The house burned to the ground c.1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Nicholas Cabell and wife Hannah Carrington:
2 CONT * Gov. William H. Cabell, 1772-1853, married (1) his cousin Elizabeth Cabell and (2) Agnes S. B. Gambell. 
2 CONT * George Cabell, MD, 1774-1837
2 CONT * Frederick Cabell, 1775-1841
2 CONT * Elizabeth Cabell, 1776-1892
2 CONT * Joseph Carrington Cabell, 1778-1856
2 CONT * Nicholas Cabell, Jr., 1780-1809
2 CONT * Mary Anne Cabell, 1783-1850
2 CONT * Hannah Cabell, 1786-1794
2 CONT * Henningham Cabell, 1787-1794
2 CONT * Paul Carrington Cabell, 1791-1791
2 CONT * Mayo Carrington Cabell, 1794-1794
2 CONT * 
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT *http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Cabell&GSiman=1&GSst=48&GSsr=201&GRid=123733478&
2 CONT *http://www.cabell.com/libertyhall.html
2 CONT *http://www2.lib.virginia.edu/small/collections/cabell/biographies/nicholas.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
