1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obadiah Smith was the son of Luke Smith and Arabella Gromarrin. He married Mary Burks, daughter of Samuel Burks and Mary Davis. He was born c.1700 in Virginia. They had eight children. He was named as one of the ex
2 CONC ecutors of his father-in-law's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obadiah’s will can be found in Chesterfield County, Va. Wills 1774-1802. The will is dated January 2, 1777. Wife Mary is not mentioned, so we assume she died before then. Several children and grandchildren are named. He bequeaths 
2 CONC property in Chesterfiled County, Virginia, in Mecklenburg County, North Carolina, and a plot along Moss Creek near the James River, which is probably in Henrico County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Obiadiah Smith and Mary Burks
2 CONT *William Smith
2 CONT *Susanna Smith
2 CONT *Lucy Smith
2 CONT *Obadiah Smith Jr.
2 CONT *Luke Smith
2 CONT *Peartree Smith
2 CONT *Elizabeth Smith
2 CONT *Joseph Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT *http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~brookefamily/smithobadiah.htm 
2 CONT *http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~harrisonrep/Harrison/d0076/g0000067.html#I12349
2 CONT *http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/cocke/834/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will of Obadiah Smith===
2 CONT
2 CONT To Grandson Obediah Smith, son of my son Peartree, all of my land in Mecklenburg County, where son Peartree lives, but his father and mother to have use of land and Negroes for life, and if he dies, to be divided among his sisters
2 CONC .
2 CONT To Granddaughter Elizabeth Smith, 1 Negro and increase except one boy given to my grandson Obediah. To son William, all my land on James River above Mosses [Moss's] Creek on road that goes from Anderson Britton's to Buckingham Roa
2 CONC d and along Jommy (sic) Winters Branch, to Powhite Creek, including land bought from Abram Cowley. To son Obediah, all rest of Chesterfield land, being plantation I live on. If sons William and Obediah die without heirs, then to m
2 CONC y duaghter Lucy Smith. To son William, all land at mouth of Hics and Dan Rivers. To son Obediah, my land in North Carolina To daughter Lucy Smith, 2 Negroes To Eadith Christmas, 3 Negroes, furniture and 100 pounds, with negroes to
2 CONC  go to my estate after her death To grandaughter Elizabeth Winston, 1 negro and 100 pounds To son Peartree, 250 pounds and a bed. Rest to sons Wiliam and Obediah and daughter Lucy. Exors: friends Drury Smith, Robert Jones, David P
2 CONC atteson, Samuel Price, William Scott, Jr., Anderson Britton and sons William Smith and Obediah Smith. Dated 2 January 1777 Wit: Benskin Easley, Ann Duvall, Lucy Smith, Martin Googer and Charles Clarke, Jr.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L856-99C FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 19 2020, 0:33:40 UTC''
