1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/168671109/john_peartree-burk
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Denell Burks email: DB1776@aol.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Basil M. Burks, Jr., 3056 Killarney Dr., Pace, FL 32571,
2 CONT 904-994-2019
2 CONT
2 CONT Brenda Watson, Rt. 1, Box 134x, Monroe, VA 24574 dated July 22,
2 CONT 1996. She is descended through Sam ISam IIDavid Burks through
2 CONT his son John. Email = BCWatson@aol.com. The packet of
2 CONT information Brenda Watson sent to Denell contained: the
2 CONT Burks/Davis genealogy of Nicketti given by Frank Wellington's
2 CONT dau, Mary Wheat Burks Dean (819 Peaksview, Bedford, VA 24523,
2 CONT April 15, 1980). She is the researcher of this Burks genealogy,
2 CONT which was begun by her mother. It is supplemented by
2 CONT information from Faye S. Poss, 471 Mimosa Drive NW., Tucker, GA
2 CONT 30084. Faye Poss is researching the Burks who migrated to GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burks-42
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peartree Burks, b. ca.1716 in Albemarle County, Virginia
2 CONT Sarah Isham, b. ca. 1737 in Albemarle County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT John Burks owned land in Bedford and Amherst Counties in Virginia before moving his family to Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT Circa 1792, John Burks and his family moved from Amherst Co., VA to the part of Green Co., KY that became Barren Co. in 1799.[2] He settled at Blue Spring Grove near present-day Hiseville, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tavern Keeper
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1799, one of the first acts of the newly created Barren County, Kentucky, was to authorize John Burks to operate a tavern at his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Public Service
2 CONT
2 CONT In those early days of the county, John Burks was ordered several times to perform such functions as to view the location of roads to be built in the new sparsely-settled county.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Married about ?1769, probably in Botetourt County, Virginia, to Mary Kendrick??, born about ?1755 in Bedford Co., Virginia, and died ?about 1834 in Barren Co., Kentucky, daughter of John Kendrick and Elizabeth Preston
2 CONT
2 CONT ?
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Silas Burks, b. ca.1772 in Virginia
2 CONT Elizabeth Burks, b. 1775 in Henry Co., Virginia
2 CONT Nancy Burks, b. ca.1777 in Virginia
2 CONT John Burks, b. 14 Jul 1779 in Henry, Amherst Co., Kentucky
2 CONT Mary Elizabeth Burks, b: ca.1781 in Virginia
2 CONT Sally Burks, 1783 in Virginia
2 CONT Thomas Burks, b. ca.1785 in Virginia
2 CONT Catherine V Burks, b. 24 Feb 1792 in Virginia
2 CONT Rachel Burks, b. 4 Feb 1794 in Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT All the above were named in John's estate settlement, with the exception of Nancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Doubtful Children (found in some family trees, but not linked to this family):
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lyon Burks?? (undocumented), born ?18 Apr 1791 Edgefield Co, South Carolina or Lincoln Co, GA, died ?09 May 1866 Damascus, Scott County, Mississippi?, 75 years
2 CONT Josiah Burk, born ?c1762 Wythe County, Virginia, United States, died ?1816 Barren County, Kentucky
2 CONT Isham Burks?? (actually a brother), born ?24 Oct 1761 Amherst, Amherst, Virginia, United States, died ?21 Aug 1839 McNairy, Tennessee, United States?, 77 years
2 CONT Benjamin Burke??, born ?1765 Virginia, died ?1828, Wayne County, Kentucky,
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT No Will has been found for John Burks but a record of his Estate Settlement can be found in Barren County, Kentucky, Will Book 2, pp. 490-499 (FHL Film 209,740)[3]
2 CONT Excerpt:
2 CONT
2 CONT This is to certify that we John Burks for myself and also for Silas Burks, Elizabeth Payton, James Jameson, Thomas Edwards, John Jameson, Thomas Burks & George Hardy, Heirs and Representatives of John Burks Dec., do agree that the
2 CONC  commissioners to settle our Fathers Estate (to wit) Isaac Wren, William Twyman, James Jolliff & Isaac M. Roberts shall report to the Barren County Court for record....
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Record
2 CONT
2 CONT William Allen and Rachel, his wife, vs. Kindrick--O.S. 94; N. S. 32--Bill, 2d August, 1805. Rachel is daughter of John Kindrick, late of Washington County. She and William were married in 177_, and lived in Botetourt until 1782, w
2 CONC hen John came and invited them to come to Washington, where he promised them a piece of land, for which they sue. Rachel had a brother, John. John Kendrick, Sr., died 1800 or 1801, intestate, leaving a large family, which descende
2 CONC d to Thomas and John Kendrick, Mary Kendrick, who married John Burks, and Rachel.[4]
