2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/89215234/person/260085389933 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 18 2022, 14:51:02 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT David Burke, born c1746, was in Amherst County, Virginia during the Revolution and provided supplies. He died in Amherst County on 19 May 1828.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT David had at least three children:
2 CONT # Richard Burke (died Amherst County before 20 November 1833), married Elizabeth Roach[1]
2 CONT # Charles Burke, married Mary Burks[1]
2 CONT # Obedience Burke, married William Roach[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard and Obedience married siblings Elizabeth and William Roach.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: David's birth is shown as 1746 in his main DAR record. However, a descendant record (for his son Charles) has David born 1736 and son Charles born 1757. Charles, born 1757, also has a DAR record, which shows his birth as Al
2 CONC bemarle County, Virginia (died before 19 May 1819 in Amherst County), married Mary Burks (b 1760). Jane, daughter of Charles and Mary, also married a Burks (Samuel, b c1784 in Amherst).[3]
2 CONT The father of the groom of this marriage? "Virginia Marriages, 1785-1940," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XRDN-6V4 : 5 December 2014), David Burks in entry for David Burks Jr. and Betsey Phillips T
2 CONC homas, 01 Oct 1799; citing Amherst County, Virginia, reference 135; FHL microfilm 30,273.
2 CONT DAR record for David (#A017293) does not show any name for his wife.[1]
2 CONT Location Notes
2 CONT Albemarle/Amherst Counties: Albemarle was formed in 1744; in 1761, Amherst was formed from Albemarle.[4]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 Daughters of the American Revolution, DAR Genealogical Research Databases, database online, (http://www.dar.org/ : accessed 30 September 2017), "Record of David Burke", Ancestor # A017293.
2 CONT # Descendant record of David Burke's son Richard
2 CONT # ↑ 2.0 2.1 Daughters of the American Revolution, DAR Genealogical Research Databases, database online, (http://www.dar.org/ : accessed 3 October 2017), "Record of Ashcraft Roach", Ancestor # A096545.
2 CONT # Descendant record of Aschcraft Roach's daughter Elizabeth
2 CONT # ↑ Daughters of the American Revolution, DAR Genealogical Research Databases, database online, (http://www.dar.org/ : accessed 3 October 2017), "Record of Charles Burke", Ancestor # A017292.
2 CONT # ↑ History of County Formations in Virginia 1617-1995
2 CONT
