1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Frances "Fanny" Houl''' was the daughter of Frances Bassett from a first marriage. The only thing known about her father is the surname Houl. She was born before 1699 in New Kent County, Virginia. (We know this 
2 CONC because her mother married Mr Horsley in 1699.) Soon after Fanny's birth, her mother married Robert Horsley of York County. Fanny was raised as a Horsley child and was left an inheritance by her stepfather. She died on July 12, 17
2 CONC 53 in Albemarle County, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fanny married Richard Burks in 1739. There are two documented children of this marriage - sons Roland and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fanny's date of birth is estimated from her step-father's will. She would have been the eldest child of the household. At Robert Horsley's death, none of his children were required to have a guardian named. This means that the dau
2 CONC ghters were at least age 18 and the sons at least age 21.
2 CONT
