1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Roland Horsley Burks''' was the son of Richard Burks and Frances Horsley. He was born c.1740 to c.1745 in Virginia, possibly in Lunenburg County. He died in c.1806 in Floyd County, Kentucky. He married Sarah (po
2 CONC ssibly Randolph). Only one child has been proven to be his. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lunenburg is possibly the place of birth because many sites claim he was born in Bedford County. That county was formed ten years after his birth, from a portion of Lunenburg. As the details of his father's later life are largely 
2 CONC unknown, it is difficult to say if the family lived in Lunenburg County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roland is often confused with a Richard Birkes of Shenandoah area of Virginia because of similar last names and similar dates. Roland married Sarah while Richard married Mary Rhoda Pipes. Roland died in Kentucky while Richard died
2 CONC  in Illinois. The children of Richard are often attributed to Roland. If the name is spelled with "i" and not "u," it is most likely not a child of Roland and Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Burks and Frances Horsley were married in 1739 and Roland Horsley Burks was born to this union sometime about 1740 - 1742. He is listed on a roster of 1758 (French and Indian War?) soldiers from Bedford County along with R
2 CONC ichard, Richard Jr., William and a John Patrick (?Partree) Burks. However, the name is spelled Bolling which is unquestionably an error in the transcription of an "R" to a "B." No other records of the area ever mentions a Bolling 
2 CONC Burks, but the Bolling family was in the area. Alexander Sayers did specify "Roland" as noted below.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Randolph Burks, born c.1765 in Pendleton, South Carolina, is most likely NOT the son of Roland Horsley Burks. There is no evidence supporting Roland ever being in South Carolina.  He is frequently placed as a son of Roland be
2 CONC cause of the middle name Randolph and the possibility that Roland Burks' wife Sarah may have been a Randolph. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Roland Horsley Burks and wife Sarah:
2 CONT *David Burks, 1770-1775, born in Virginia and died in Floyd County, Kentucky, married Rebecca Duncan
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT *http://www.jillandfamily.com/genealogy/showsource.php?sourceID=S523&tree=jilltree
