1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Huddleston-1335
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103639436/abraham-huddleston
2 CONT There isn't any definite proof of where Abraham is buried, but his land was right on the south side of Thomasville, very near Bellah Cemetery and Thomas/Lasley Cemetery (now defunct), so if he had a cemetery burial, it might have 
2 CONC been in one of these cemeteries. It's likely that this is the closest we will get to where he was actually buried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham was the son of William Huddleston and Martha Myer(s). William moved from Bucks Co, PA to Bedford Co, VA in 1770, three years before Abraham was born. 
2 CONT Abe married March 5, 1793 in Bedford Co., Va to Mary Allen. Some of his family moved to Kanawha Co., (W)Va. 
2 CONT About 1794 Abe moved to Smith Co., Tn, probably with his brother Henry [sic] and sister Polly. Then about 1818/19 Abe and his children moved on to Pope Co, IL. They were there in 1820, but didn't stay long.
2 CONT By Oct 6, 1821 Abe and family had moved south to the Missouri Ozarks, being one of the first four white families who settled in the area around Thomasville (the others were Smith, Thomas and Perkins). This area was originally part
2 CONC  of Wayne Co. In 1833 it became Ripley Co., and in 1845 it became Oregon Co. and Thomasville was the original county seat. In 1859 (the year after he died) the county seat moved to Alton.
2 CONT This area where he and his sons, a sister, and a few nieces and nephews lived was in 1858 called the Huddleston settlement. It was on the Eleven Point River, three miles 
2 CONT "below" Thomasville (probably east as the river runs). Abe outlived all but four of his twelve children (Nancy, Charles, Abraham, Jr. and Benjamin). Abraham had ten sons and many descendants are still in the county today.
2 CONT I wonder if there was some kind of epidemic at his death. His son Joseph died 6 weeks before him, and son Abraham, Jr died three days after him. 1857-59 had one of the largest worldwide outbreaks of influenza, but I wonder if it c
2 CONC ould have reached Oregon County.
2 CONT No burials places are known for any of his children, though it's likely they were all buried in the same cemetery.
2 CONT Bio by Mary Jo Freeman
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/ftm/d/a/v/Kathy-S-Davis/GENE2-0004.html
2 CONT 8.ABRAHAM H.9 HUDDLESTON (WILLIAM8, HENRY II7, HENRY I6, RICHARD5, HENRY4, HENRY3, EDMUND2, JOHN1) was born 1773 in Bucks Co., Pennsylvania, and died February 1, 1858 in Oregon Co., Missouri.He married MARY ALLEN March 5, 1793 in 
2 CONC Bedford Co., Virginia.She was born 1777 in Bedford County, Virginia, and died Aft. 1850 in Ripley Co., Missouri2.
2 CONT Notes for ABRAHAM H. HUDDLESTON:
2 CONT The Wayne Co., MO census shows Abraham aged between 50 and 60. Joseph between 30 and 40, Nathan, Charles, Israel, and John all between 20 and 30, as heads of families.
2 CONT Wayne County-1830 CensusMO
2 CONT p46Huddleston, Abraham      50-60      1770-1780     1 m            10-15      1815-1820
2 CONT      1 m            15-20      1810-1815     
2 CONT 1 m            15-20      1810-1815     
2 CONT 1 m            15-20      1810-1815
2 CONT      1 m            20-30      1800-1810     
2 CONT 1 fm            10-15      1815-1820     
2 CONT 1 fm            50-60      1770-1780
2 CONT *****************
2 CONT 1840 HUDDLESTON ABRAHAM Ripley County MO 337 No Township Listed Federal Population Schedule MO 1840 Federal Census Index MOS4a1338462
2 CONT +++++++++++++++
2 CONT 1850 Oregon Co., Missouri census
2 CONT 400 65-65 Huddlestun Sr. Abraham 77 MFarmer 500 Penn x
2 CONT Mary 73 FVia x
2 CONT Henry 13 MMo/
2 CONT Martha 12 FMo/
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT Marriage Notes for ABRAHAM HUDDLESTON and MARY ALLEN:
2 CONT Bedford County, VA Marriage Bonds-
2 CONT Mar. 2, 1793; Abraham Huddleston & Mary Allen; Daniel Huddleston, Surety; Request from Ann Allen; Married by Nathaniel Shrewsbury, March 5, 1793.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of ABRAHAM HUDDLESTON and MARY ALLEN are:
2 CONT 21.	i.	 	BENJAMIN A.10 HUDDLESTON, b. February 10, 1817, Smith Co., (now Macon Co., ) Tennessee; d. February 1904, Oregon County, Missouri.
2 CONT 22.	ii.	 	NANCY HUDDLESTON, b. 1794, Bedford, Virginia; d. Ripley Co., Missouri.
2 CONT 23.	iii.	 	CHARLES HUDDLESTON, b. January 26, 1796, Virginia; d. 1872.
2 CONT  	iv.	 	WILLIAM HUDDLESTON, b. Bet. 1798 - 1807, Smith Co., Tennessee; m. MARTHA A. HOWELL.
2 CONT 24.	v.	 	JOSEPH HUDDLESTON, b. 1800, Virginia; d. 1857.
2 CONT  	vi.	 	JOHN F. HUDDLESTON, b. Bet. 1801 - 1803, Bedford, Virginia; m. SARAH AUSTMAS, April 19, 1833, Marion Co., Missouri; b. Abt. 1802.
2 CONT 25.	vii.	 	ISRAEL HUDDLESTON, b. 1803; d. Abt. 1839.
2 CONT 26.	viii.	 	NATHAN HUDDLESTON, b. 1805, Smith Co., Tennessee (census has Virginia).
2 CONT 27.	ix.	 	ABRAHAM HUDDLESTON, SR., b. 1809.
2 CONT 28.	x.	 	MILINER HUDDLESTON, b. 1811, Tennessee.
2 CONT 29.	xi.	 	JESSE HUDDLESTON, b. 1814, Tennessee.
2 CONT  	xii.	 	MARTHA PATSY HUDDLESTON, b. 1815, Smith Co., Tennessee.
