1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ewell Venable Unthank moved to Harlan, Kentucky in the 1830s.  He became a prominent merchant and participated in many community affairs with his name appearing frequently in the Harlan County Court Orders such as 
2 CONC the reference in 1850 as a school commissioner.  He is buried in the main cemetary in Pineville, Kentucky.
