1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mildred went to Mary Baldwin College and made the "Grand Tour of Europe" with her sister, Stella, in the spring & summer of 1891. She was married first to Mr. Eduard Mugge, Jr of Cuero, TX on 4/6/1896 at St. John's
2 CONC  Episcopal Church in Washington, D.C. & by whom she had a daughter, Pauline. His death in early 1900 put Mildred into a deep depression. She eventually married secondly Mr. Paul Kendall Clymer in 1905 by whom she had a daughter, E
2 CONC lizabeth (Libby). They were divorced in 1930. Mildred was described by her family as a warm, friendly person with a great sense of fun & humor.
