1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fontaine was a child of delicate health according to his father. He was the light of his father's life after "Fonny's" mother passed away; and in her absence, Fonny continued to be mothered by his "Aunt Kate", Mrs.
2 CONC  Catherine C. Thompson. Fontaine's life was taken suddenly from him on a summer holiday while he was visiting the farm of his uncle & aunt, John & Alice Young, and members of the Hutcheson family at "Mt. Airy", Mecklenburg County,
2 CONC  VA. First buried at "Mt. Airy", his remains were exumed and brought back by his father's direction to lie with his mother in Glenwood Cemetery.
