0 @N6000000002867182291@ NOTE He lived in Charlottesville and was a most distinguished lawyer and debater.  He was a member of the Virginia Legislature in 1842, a member  of Congress for the session of 1845-1847, Lieutenant Governonr of  Virginia in 1851, and 
1 CONC was a candidate for Governor in 1854, but was  defeated by a very close vote by Henry A Wise.  In 1859-1861, he was  again a member of Congress.  He was commonly known as the Demosthenses of  the hustings.
1 CONT History of Albemarle County
1 CONT The career of Shelton F. is well known, not only in the county, but in the State. His natural gifts were unusually brilliant. He settled in  Charlottesville, was admitted to the bar in 1838, easily attained a place  in its front r
1 CONC ank, was a member of the House of Delegates, was Lieutenant  Governor of the State, and for a term represented the district in  Congress. He married Rebecca Gray, and departed this life in 1884.
