0 @N6000000006348274216@ NOTE A William Morton, aged 20 years, emigrated to Virginia in the Margett
1 CONT & John, in 1620
1 CONT
1 CONT William Morton of Orange was an ancestor of Gen. J. E. B. Stuart.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gleanings of Virginia History
1 CONT William Fletcher Boogher
1 CONT Washington: 1903, Reprinted by Genealogical Publishing Company, 1995
1 CONT
1 CONT William Morton of Orange county, Va.  Married Ann Mothershead.  Died 1748.  Made will December 8, 1747, proved July 28, 1748, will book 2, p. 131.  Witnesses George Taylor, Taverner Beale, W. Russel, J. Branham, Fr., John Smith.  
1 CONC Appoints his wife Ann, executrix and son Elijah and son in law Andrew Bourne, executors.
1 CONT
1 CONT William Morton was an ancestor of Gen. J. E. B. Stuart, Confederate states of America.  See William and Mary Quarterly Magazine, 1897-1898.
1 CONT
1 CONT Genealogies of Virginia Families *V, He-S, The Morton Patriarchs of Virginia, Page 442
0 @N6000000004210619502@ NOTE The BROWN'S of AUCHLOCHAN!
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas and Elizabeth are entered as parents of John George BROWN on his Death
1 CONT entry.  Informant was Alex Francis BROWN, son of John George.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1841 Census shows a Martha BROWN present, aged 55 years, of independent
1 CONT means, not born in County.  She is of an age that means she could be the second
1 CONT wife of Thomas? (Born c1786) Thomas was still alive, but not present.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1851 Census shows Thomas, aged 75, a widower, and James Thomas, aged 40, and
1 CONT Elizabeth M., aged 30 (not Married) as being present and living at AUCHLOCHAN
1 CONT HOUSE, in the Parish of LESMAHAGOW. It also shows that children were all born in
1 CONT Granville, North Carolina, Virginia, USA, but were British Subjects.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1861 Census showes James as the Landed Proprietor, he succeeded in 1856.
1 CONT
1 CONT Death certificate confirms wife as Isabella ALSTON.
1 CONT Henry intered in Churchyard of Lesmahagow, by WYLIE and LOCHHEAD, undertakers.
1 CONT Informant John BROWN, 48 Mitchell street, Glasgow.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ref: Letters from F.W.H & Census records 1841,51,61 , and Death Certificate.
1 CONT [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT The BROWN'S of AUCHLOCHAN!
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas and Elizabeth are entered as parents of John George BROWN on his Death
1 CONT entry.  Informant was Alex Francis BROWN, son of John George.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1841 Census shows a Martha BROWN present, aged 55 years, of independent
1 CONT means, not born in County.  She is of an age that means she could be the second
1 CONT wife of Thomas? (Born c1786) Thomas was still alive, but not present.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1851 Census shows Thomas, aged 75, a widower, and James Thomas, aged 40, and
1 CONT Elizabeth M., aged 30 (not Married) as being present and living at AUCHLOCHAN
1 CONT HOUSE, in the Parish of LESMAHAGOW. It also shows that children were all born in
1 CONT Granville, North Carolina, Virginia, USA, but were British Subjects.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1861 Census showes James as the Landed Proprietor, he succeeded in 1856.
