0 @N6000000004210730203@ NOTE [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT James was born in the USA.
1 CONT
1 CONT c1864 James Thomas was the owner of AUCHLOCHAN, and described as
1 CONT Major-Commandant of the third Administrative Battalion of the Lanarkshire (Upper
1 CONT Ward) Rifle Volunteers. He succeeded to AUCHLOCHAN on the death of his Father.
1 CONT
1 CONT On his death 28/10/1880, he left 1200 Pounds to the Parish to keep the burying
1 CONT ground in good repair.  A few friends placed a tablet on the south wall to mark
1 CONT his, and the BROWNS of AUCHLOCHAN, family burying grounds.
1 CONT BROWNS had possesed property in the Parish for over 300 years!
1 CONT
1 CONT Ref: MI's of Lesmahagow Churchyard. Page 302,
1 CONT See also 'Annals of the Parish of Lesmahagow' by J.B. GREENSHIELDS, Page 98
1 CONT (Published c1864)
