0 @N6000000002867139105@ NOTE WILL OF WALTER LEAK OF GOOCHLAND
1 CONT In the Name of God Amen. I Walter Leak, of Goochland County, make this my  last will and testament, (being very sick) Revoking all other wills by Me  formerly made. And Appoint this my last, Acknowledging myself in my  proper sens
1 CONC es, I praise God for the Same.
1 CONT First: Desire my Body to be buried according to the Discression of my  Executors hereafter named, without pomp.
1 CONT Secondly: that my Debts may be all paid when due, and as for my Temporal Estate it hath pleased God to bestow upon me, I give as follows, Viz.  Impris. I give and bequeath to my son Josiah Leak part of the land  whereon I now live
1 CONC , viz. the South Side from the road beginning at  Groom's line and thence up the road to the Creek and up the Creek to  Coles' Spring branch, thence up the sd. branch to the line, to him and  his heirs forever. And the said Josiah
1 CONC  Leak is to pay to Samuel Leak five  and twenty Pounds Currt. Money.
1 CONT Item. I give and bequeath to my two sons John Leak and William Leak the  remainder of the aforesaid land on the North Side of the aforesaid road  that is to say any one of them is to have the whole Paying the other for  his part o
1 CONC f it. and he that will give to the other the most for his part  of it, shall take the whole to him and his heirs forever.
1 CONT Item. I give and bequeath to my two sons Mask Leak and Elisha Leak my  Piece of Land in Albemarle which I bought of Paul Michaux to be equally  divided between them in quantity and quality to them and their heirs  forever.
1 CONT Item. I give and bequeath to my three daughters, Mary Christian, Christian Johnston and Judith Leak twenty Pounds apiece after their Mother's decease.
1 CONT Item. I lend to my Daughter Elizabeth Coleman my negro girl Agge to wait  on her and to work for her, her life time and after her decease the said  Agge and her increase if she has any shall be Equally divided amongst her  childre
1 CONC n.
1 CONT Item. I lend to my loving wife and desire that she may have the use of all my Estate induring her lifetime and widowhood, both land negroes, cattle, etc., and after her decease or marriage then these legacies to be  paid, and the 
1 CONC remainder of my Estate to be equally divided amongst all my  children. I also desire that those of my children which have not been  helped towards housekeeping with Bed, Pot, and Stock, etc. as the others,  may be helped with such
1 CONC  necessaries equally to what the others have been.  I also appoint my loving wife Judith Leak and my son Josiah Leak  Executors of this my last will and Testament, desiring my estate may not  be appraised nor give security.
1 CONT Whereunto I set my hand and seal this 31st day of October Anno Dom. 1757.  Published in Presence of us.
1 CONT John Humber
1 CONT Charles Christian Junr   Walter Leak (seal)
1 CONT Elizabeth Humber
1 CONT At a court held for Goochland County May 16th, 1758. This writing was  proved by the Oaths of John Humber and Charles Christian Junr. to be the  Last Will and Testament of Walter Leak decd. which was admitted to record.
1 CONT Teste, Va. Wood Cl. Cur.
1 CONT Walter Leake's will is recorded in Goochland County in Will Book 7 on  page 279.
