0 @N6000000002867139536@ NOTE He was a Presbyterian minister and a graduate of Yale.  At his death, he  left a wife and three daughters.
1 CONT History of Albemarle County
1 CONT Samuel was one of the first Presbyterian ministers, who were natives of  Virginia. In 1770 he was installed pastor of the Cove and D. S. Churches,  and his home was four or five miles northeast of Covesville. He died  young in 177
1 CONC 5. He and his wife Elizabeth had three children, Elizabeth,  the first wife of Andrew Hart, Sarah, the wife of Rev. James Robinson,  one of Mr Leake's successors in the Cove pastorate, and Mary. His widow  died in 1799.
