1 CONT
1 CONT For some years the address of Rebecca Monteith BROWN was at Yewlands Villa, in
1 CONT the Parish of Liberton, on the outskirts of Edinburgh.  On her Death the tenancy
1 CONT was taken over by her Solicitors, MacGregor, Donald, of GLASGOW as Trustee.
0 @N6000000004210721841@ NOTE [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT Monti Married James William ALSTON in 1867, he died in 1880.  During the Census
1 CONT of 1881 she was living at 16 Douglas Crescent, in the Parish of St.George,
1 CONT EDINBURGH.  This palatial residence was built in 1875.  She had a Housemaid,
1 CONT Cook, and a Tablemaid.  Her Sister-in-law Jane ALSTON lived there with her and
1 CONT in 1890 this was the address of John Robert BROWN, her youngest Brother.
0 @N6000000004210721853@ NOTE [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT Sarah Married Charles Henry ALSTON, c1868.
0 @N6000000004210721535@ NOTE [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT On Marriage Certificate his occupation is shown as Woollen Manufacturer, and he
1 CONT was living at 197 Pitt Street, GLASGOW. [February 1878]
1 CONT
1 CONT He, and his wife, were a very wealthy family, and set up a family trust in 1878
1 CONT that provided cash to family members till the year 1983 when the trustees wound
1 CONT up the trust.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1902 when F.G. BROWN married his address was 'VILLA NOVA' Bryon Place,
1 CONT Bristol, ENGLAND. Occupation 'of independant means'.
1 CONT
1 CONT They retired to the Isle of WIGHT, (pre 1922) and lived at Mottistone House,
1 CONT Brighstone, and when AFG died, aged 85, in 1935 he was living at
1 CONT Strathwell Park, Whitewell, in the Isle.
1 CONT
1 CONT At time of death the estate was administered by John Marshall COWAN, a Dr of
1 CONT GLASGOW, William Hamilton ALSTON, retired Merchant, of Helensburg, SCOTLAND,
1 CONT and family Solicitor, (a relation?) Thomas Walter DONALD.
1 CONT
1 CONT A Mrs Janet COWAN, was a resident in Yewlands Villa, at the time of death of
1 CONT Mrs Rebecca Monteith BROWN, widow of his father, John George BROWN, 1888/89.
1 CONT On Marriage Certificate his occupation is shown as Woollen Manufacturer, and he
1 CONT was living at 197 Pitt Street, GLASGOW. [February 1878]
0 @N6000000004210730085@ NOTE [watkins.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT John Robert BROWN was informant when his mother, Rebecca Monteith (Monti) died.
1 CONT His address was given as 16 Douglas Crescent, Edinburgh, the address of his
1 CONT eldest Sister, Rebecca Monteith (Monti) (BROWN) ALSTON.
1 CONT
1 CONT So far no other corroboration or history on this relative!
1 CONT
1 CONT Ref: Letter from F.W.H 21/03/1992
