0 @N6000000000360639712@ NOTE RFN1
1 CONT [FN::FN][BO::BO]Moved to Lunenburg Co., VA from Cumberland Co., VA
1 CONT with his parents in 1762-62.  The area in which they settled later was
1 CONT changed to Charlotte Co.  Charles Jr bought the home plantation from
1 CONT his father on November 1, 1784 as recorded in county deed book #5.
1 CONT The plantation consisted of 247 acres and was bought for 210 pounds.
1 CONT Charles Jr. is listed in the 1782 Virginia census as head of a
1 CONT household of three white persons and four negro slaves.[Miles Whole.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT RFN1
1 CONT [FN::FN][BO::BO]Moved to Lunenburg Co., VA from Cumberland Co., VA
1 CONT with his parents in 1762-62.  The area in which they settled later was
1 CONT changed to C harlotte Co.  Charles Jr bought the home plantation from
1 CONT his father on Novembe r 1, 1784 as recorded in county deed book #5.
1 CONT The plantation consisted of 247 acres and was bought for 210 pounds.
