0 @N6000000005965732222@ NOTE COLUMBUS BELL MOORE
1 CONT Bonnie Storm Braswell  (View posts)  Posted: 6 Aug 1999 7:00AM
1 CONT
1 CONT Classification: Obituary
1 CONT Surnames: Moore, Branscome, Roper
1 CONT STATE PIONEER PASSES AWAY AT HOME HERE
1 CONT
1 CONT COLUMBUS BELL MOORE, 73years old departed this life at 3 o?clock this morning at the home of Jay MOORE, His son-in-law, 1211 west MOORE Street.
1 CONT Deceased had suffered from heart leakage for two or three years, but the acute attack was recent. In fact he drove his car up town only last Saturday. No Funeral arrangements as yet have been made for the reason the same of the re
1 CONC latives must came from New Mexico.
1 CONT Mr. Moore is native of Tenn. Was born at Wayneboro, Nov. 16,1856. He went to Texas in 1881 and came to Indian Territory in 1885 and for many years lived in the region where Hanna is. He was a farmer for a time, and then went into 
1 CONC merchants business. At one time he was in the hotel business.
1 CONT His children are grown and all married, the youngest son Billie who is well known here in Henryetta, having attended High school here.
1 CONT The deceased leaves four sons and three daughters, as well as four brothers. His wife passed away some years ago.
1 CONT The editor of Free-Lance who writes these lines has enjoyed 40 years of close friendship with the departed, and can attest to his high character and citizenship. His loss is natural, for he had attained man?s allotted time; but ne
1 CONC vertheless, the country loses a of the very highest type.
1 CONT His brother, R. B. Moore, Ada; son-in-law Ivan Branscome, Ada: and H. C. Roper, Ada, are here today. Further announcements will be made tomorrow.
1 CONT
1 CONT From the Henyetta Daily Free-Lance on March 19,1930
0 @N6000000005965760110@ NOTE ROBERT B. MOORE
1 CONT Bonnie Storm Braswell  (View posts)  Posted: 6 Aug 1999 7:00AM
1 CONT
1 CONT Classification: Obituary
1 CONT Surnames: Moore, Ferrier, Wahlman, Miles, Meek, O'Neal, Shelton, Sizemore
1 CONT Robert B. Moore, 314 West Eighteenth died Friday afternoon at 2:30 Funeral Monday at 4:00 Criswell Funeral Chapel, Mack Lyons, Rosedale Cemetery.
1 CONT Surviving are the widow Mrs. Martha Moore, Daughters Mrs. Edna W. Ferrier, Mercedes Tex., and Mrs. Ethel Wahiman, Ada, son Robert D. Moore, Peru, Neb., sevens grandchildren.
1 CONT Bearers?W.T. Moore, W.T. Miles, Roy Meek, Delmer O?Neal, Orh Shelton, Burch Sizemore
1 CONT
1 CONT From The Ada Evening News October 4,1953
0 @N6000000005965760050@ NOTE RICHARD FRANKLIN MOORE PASSES AWAY.
1 CONT Bonnie Storm Braswell  (View posts)  Posted: 6 Aug 1999 7:00AM
1 CONT
1 CONT Classification: Obituary
1 CONT Surnames: Moore, Creesy, Owens, Perguson, Spillers, Bean, Allen
1 CONT RICHARD FRANKLIN MOORE, who recently moved to Weleetka from Eufaula, died at his home in this city Wednesday night or last week. He had been in poor health for several months.
1 CONT Mr. Moore was born on May 18,1865, at Wayne County, Tennessee. He was 75 years 6months and 20 daysolds at the time of his departure.
1 CONT He was united in marriage to Miss Jesse Creesy on December 15,1885. To this union was born nine children, five having proceeded him in death.
1 CONT Those surviving are his wife and four daughters, Fannie Owens of Carnage,Viola Perguson of Coolidge,Arizona, Sallie Spillers, Weleetka, and Lula May Bean of Checotah, two brothers, John MOORE, of Weleetka, and Robert MOORE of Norm
1 CONC an; one daughter-in-law, Mrs. Wayne MOORE of Tulsa, also 27 grandchildren, and 15 grant-grandchildren, and many other relatives and frinds.Mr. Moore united with Missionary Baptist church in 1895 at Moletta, Okla.
1 CONT Funeral services were conducted at the Baptist church Saturday by Rev. Pittman Allen pastor and burial was made in the cemetery at Hanna, Okla.
1 CONT
1 CONT From The Weleetka American on Dec. 15,1943.
0 @N6000000005965748095@ NOTE JOHN MACK MOORE DIES FROM FALL INJURIES
1 CONT Bonnie Storm Braswell  (View posts)  Posted: 6 Aug 1999 7:00AM
1 CONT
1 CONT Classification: Obituary
1 CONT Surnames: Moore, McCready
1 CONT John Moore local citizen died Sunday in a Henryetta hospital from an injury of the skull which he sustained when he fall at the dam at Weleetka Lake while fiahing that afternoon. Moore was crossing the lower portion of the dam whe
1 CONC n he missed his footing, falling several feet.
1 CONT Moore was 77 years old, and resided in Weleetka for several years, being a retired operator of a gin at Hanna. Survivors are one brother.
1 CONT Funeral services were conducted at the Weleetka Funeral Home Tuesday afternoon at 1:30 p.m. by Rev. J.H. McCready pastor of the Free Will Baptist Church. Burial was made in the cemetery at Hanna. The Weleetka Funeral Home was in c
1 CONC hange.
1 CONT
1 CONT From the Weleetka American April 3,1946
